s#placeholders","content":"Steps, server commands and environments","locale":"en"},"5135":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-151","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#placeholders","content":"`{{` and `}}` are literal braces. An undeclared component or parameter, `{port}` anywhere else, and an unclosed `{` are errors at registration.","locale":"en"},"5136":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-152","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#placeholders","content":"`{extension.root}` locates package files. Use a component path for a step's output. When a `run` step's or a server's program is `{host.python}`, it runs with the application's `sd_webui_all_in_one` importable (the launcher code first on `PYTHONPATH`) and `PYTHONUTF8`, `PYTHONUNBUFFERED` and `PYTHONNOUSERSITE` set to `1`. Resolving the interpreter waits while App Runtime prepares it. If preparation has failed, the operation returns the runtime's error.","locale":"en"},"5137":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-153","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#placeholders","content":"**Step paths** (`to`, `unpackTo`, `archive`, `into`, `dir`, `cwd` and `path`) start with `{component.<name>}`, optionally followed by `/` and a path inside the component, such as `{component.core}/bin/server`. A step whose resolved path would leave its component is refused. Entries in `environment.path` may also start with `{instance.root}`.","locale":"en"},"5138":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-154","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`[[install.steps]]` run for initial installation and retry. To give explicit reinstallation its own plan, declare `[[reinstall.steps]]`; otherwise it follows the installation plan. Each step may have a localized title, e.g. `title = { en = \"Build model index\", zh = \"生成模型索引\" }`. The workspace shows the title while running and retains it on failure. For static types, `[[update.steps]]` run when a ready instance is updated (`install.steps` when none are declared). They run in order, and the first that fails fails the operation. The install progress names the current step and counts the finished ones.","locale":"en"},"5139":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-155","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`kind`","locale":"en"},"5140":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-156","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Keys","locale":"en"},"5141":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-157","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5142":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-158","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`download`","locale":"en"},"5143":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-159","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`url`, `sha256`, and one of `to` or `unpackTo`","locale":"en"},"5144":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-160","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Downloads through the application's proxy, trying the configured GitHub mirror first for a `https://github.com/...` URL. `sha256` is required: 64 hex digits, or a parameter; a mismatch replaces nothing. `to` keeps the file, `unpackTo` unpacks it into a directory, with an optional `strip` as `unpack`","locale":"en"},"5145":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-161","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`unpack`","locale":"en"},"5146":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-162","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`archive`, `into`, optional `strip`","locale":"en"},"5147":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-163","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Unpacks a zip or tar (gz, xz, bz2); an entry or link that would leave the target is refused; into an existing directory, entries of the same name are replaced and the rest kept. `strip = N` drops the first `N` path components of every entry (an archive's top directory with `1`); a file with nothing left, or two entries that strip to one name, are refused. A tar's symbolic link may point up with leading `..` (as Node.js's `bin/npm -> ../lib/...`), but not out of what `strip` keeps","locale":"en"},"5148":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-164","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`git-clone`","locale":"en"},"5149":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-165","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`url`, `into`, optional `branch`","locale":"en"},"5150":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-166","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Clones with the application's Git; a repository already there is left for `git-pull`","locale":"en"},"5151":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-167","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`git-pull`","locale":"en"},"5152":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-168","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`dir`","locale":"en"},"5153":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-169","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Pulls an existing repository","locale":"en"},"5154":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-170","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`run`","locale":"en"},"5155":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-171","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`command`, optional `cwd` (`{component.core}` by default) and `env`","locale":"en"},"5156":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-172","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Runs a program directly (no shell), the program first in `command`; its output goes to the task, and a failure carries its last 4 KiB","locale":"en"},"5157":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-173","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`python-env`","locale":"en"},"5158":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-174","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"none","locale":"en"},"5159":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-175","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Prepares the managed Python in the `python` component; later `run` steps find it first on `PATH`. Only for a Python runtime","locale":"en"},"5160":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-176","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`write-file`","locale":"en"},"5161":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-177","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`path`, `content`","locale":"en"},"5162":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-178","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Writes a file; refused when the target's directory resolves outside its component","locale":"en"},"5163":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-179","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`probe`","locale":"en"},"5164":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-180","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`url`, optional `timeoutSeconds` (60 by default)","locale":"en"},"5165":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-181","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"Waits for a 2xx answer from a loopback `http://` URL (`127.0.0.1`, `localhost`, or `[::1]`)","locale":"en"},"5166":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-182","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#steps","content":"`unpack` and `download` with `unpackTo` also accept `replace = true`. Use it when an update archive should remove files left by the old version. The host extracts beside the target and swaps in the completed directory. It refuses replacement if the target contains another instance component. Without `replace`, unpacking into an existing directory keeps unrelated entries.","locale":"en"},"5167":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-183","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Each `[[servers]]` entry is a server role. Starting a declarative instance means starting its servers in order.","locale":"en"},"5168":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-184","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"5169":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-185","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5170":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-186","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`role`","locale":"en"},"5171":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-187","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Required: 1 to 64 characters of `a-z`, `0-9`, `-`; `control` is the management API (below)","locale":"en"},"5172":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-188","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`command`","locale":"en"},"5173":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-189","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"The program and its arguments. A backend-provided type may omit this to call `provider.launchPlan` for this role.","locale":"en"},"5174":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-190","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`env`","locale":"en"},"5175":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-191","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Environment variables; values may use placeholders","locale":"en"},"5176":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-192","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`port`","locale":"en"},"5177":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-193","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`{ allocate = true }` (the default), `{ fixed = 8080 }`, `{ param = \"<numeric install field>\" }`, or `{ launch = \"<numeric launch field>\" }`","locale":"en"},"5178":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-194","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`readiness`","locale":"en"},"5179":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-195","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Required for every role but `control`. Choose one of `{ http = \"/health\" }` (an absolute path), `{ tcp = true }`, `{ stdout = \"<regex>\" }` or `{ captured = true }`. Optional `timeoutSeconds` defaults to 120.","locale":"en"},"5180":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-196","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`after`","locale":"en"},"5181":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-197","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"The roles it starts after; only declared roles, with no cycle","locale":"en"},"5182":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-198","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`restart`","locale":"en"},"5183":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-199","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`never` (the default) or `on-failure` (restarted automatically within a limit)","locale":"en"},"5184":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-200","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`webview`","locale":"en"},"5185":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-201","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"When `true`, the running role's address is offered as a page in the WebUI tab; `false` by default","locale":"en"},"5186":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-202","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`required`","locale":"en"},"5187":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-203","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"`true` by default. A required role that fails fails the start; an optional one that fails leaves the instance running degraded","locale":"en"},"5188":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-204","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"A server process runs in the `core` component. The variables in `env` are merged with the instance's environment variables, and the instance's win on a name both set.","locale":"en"},"5189":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-205","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"For a UI hosted below the root, set `webview = true` and\n`webviewPath = \"/dashboard/\"`. The readiness probe may use a separate path. Set `externalBrowserPath = \"/studio\"` to choose a different same-origin page for the title bar browser button.\nA role with `after = [\"api\"]` can pass `{endpoint.api}` in its command or\nenvironment. It resolves at start to the running API role's base URL, including\nthe allocated port.","locale":"en"},"5190":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-206","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#servers","content":"Use `readiness = { captured = true }` for a server that chooses its own browser URL, for example one that includes a session token in the query. The host gives each start a fresh runtime broker session. The program reports its loopback HTTP(S) URL with a `browser.open` event. With `sd_webui_all_in_one`, create the client with `DesktopBrokerClient.from_env()` and call `emit_event(\"browser.open\", {\"url\": url})` on it. The first accepted URL makes the role ready, and `webview = true` opens that URL with its query intact. Printing a URL to stdout alone leaves this probe waiting until timeout.","locale":"en"},"5191":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-207","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#the-management-api","content":"A type with a Python runtime may also run the application's management API, the control server every built-in WebUI runs, on the instance's own Python. Declare the `control` role with nothing but `after` and `required`, and order your own roles after it:","locale":"en"},"5192":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-208","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#the-management-api","content":"The application then starts it before your roles, shows the instance's Management API in its information and in Settings → API Servers, and keeps it running while the instance is managed or launched. Stopping or restarting it does not stop your roles. A type without a Python runtime cannot declare `control`, and the error says why. The role alone adds no management section; a type takes the built-in WebUIs' versions, extensions, models, and PyTorch sections by adopting a built-in type's management.","locale":"en"},"5193":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-209","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#the-management-api","content":"Declare per-instance launch fields in `[[launch.parameters]]` using install parameter syntax. Users edit them under **Launch**; the next service start reads them without reinstalling. Use `{launch.name}` in a server command or environment. A server may set `cwd = \"{component.core}/service\"`. The default working directory is `core`. Backend launch plans receive `launchValues` alongside the install `values`.","locale":"en"},"5194":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-210","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#the-management-api","content":"Set `preflight = true` under `[launch]` to check the whole instance once before starting its roles. The host sends `provider.launchPreflight` with `type`, `instance`, install `values` and effective `launchValues`. Return `{}` on success or an RPC error with a reason. For example, the greeter checks that the selected greeting file still exists. Role restarts do not repeat this check.","locale":"en"},"5195":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-211","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#the-management-api","content":"A launch field with `kind = \"select\"` may set `optionsSource = \"models\"` when its extension has a backend. Opening Launch for this instance requests its choices from `provider.launchOptions`. For example, return `{ \"options\": { \"models\": [\"a.gguf\", \"b.gguf\"] } }`. The management tool `get_instance_launch_options` lists the nonsecret choices for this instance by field key. Static options remain available. The host checks a newly selected dynamic value on save. A saved value can be kept when the backend is offline or the model has disappeared.","locale":"en"},"5196":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-212","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#the-management-api","content":"Type-level `quickPaths = [{ name = \"Outputs\", component = \"core\", path = \"output\" }]` seeds Overview when an instance is created or imported, including discovery. Users may rename, reorder or remove those shortcuts. Moving an instance also moves shortcut targets inside the old root. Set a type's top-level `migrationNotice` to localized text to tell users, in the migration preview, about paths stored by your program that may need attention.","locale":"en"},"5197":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-213","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#environment","content":"`[environment]` applies to the type's `run` steps, its servers, and its terminal:","locale":"en"},"5198":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-214","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#environment","content":"`unset` removes inherited variables by exact name or by prefix with a trailing `*`. Windows matches variable names without regard to case. An explicitly supplied variable can set the name again. The instance's own variables take precedence over `vars` and a step's or server's `env`. Each `path` entry starts at a component or the instance root. Use `{port}` only in the role's command or environment.","locale":"en"},"5199":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-215","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#management-operations","content":"`[management] operations` lists the management operations an instance offers beyond the standard lifecycle. A declarative type can declare `update` and `terminal`. With `update`, updating a ready instance runs `update.steps` (or `install.steps`); without it, its instances cannot be updated. With `terminal`, its instances offer a terminal in `core` with the type's environment.","locale":"en"},"5200":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-216","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#read-only-model-component","content":"Add a component such as `weights` to `components`, then set `[management] modelComponent = \"weights\"`. The Models page browses that component’s folders and files, including when its path is outside the instance directory. The same data is available through `list_model_entries` and `list_model_directories`. This needs no control server and grants no model writes. Choose either this option or the adopted `models` operation.","locale":"en"},"5201":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-217","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"A type can take selected management sections from the application by adopting a built-in type:","locale":"en"},"5202":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-218","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Use `allowedMutations = []` in `[management]` to provide read-only sections, or list the writes your type supports, such as `[\"model.download\", \"extension.update\"]`. This also controls the model library installer (`model.library_install`) and PyTorch reinstall (`pytorch.reinstall`). Omit the option to expose the family’s usual actions.","locale":"en"},"5203":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-219","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`adopts` names a built-in type by its id: `builtin:sd-webui`, `builtin:comfyui`, `builtin:invokeai`, `builtin:fooocus`, `builtin:sd-trainer`, `builtin:qwen-tts-webui`, `builtin:rvc-next-webui`, or `builtin:mizuoto-tts-webui`. The type needs:","locale":"en"},"5204":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-220","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`runtime = { kind = \"python\" }` and the `control` role: the management API serves the sections;","locale":"en"},"5205":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-221","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"a `core` that is the instance's own. A type whose `core` is `external = \"allowed\"` cannot adopt, because the sections change what `core` holds.","locale":"en"},"5206":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-222","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Each operation you list adds one section to the instance's management page:","locale":"en"},"5207":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-223","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"5208":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-224","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Section and what it does","locale":"en"},"5209":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-225","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"What you assert about the instance","locale":"en"},"5210":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-226","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`versions`","locale":"en"},"5211":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-227","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Versions: the checkout's status, branches, and commits; switching a branch or a commit. It has no Update button","locale":"en"},"5212":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-228","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`core` is a Git checkout","locale":"en"},"5213":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-229","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`extensions`","locale":"en"},"5214":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-230","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Extensions: the adopted type's extensions (`core/extensions`, or `core/custom_nodes` for ComfyUI)","locale":"en"},"5215":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-231","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`core` is laid out as the adopted type's installation","locale":"en"},"5216":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-232","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`models`","locale":"en"},"5217":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-233","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Models: the files under `core/models` (`core/sd-models` for SD Trainer), and the adopted type's model library","locale":"en"},"5218":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-234","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`core` is laid out as the adopted type's installation","locale":"en"},"5219":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-235","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`environment`","locale":"en"},"5220":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-236","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"The environment report","locale":"en"},"5221":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-237","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"The instance's `python` runs your program","locale":"en"},"5222":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-238","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"`pytorch`","locale":"en"},"5223":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-239","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"The PyTorch catalog and reinstall","locale":"en"},"5224":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-240","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"The instance's `python` runs your program","locale":"en"},"5225":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-241","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"A type may adopt for `versions` and `environment` alone; those need no particular layout. Whether the adopted type supports a section follows that type: adopting `builtin:fooocus` gives no Extensions, and the section then shows as unsupported. Adopting `builtin:invokeai` gives its extensions and the environment report only: its versions, models, and PyTorch reinstall are its own package's.","locale":"en"},"5226":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-242","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"What stays the built-in types' own, and is refused for your type:","locale":"en"},"5227":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-243","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"**The kernel update and its update summary.** Your type's `update` is its update, and an `update-check` is its check. A found update shows beside the Update action in Maintenance.","locale":"en"},"5228":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-244","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"**Snapshots**, including creating an instance from one.","locale":"en"},"5229":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-245","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"**The hotpatch, launch arguments, and the launch checks.** Your servers start from your own commands.","locale":"en"},"5230":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-246","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"**Branch variants.**","locale":"en"},"5231":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-247","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"Two things to know when you write the type:","locale":"en"},"5232":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-248","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"A switch to a commit leaves `core` detached. If your `update.steps` is a `git-pull`, it reports that; write the step you want for that case.","locale":"en"},"5233":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-249","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"The PyTorch reinstall is refused while the instance is launched. A role started from Settings → API Servers is not a launch, so stop such a role before reinstalling PyTorch.","locale":"en"},"5234":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-250","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#adopting-a-built-in-types-management","content":"The sample adopted-webui is a complete type of this kind.","locale":"en"},"5235":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-251","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"The application's discovery (the instance scan, and dropping a folder on the application) recognizes the built-in WebUIs by their layouts. Your type recognizes its own installations with `[[discovery]]` signatures; a type without one is never discovered.","locale":"en"},"5236":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-252","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"At each directory the scan visits, the built-in layouts are tried first; then, outside every installation found so far, the registered types' signatures in order. A directory a signature matched is not scanned further.","locale":"en"},"5237":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-253","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"A marker counts only when it is a regular file or directory reached without following a link. Paths are relative, `/`-separated, of ordinary names: `..`, a leading `/`, a backslash, or a drive is refused at registration.","locale":"en"},"5238":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-254","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"`components` names only components the type declares. The others are `<root>/<name>`, and every component must exist: an import adopts existing directories.","locale":"en"},"5239":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-255","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"`values` are checked against your install parameters at registration: an unknown parameter or a required one without value or default is an issue at `discovery[<index>].values`. The others take their defaults.","locale":"en"},"5240":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-256","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"A match is imported as a ready instance of your type. A directory already managed is reported, never imported twice. Values the type refuses then (for a type a backend provides, `provider.validateSpec`), or a component missing on disk, make it a warning instead of an instance.","locale":"en"},"5241":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-257","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"`external = [\"core\", \"node\"]` records those components of an attached installation as external (each declared `external = \"allowed\"`): deleting or reinstalling the instance never removes them.","locale":"en"},"5242":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-258","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"`attachOnly = true` (a top-level key) makes discovery the only way to an instance, for an installation the user made, such as an npm global prefix: the creation page does not list the type, and creating or importing one by hand is refused. A type that sets it needs a signature.","locale":"en"},"5243":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-259","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#discovery","content":"Signatures leave with your type: once the extension is turned off, its types are no longer discovered.","locale":"en"},"5244":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-260","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"A type with `provider = \"backend\"` keeps what is static in its descriptor (id, text, components, runtime, parameters, servers, operations) and asks the extension's backend for the rest:","locale":"en"},"5245":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-261","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"The extension must have a `[backend]`; otherwise the install fails.","locale":"en"},"5246":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-262","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Declare `install.steps` (even an empty list) to supply fixed install steps. Declare `[reinstall]` to override those steps for explicit reinstalls. Declare `[update]` to supply fixed update steps. The backend plans each omitted phase. Each role may declare a static `command` or request its command from the backend.","locale":"en"},"5247":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-263","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Besides `update` and `terminal`, its `operations` may name `update-check` and operations of its own, of `a-z`, `0-9`, `-`, other than the built-in types' standard ones (`launch-arguments`, `snapshots`, `hotpatch`, `diagnostics`; and `versions`, `extensions`, `models`, `environment`, `pytorch`, which it declares only by adopting a built-in type's management).","locale":"en"},"5248":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-264","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`update-check` puts its instances in the application's update check: the card's \"check for updates\" and the daily check ask the backend `provider.checkUpdate`, even while the instance runs, and an update it finds shows on the card and in Maintenance. It is not an operation of its own: the instance's management lists no button for it. Any type in an extension with a backend can declare it independently of `update`, including one with static install steps and server commands.","locale":"en"},"5249":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-265","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"A custom operation can accept input and ask for confirmation in the operations panel.\nUse install parameter syntax under its form. The backend receives the checked `values`;\nthe management tool `run_instance_operation` accepts the same object.\nA management list action may specify `operation = \"refresh-index\"` and\n`rowField = \"target\"` to fill the form's text field with the selected row ID.\nReturn `steps` for a long operation. The host executes them under exclusive\nmaintenance and returns an activity ID for tracking and cancellation.","locale":"en"},"5250":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-266","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"The backend takes part through these callbacks (see Backends):","locale":"en"},"5251":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-267","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"When","locale":"en"},"5252":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-268","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Callback","locale":"en"},"5253":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-269","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"The backend answers","locale":"en"},"5254":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-270","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Checking the values","locale":"en"},"5255":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-271","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`provider.validateSpec`","locale":"en"},"5256":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-272","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Problems by parameter; the application runs its own form checks first","locale":"en"},"5257":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-273","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Install, retry, reinstall, update","locale":"en"},"5258":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-274","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`provider.installPlan`","locale":"en"},"5259":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-275","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"A list of steps, written as `install.steps` are, placeholders and all","locale":"en"},"5260":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-276","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Starting a role","locale":"en"},"5261":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-277","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`provider.launchPlan`","locale":"en"},"5262":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-278","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`argv` and `env`, written as a server's `command` and `env`, `{port}` allowed","locale":"en"},"5263":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-279","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Checking for an update (`update-check`)","locale":"en"},"5264":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-280","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`provider.checkUpdate`","locale":"en"},"5265":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-281","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Whether an applicable update exists, and its current and latest version","locale":"en"},"5266":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-282","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Reading an instance’s select choices","locale":"en"},"5267":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-283","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`provider.launchOptions`","locale":"en"},"5268":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-284","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Values grouped by each field’s `optionsSource`","locale":"en"},"5269":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-285","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Running an operation of its own","locale":"en"},"5270":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-286","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"`provider.manage.<operation>`","locale":"en"},"5271":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-287","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Optional notice and an optional maintenance step plan","locale":"en"},"5272":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-288","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"The application checks a plan as it checks a descriptor's steps: an undeclared placeholder, a path that does not start in a declared component, an unknown step kind, or a value that would leave its component refuses the whole plan before anything runs. The backend names components, never paths; the application runs the steps.","locale":"en"},"5273":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-289","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#types-a-backend-provides","content":"Reading an existing instance's record never asks the backend, so its instances stay listed while the backend is down. While the backend fails or restarts, these types stay registered, and operations that need it fail with \"extension backend unavailable\". The types leave only when the extension is turned off, updated, or uninstalled.","locale":"en"},"5274":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-290","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"A preset is a set of defaults over one instance type, which the new installation page lists under that type: choosing it fills the form, and the user can still change every value. Every `.toml` or `.json` file the manifest's `contributes.presets` glob matches is one preset, whose id is `<extension id>:<id>`, such as `com.example.greeter:morning`. Its base type can be one of your extension's types, another extension's, or a built-in one.","locale":"en"},"5275":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-291","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"`[install]` sets fields of the base type's install form. The user's edits take precedence. A field the preset leaves out keeps the type's default, and the user fills any remaining required fields. Leave `secret` fields for the user to enter. Naming one in a preset makes that preset unusable, and **Save as preset** omits secret fields.","locale":"en"},"5276":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-292","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"`[launch.values]` sets declared nonsecret launch fields for a new instance, e.g. `threads = 4`. Changing the preset affects future instances only.","locale":"en"},"5277":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-293","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"`[launch] arguments` replaces the type's default argument of the same name (`true` passes the option alone, a number or text passes it with that value, `false` removes it) and appends the others. Only built-in types take launch arguments.","locale":"en"},"5278":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-294","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"The application checks a preset against its base type each time it lists it. A preset whose base type is not installed, that sets a field the form does not have, or a value the field does not take, is listed as unavailable with the reason; it never fails your extension. A file that does not read, or a malformed id, base or argument, fails the install as a type descriptor does.","locale":"en"},"5279":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-295","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"An instance keeps the preset's launch arguments as they were at creation. Editing or removing the preset leaves existing instances’ configuration intact. Their availability follows the base type. If that type belongs to the same extension, turning the extension off makes its instances unavailable until the type is registered again.","locale":"en"},"5280":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-296","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"The sample extension contributes `package/presets/morning.toml` over its own type.","locale":"en"},"5281":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-297","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"The preset schema documents extension files, including their required `id`. Catalog annotations explain why a structurally valid preset may currently be unavailable. Complete examples above are read from validated source packages; install steps and network endpoints are not executed by the documentation checks.","locale":"en"},"5282":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types-298","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-instance-types#presets","content":"For descriptor defaults, conditional requirements and validation stages, see the instance-type descriptor reference.","locale":"en"},"5283":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"page","content":"Interface Reference","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Extension Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","locale":"en"},"5284":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-0","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","content":"Every interface an extension can use - the frame protocol, the UI kit's classes, panel blocks and form fields, components, the host API, the application's calls on a backend, and the manifest and instance-type descriptor keys, and the management tools. Generated from the application's interface exports.","locale":"en"},"5285":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-1","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#versions","content":"Versions","locale":"en"},"5286":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-2","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frontend","content":"Frontend","locale":"en"},"5287":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-3","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frame-messages","content":"Frame messages","locale":"en"},"5288":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-4","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frame-theme","content":"Theme, language, and bounds","locale":"en"},"5289":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-5","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frame-client","content":"Frame client","locale":"en"},"5290":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-6","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#ui-kit","content":"UI kit","locale":"en"},"5291":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-7","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#panel-blocks","content":"Panel blocks","locale":"en"},"5292":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-8","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#form-fields","content":"Form fields","locale":"en"},"5293":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-9","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#components","content":"Components","locale":"en"},"5294":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-10","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#backend","content":"Backend","locale":"en"},"5295":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-11","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#host-api","content":"Host API","locale":"en"},"5296":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-12","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#backend-calls","content":"The application's calls on a backend","locale":"en"},"5297":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-13","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#event-topics","content":"Event topics","locale":"en"},"5298":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-14","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#manifest","content":"Manifest","locale":"en"},"5299":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-15","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#instance-type","content":"Instance-type descriptor","locale":"en"},"5300":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-16","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#steps","content":"Install and update steps","locale":"en"},"5301":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-17","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#management-tools","content":"Management tools","locale":"en"},"5302":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-18","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#design-tokens","content":"Theme and motion token dictionary","locale":"en"},"5303":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-19","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#utilities","content":"Frame-safe utilities","locale":"en"},"5304":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-20","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#motion-examples","content":"Executable motion examples","locale":"en"},"5305":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-21","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#preset","content":"Extension presets","locale":"en"},"5306":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-22","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#configuration-examples","content":"Complete TOML source examples","locale":"en"},"5307":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-23","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","content":"This page lists every interface an extension can use, each item with an anchor to link to and a short example. It is read when the site is built from the interface export committed in the application's repository, `sdk/interfaces/` (written by `bun run export:backend-interfaces` and `bun run export:frontend-interfaces`, whose checks fail while it is stale), so it always matches the application's code. What each item is for and how to use it is on Backends, Instance Types, and Interface.","locale":"en"},"5308":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-24","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#versions","content":"`api` is the backend protocol's version, the one a manifest names in `engines.api`. Within a version, methods and optional fields are only added; removing or renaming one raises it.","locale":"en"},"5309":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-25","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#versions","content":"`kitVersion` is the UI kit's class API version, under the same rule.","locale":"en"},"5310":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-26","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#versions","content":"`uiApiVersion` is the version of the components a frame may use (the component bundle, UI API). Within a version, components and optional props are only added; removing or renaming one raises it.","locale":"en"},"5311":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-27","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#versions","content":"`exportVersion` is the version of the export files' own format.","locale":"en"},"5312":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-28","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frame-messages","content":"The messages a frame's page and the application exchange with `postMessage`. A page does not usually send them itself: the frame client wraps all of them.","locale":"en"},"5313":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-29","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frame-theme","content":"The colour scheme, CSS variables, and language the application sends with `theme`, and the frame's height and timing bounds.","locale":"en"},"5314":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-30","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#frame-client","content":"The ES module the application serves at a reserved path of every extension package's root, with its functions and types. How to use it is on Interface.","locale":"en"},"5315":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-31","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#ui-kit","content":"The classes of `__hanafubuki/ui.css` by group, with their modifiers, attributes, and example markup.","locale":"en"},"5316":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-32","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#panel-blocks","content":"The blocks of a panel (a `ui` entry of `kind = \"schema\"`). Each kind lists how the application renders it, how a panel's file writes it, and the data it is rendered from.","locale":"en"},"5317":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-33","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#form-fields","content":"The field kinds of an extension's settings and of a panel action's form, with the control, value type, and keys of each.","locale":"en"},"5318":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-34","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#components","content":"The application's components a frame may use: the component bundle, `__hanafubuki/ui.js`, with Vue at `__hanafubuki/vue.js` and their styles at `__hanafubuki/ui-components.css`. A page installs `frameUi(frame)` on each Vue app and renders them with `h()`, since the served Vue has no template compiler. Their typings are `sdk/ui/ui.d.ts`. How to use them is on Interface.","locale":"en"},"5319":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-35","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#host-api","content":"What a backend calls on the application, grouped by the first segment of the name. Each method lists its direction, whether it is a request or a notification, the permission it needs, its bounds, an example message, and the shape of its params and result.","locale":"en"},"5320":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-36","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#host-api","content":"For bounded UTF-8 requests, mirror-aware downloads and per-process proxy selection, see the SDK networking example. The entries below include their optional fields and defaults directly from the Rust contract; HTTP status codes are part of the response, while transport and permission failures are RPC errors.","locale":"en"},"5321":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-37","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#host-api","content":"The settings API edits only the calling extension: `settings.patch` returns canonical values, with `null` removing an override. Frames use the generated `getSettings` / `patchSettings` client signatures above, including without a backend.","locale":"en"},"5322":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-38","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#backend-calls","content":"The requests and notifications the application sends a backend: its lifecycle, provider callbacks, panel and frame calls, the UI state, services between extensions, and events and process output.","locale":"en"},"5323":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-39","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#backend-calls","content":"The `initialize` result lists known hooks from the method registry itself, including `diagnostics`. Expand `diagnostics.collect` for document fields and its timeout, count and byte bounds; runtime tools are listed in the host API above. See the SDK examples.","locale":"en"},"5324":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-40","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#event-topics","content":"`events.subscribe` replaces the subscription. Each `event` notification names its `topic` and carries the payload below in `data`. The topic registry is the source of these schemas; `preferences` uses the same full snapshot as `host.preferences`, while `settings` remains the extension's own values. Read the current preferences when starting or subscribing again; notifications are not replayed.","locale":"en"},"5325":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-41","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#manifest","content":"The keys of `hanafubuki-extension.toml`. Expand a key to see what it holds.","locale":"en"},"5326":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-42","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#manifest","content":"The nested `contributes.agent` schema below includes Skills, MCP transports, command sources and settings references. Permission checks, namespaced ownership and lifecycle are described in Agent contributions.","locale":"en"},"5327":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-43","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#instance-type","content":"The keys of a declarative instance type's descriptor.","locale":"en"},"5328":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-44","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#steps","content":"The keys of each kind of step in `install.steps` and `update.steps`.","locale":"en"},"5329":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-45","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#management-tools","content":"A backend lists management tools with `tools.list` and invokes them with `tools.call`. In the table, `read` identifies read-only tools. Changes require `management = \"confirm\"` and the user's confirmation in the main window for each call. Tools marked “built-in instances only” refuse instances of extension-provided types. Tools that start work return an `activityId`. Subscribe to the `task` topic to follow their progress. See Backends.","locale":"en"},"5330":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-46","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#management-tools","content":"Choose the tool for the kind of extension you manage. For example, `install_extension` installs a plugin into a specific WebUI instance. For desktop extensions, `list_host_extensions` lists installed packages and `browse_host_extension_marketplace` searches the marketplace. Users confirm desktop package installations in Settings.","locale":"en"},"5331":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-47","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#design-tokens","content":"Search by name or purpose, select a group, and expand a token to see every source declaration, selector and condition. Values are CSS expressions in cascade order, not a computed snapshot. `root` identifies shared tokens; `local` applies to a component or region; `internal` is implementation detail, not a public override contract; `runtime` is projected by the host. The dictionary does not expand the frame's theme message or authorize changing application settings.","locale":"en"},"5332":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-48","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#utilities","content":"These signatures come from the same exports as `sdk/ui/ui.d.ts`. They operate on the frame's DOM and Vue scope; they do not expose Tauri, native windows or the host's global appearance authority. Timing helpers read resolved CSS; unresolved timing is zero. Motion roles are the normal consumer entry point; duration steps and curves serve shared implementations.","locale":"en"},"5333":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-49","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#motion-examples","content":"Download frame-components, install it as a linked folder, and open its page or settings section. These modules run beside the existing component gallery with the host's Vue runtime and UI bundle. Each code listing below is the complete source of the module mounted there, exported without maintaining a second snippet.","locale":"en"},"5334":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-50","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#preset","content":"This schema describes extension-contributed files, not entries of the user's persisted preset store. Structural defaults are JSON facts: TOML has no `null` literal. Domain annotations separately explain omission, effective defaults and catalog availability.","locale":"en"},"5335":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference-51","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-reference#configuration-examples","content":"These complete files are exported from curated source packages and checked with the real loaders, package readers and catalog. Related files belong to the same package. Validation does not run install steps, download software, prepare Python or start servers. Keys, source comments and domain rule descriptions retain their source language.","locale":"en"},"5336":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"page","content":"SDKs","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Extension Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","locale":"en"},"5337":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-0","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","content":"Write an extension backend with the Rust SDK (hanafubuki-extension-sdk) or the Python SDK (hanafubuki_extension), with a minimal example of each.","locale":"en"},"5338":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-1","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#downloads","content":"Downloads","locale":"en"},"5339":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-2","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#rust","content":"Rust","locale":"en"},"5340":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-3","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"API","locale":"en"},"5341":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-4","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-minimal-example","content":"A minimal example","locale":"en"},"5342":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-5","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-ui-state","content":"A UI state","locale":"en"},"5343":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-6","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#python","content":"Python","locale":"en"},"5344":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-7","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"API","locale":"en"},"5345":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-8","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-minimal-example-1","content":"A minimal example","locale":"en"},"5346":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-9","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#without-an-sdk","content":"Without an SDK","locale":"en"},"5347":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-10","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#networking-and-per-process-proxy-selection","content":"Networking and per-process proxy selection","locale":"en"},"5348":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-11","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#own-settings","content":"Own settings","locale":"en"},"5349":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-12","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#host-preference-snapshots","content":"Host preference snapshots","locale":"en"},"5350":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-13","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#runtime-tools-and-diagnostics","content":"Runtime tools and diagnostics","locale":"en"},"5351":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-14","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#frame-host-operations-and-declarative-agent-content","content":"Frame host operations and declarative Agent content","locale":"en"},"5352":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-15","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","content":"Both SDKs implement the plumbing of the backend protocol: reading and writing frames, answering `initialize` and `ping`, dispatching ordinary requests to worker threads, and a `Host` to call the host API with. A backend implements only the methods it cares about.","locale":"en"},"5353":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-16","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","content":"A backend never writes anything but the protocol to stdout. In Rust, log with `eprintln!`; the\nPython SDK moves `sys.stdout` to stderr, so a `print` goes to the log instead of breaking a frame.","locale":"en"},"5354":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-17","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#downloads","content":"The SDKs and the frame typings, as files to keep in your own repository. Each archive has a README that says how to refer to what it holds.","locale":"en"},"5355":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-18","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#rust","content":"`hanafubuki-extension-sdk` is not published on crates.io, and the application's repository is not public, so there is no Git URL to depend on. Unpack the Rust SDK from above into your project and depend on it by path:","locale":"en"},"5356":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-19","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"5357":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-20","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5358":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-21","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`run(handler)`","locale":"en"},"5359":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-22","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Runs over stdin and stdout until the application sends `shutdown` or closes stdin; returns `Result<(), String>`, an error meaning what arrived was not the protocol","locale":"en"},"5360":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-23","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`run_on(handler, reader, writer)`","locale":"en"},"5361":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-24","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`run` over any pair of streams, for tests","locale":"en"},"5362":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-25","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`Handler`","locale":"en"},"5363":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-26","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"The trait a backend implements; every method has a default","locale":"en"},"5364":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-27","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`Host`","locale":"en"},"5365":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-28","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Calls the application: `call(method, params)`, `call_as::<P, R>(method, &params)`, `notify(method, params)`, `log(level, message)`, `emit_frame(frame, event, payload)` (an event for its frames, `ui.frame.emit`), `emit_state(state)` (pushes its UI state, `ui.emit`), and `initialize_params()` (the extension, its permissions, its data directory, the locale)","locale":"en"},"5366":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-29","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`Ui`","locale":"en"},"5367":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-30","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"The trait of a backend's UI state: `state(host, context)` answers `ui.state`, `call(host, action, args, context)` answers `ui.call` (by default every action is `INVALID_PARAMS`)","locale":"en"},"5368":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-31","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`protocol`","locale":"en"},"5369":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-32","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`hanafubuki-extension-protocol` re-exported: method name constants (`protocol::method`, `protocol::hooks`), params and result types, `RpcError` and the error codes","locale":"en"},"5370":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-33","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`Handler`'s methods:","locale":"en"},"5371":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-34","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"5372":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-35","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"5373":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-36","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`hooks()`","locale":"en"},"5374":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-37","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Announces no hooks","locale":"en"},"5375":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-38","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`initialize(host, params)`","locale":"en"},"5376":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-39","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Answers protocol version 1 and `hooks()`","locale":"en"},"5377":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-40","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`ui()`","locale":"en"},"5378":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-41","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`None`; return `Some(ui)` to announce the hook `ui` (whatever `initialize` answers) and have `ui.state` and `ui.call` answered by it","locale":"en"},"5379":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-42","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`ping(host)`","locale":"en"},"5380":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-43","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Answers at once","locale":"en"},"5381":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-44","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`request(host, method, params)`","locale":"en"},"5382":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-45","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Every other request: hooks, provider callbacks, panel and frame calls, service calls; `METHOD_NOT_FOUND` by default","locale":"en"},"5383":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-46","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`notification(host, method, params)`","locale":"en"},"5384":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-47","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"A notification (an event, a process's output); runs on the loop's thread, so it returns quickly and never calls the application","locale":"en"},"5385":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-48","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"`shutdown(host)`","locale":"en"},"5386":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-49","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Runs when the application asks it to shut down; `run` returns after it","locale":"en"},"5387":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-50","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api","content":"Both SDKs handle ordinary requests (including `deactivate`) on worker threads, where a handler may wait for a host call. They invoke `notification` and `shutdown` on the thread that reads replies. Return promptly from those two callbacks. Queue any work that needs a reply from a notification, and finish local cleanup synchronously in `shutdown`. Once the connection closes, pending and subsequent host calls fail with `UNAVAILABLE`.","locale":"en"},"5388":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-51","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-minimal-example","content":"A backend that provides an instance type: it checks the values, answers the install plan and the launch command, and logs a line from its `activate` hook.","locale":"en"},"5389":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-52","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-minimal-example","content":"The host starts its managed Python in the instance’s `core` directory. Open `/title.txt` on the allocated port to read the title written by the install step. For a native backend that serves HTTP itself, the Greeter example includes the `serve` subcommand and its dispatcher.","locale":"en"},"5390":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-53","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-minimal-example","content":"Install and launch plans are templates, where `{` and `}` read as placeholders. Double the braces\nof any text the backend did not write itself, such as a path or a setting's value, before putting\nit in a plan.","locale":"en"},"5391":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-54","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-ui-state","content":"A backend with a UI state returns its `Ui` from `Handler::ui`, and pushes each new state with `Host::emit_state`:","locale":"en"},"5392":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-55","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#python","content":"The Python SDK is `hanafubuki_extension`. It uses only the standard library and needs Python 3.10 or later. It ships with the application and is on a Python backend's `PYTHONPATH`, so a backend imports it directly; it goes neither in the package nor in `requirements`. To read it offline, or to run a backend outside the application, use its archive in the list above: its `tests/` show how the protocol is spoken.","locale":"en"},"5393":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-56","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"5394":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-57","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5395":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-58","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`run(handler)`","locale":"en"},"5396":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-59","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Runs until `shutdown` or the end of stdin; moves `sys.stdout` to stderr","locale":"en"},"5397":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-60","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`Handler`","locale":"en"},"5398":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-61","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Subclass it and override what you implement","locale":"en"},"5399":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-62","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`Host.call(method, params)`","locale":"en"},"5400":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-63","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Calls the application and waits; raises `RpcError` on failure","locale":"en"},"5401":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-64","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`Host.notify`, `Host.log(level, message)`, `Host.emit_frame(frame, event, payload)`, `Host.emit_state(state)`","locale":"en"},"5402":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-65","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Send notifications; `emit_frame` is `ui.frame.emit`, `emit_state` is `ui.emit`","locale":"en"},"5403":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-66","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`Host.initialize_params`","locale":"en"},"5404":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-67","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"What `initialize` said","locale":"en"},"5405":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-68","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`RpcError(code, message)`","locale":"en"},"5406":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-69","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Raise it to answer with that error; any other exception answers `INTERNAL_ERROR` with its type and message","locale":"en"},"5407":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-70","pag