ui_call(host, action, args, context)`","locale":"en"},"5444":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-107","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`ui.call`; an action it does not have is `INVALID_PARAMS` by default","locale":"en"},"5445":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-108","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"What the UI's call resolves with","locale":"en"},"5446":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-109","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`service(host, method, caller, params)`","locale":"en"},"5447":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-110","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`service.<method>`","locale":"en"},"5448":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-111","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"What the caller receives","locale":"en"},"5449":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-112","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`request(host, method, params)`","locale":"en"},"5450":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-113","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Any other request","locale":"en"},"5451":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-114","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Anything","locale":"en"},"5452":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-115","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`notification(host, method, params)`","locale":"en"},"5453":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-116","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"A notification; runs on the loop's thread","locale":"en"},"5454":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-117","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Nothing","locale":"en"},"5455":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-118","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"`shutdown(host)`","locale":"en"},"5456":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-119","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Called on the reader thread before the SDK replies and returns","locale":"en"},"5457":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-120","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"Nothing","locale":"en"},"5458":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-121","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#api-1","content":"The SDK passes `instance` to `validate_spec` by keyword when validating an existing instance with new values. Use a default of `None` for creation. If you override `initialize`, return the result of `super().initialize(host, params)` to keep the hooks inferred from your handler, including `ui` and `diagnostics`.","locale":"en"},"5459":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-122","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#a-minimal-example-1","content":"`launch_plan` runs the standard library's `http.server` with the backend's own interpreter (the application's managed Python) in the instance's `core` component, serving the page `install_plan` wrote. `servers.status` in `frame_call` needs `permissions.instances = \"own-types\"`. `ui_state` is the UI state a panel block with `\"source\": \"state\"` and `\"path\": \"visits\"` shows; each press of a panel action pushes the new one.","locale":"en"},"5460":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-123","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#without-an-sdk","content":"A backend may implement the protocol directly in any language: read and write JSON-RPC messages with the framing in The protocol in summary, and answer `initialize` (`protocolVersion` of `1`, `hooks` listing the hooks it implements), `ping`, and `shutdown`. Every method and its params are in the Interface Reference and the backend protocol reference.","locale":"en"},"5461":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-124","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#networking-and-per-process-proxy-selection","content":"Rust exposes `Host::http_request(&HttpRequestParams)`, `download_fetch(&DownloadFetchParams)`, and `process_run(&ProcessRunParams)`; types are re-exported through `protocol`. Python's same-named methods use the typed dict params/results in `hanafubuki_extension.protocol`. Omit optional fields for host defaults; the SDK does not repeat host validation.","locale":"en"},"5462":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-125","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#networking-and-per-process-proxy-selection","content":"The example requires the source hosts in the manifest's `network` permission and `processes = true`. Handle HTTP statuses in the caller; RPC failures raise `RpcError`. Use a publisher-provided expected `sha256`; without one, `cache` does not create reusable hits. Fields, defaults, permissions and bounds are in the generated reference.","locale":"en"},"5463":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-126","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#own-settings","content":"Rust reads with `host.settings()` and writes with `host.settings_patch(&SettingsPatchParams { patch })`. Python uses `host.settings_get()` and `host.settings_patch({\"patch\": {...}})`. Both return `{values}`. No extension id or extra permission is accepted: the host binds the caller to its own settings.","locale":"en"},"5464":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-127","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#own-settings","content":"`None` (wire `null`) removes the saved override and restores the declared default. Unknown setting keys and invalid values fail the entire patch; failed writes do not publish success. A successful save returns canonical values and publishes one `settings` event to this backend if it subscribed. Changes from the application's settings page, the backend and a custom frame use the same Rust validation and store. Avoid logging values: they may include secrets. For a custom frame, use `getSettings()` and `patchSettings(patch)`; these also work without a backend.","locale":"en"},"5465":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-128","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#host-preference-snapshots","content":"Rust uses `host.host_preferences() -> Result<HostPreferences, RpcError>`; Python uses `host.host_preferences() -> HostPreferences`. `HostPreferences` is also the `preferences` event's data type. These are read-only projections; a custom frame continues to use the existing theme/locale notifications.","locale":"en"},"5466":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-129","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#host-preference-snapshots","content":"Keep notification handlers quick and do not call the host from them. A proxy configuration change may emit an identical public snapshot; subsequent host networking calls use the latest policy. The Python SDK also exports `PreferencesEvent`, `HostNetworkPreferences`, and mirror types from `hanafubuki_extension.protocol`. Optional `instancesDir` and `mirrors` may be `None`; the snapshot never supplies proxy credentials.","locale":"en"},"5467":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-130","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#runtime-tools-and-diagnostics","content":"Rust has `host.runtime_status(&RuntimeStatusParams { tool: None })` and `host.runtime_resolve(&RuntimeResolveParams { tool: RuntimeTool::Python })`. Their results are `RuntimeStatusResult` and `RuntimeResolveResult`. Python uses the corresponding typed methods:","locale":"en"},"5468":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-131","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#runtime-tools-and-diagnostics","content":"Resolving and running require the manifest's `processes = true`. Status is read-only; resolve waits for the existing host preparation and stops with the backend. An optional `version` is verified version/output, not necessarily semver.","locale":"en"},"5469":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-132","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#runtime-tools-and-diagnostics","content":"A Python handler overrides `diagnostics_collect`; the SDK announces the `diagnostics` hook automatically:","locale":"en"},"5470":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-133","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#runtime-tools-and-diagnostics","content":"Rust implements `Diagnostics::collect(&self, host) -> Result<DiagnosticsCollectResult, RpcError>` and returns `Some(self)` from `Handler::diagnostics()`. The SDK adds the hook even with a custom initialize result and dispatches collection to the trait. Without a provider, the method follows the ordinary request handler. Document names are single filenames; return only your own diagnostic text and no credentials. The host enforces the limits shown in the generated reference.","locale":"en"},"5471":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-134","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#frame-host-operations-and-declarative-agent-content","content":"The frame SDK exports `openSettings(section: string): Promise<void>` and `openExternal(url: string): Promise<void>`. They wrap `open-settings` and `open-external` host requests; unknown sections, invalid URLs and host errors settle as `FrameError`. Use the frame examples.","locale":"en"},"5472":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-135","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#frame-host-operations-and-declarative-agent-content","content":"Agent Skills/MCP are manifest contributions, not backend SDK methods that write Agent configuration. The host adapts the declaration to a namespaced linked Agent package and keeps its lifecycle with the extension; see Agent contributions. Rust/Python backends can patch their own declared string settings used by `{setting: \"key\"}` references through `settings.patch`; a successful setting change refreshes the host-managed contribution.","locale":"en"},"5473":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks-136","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-sdks#frame-host-operations-and-declarative-agent-content","content":"The generated UI declarations also include frame-safe motion helpers and their associated types. For generic components used with Vue's `h`, explicitly instantiate the component, such as `NavList<Item>`, to retain the relationship between item props, event values and slot payloads. Do not assume `h` can infer every generic relationship automatically. The executable motion examples are checked strictly against `sdk/ui/ui.d.ts`, in the frame typings above; their documentation displays the same source that the linked gallery runs.","locale":"en"},"5474":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"page","content":"Testing and Packaging","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Extension Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","locale":"en"},"5475":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-0","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","content":"Build, test, package, install, and debug an extension, and copy it into a repository of its own, using the Greeter sample extension as the worked example.","locale":"en"},"5476":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-1","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#first-extension","content":"Try an extension without a build","locale":"en"},"5477":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-2","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"What is where","locale":"en"},"5478":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-3","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"How it works","locale":"en"},"5479":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-4","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"Building and packaging","locale":"en"},"5480":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-5","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#testing","content":"Testing","locale":"en"},"5481":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-6","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#the-program-on-its-own","content":"The program on its own","locale":"en"},"5482":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-7","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"End to end in the application's suite","locale":"en"},"5483":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-8","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#by-hand-in-the-application","content":"By hand in the application","locale":"en"},"5484":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-9","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"Linking a folder while you work","locale":"en"},"5485":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-10","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"Debugging and iterating","locale":"en"},"5486":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-11","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#copying-it-out","content":"Copying it out","locale":"en"},"5487":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-12","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","content":"Greeter is a complete sample extension, and you can download it. It is small, but it goes through the main paths an extension takes: a native backend on the Rust SDK, an instance type its backend provides, an install parameter, a preset that fills it, a server role the embedded browser opens, extension settings, a frame, a panel that follows the state its backend pushes, and text in two languages. The application's own tests build, install, and run it, and it is already a repository of its own, so it can start a new extension as it is.","locale":"en"},"5488":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-13","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#first-extension","content":"Download and unpack the configuration guide below, then open **Settings → Extensions → Install extension**, choose **Linked folder**, and select the unpacked `configuration-guide/`. Click **Check**, confirm the installation, and turn the extension on.","locale":"en"},"5489":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-14","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#first-extension","content":"On the new installation page, choose **Local notes** and the **Welcome note** preset. Change **Message** to a line you will recognize, then create and install the instance.","locale":"en"},"5490":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-15","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#first-extension","content":"Open the instance's `core` component directory. Its `notes.txt` should contain the line you entered. The preset in `presets/welcome.toml` fills the form, and the `write-file` step in `types/notes.toml` writes the final value. This type needs no download or running server. See the complete configuration files.","locale":"en"},"5491":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-16","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#first-extension","content":"To try a Python backend, unpack and link `configuration-python/`. To try the host's Vue components and theme, link `frame-components/`. The rest of this guide uses Greeter to show how to build and package a native backend.","locale":"en"},"5492":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-17","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"Path","locale":"en"},"5493":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-18","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"What","locale":"en"},"5494":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-19","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/hanafubuki-extension.toml`","locale":"en"},"5495":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-20","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"The manifest: id `com.example.greeter`, the backend program per OS, the `instances = \"own-types\"` permission, what it contributes","locale":"en"},"5496":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-21","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/types/greeter.toml`","locale":"en"},"5497":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-22","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"The `greeter` type: `provider = \"backend\"`, only the `core` component, no runtime, the `greeting` parameter, one `ui` server role","locale":"en"},"5498":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-23","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/presets/morning.toml`","locale":"en"},"5499":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-24","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"A preset over the `greeter` type: the new installation page lists it under Greeter and fills the greeting with it","locale":"en"},"5500":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-25","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/schemas/settings.json`","locale":"en"},"5501":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-26","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"Its Settings section: the `signature` field","locale":"en"},"5502":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-27","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/locales/en.json`, `zh.json`","locale":"en"},"5503":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-28","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"Its text, merged under `ext['com.example.greeter']`","locale":"en"},"5504":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-29","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/ui/status.html`, `status.js`","locale":"en"},"5505":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-30","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"A frame in the instance's management showing the instance's servers and, from the UI state, how many greetings were sent","locale":"en"},"5506":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-31","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`package/ui/greetings.json`","locale":"en"},"5507":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-32","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"A panel in Settings: a **Greet** action and a table of the greetings sent, shown from the UI state (`\"source\": \"state\"`)","locale":"en"},"5508":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-33","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`src/main.rs`","locale":"en"},"5509":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-34","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"One program, two modes: the backend without arguments, the instance's server with `serve`","locale":"en"},"5510":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-35","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`src/backend.rs`","locale":"en"},"5511":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-36","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"The backend: `provider.validateSpec`, `provider.installPlan`, `provider.launchPlan`, the frame's `status` call, the panel's `greet` action, and its UI state (`Ui`, `Host::emit_state`)","locale":"en"},"5512":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-37","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`src/server.rs`","locale":"en"},"5513":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-38","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"The instance's HTTP server: `/` the greeting, `/health` its readiness","locale":"en"},"5514":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-39","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`tests/greeter.rs`","locale":"en"},"5515":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-40","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"The program on its own: the backend over its stdio, the server over HTTP","locale":"en"},"5516":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-41","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"`Cargo.toml`","locale":"en"},"5517":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-42","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#what-is-where","content":"Crate `greeter-extension`, binary `greeter`, `publish = false`, with the SDK and protocol crates in `vendor/` beside it","locale":"en"},"5518":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-43","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"Greeter uses the same binary for its extension backend and its instance server. At instance start, the backend reads the user's saved signature, finds its own program with `std::env::current_exe()`, and returns a command that runs it with `serve`. For a server with a fixed command, a declarative type can also use `{extension.root}` to run a program or script from its package. See Placeholders.","locale":"en"},"5519":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-44","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"**Create**: the application checks the values against the type's form, then asks `provider.validateSpec`, which refuses a greeting over 200 characters.","locale":"en"},"5520":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-45","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"**Install**: `provider.installPlan` answers one `write-file` step, `{component.core}/greeting.txt` from `{param.greeting}`. The application resolves the placeholders and keeps the step inside `core`.","locale":"en"},"5521":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-46","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"**Start**: `provider.launchPlan` answers `[<the program>, \"serve\", \"--port\", \"{port}\", \"--signature\", <setting>]`, the signature being the extension setting read with `settings.get`. A plan is a template, so the backend doubles every brace in text it did not write. The application starts it in `core` on the port it allocated, and opens the role in the embedded browser once `/health` answers.","locale":"en"},"5522":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-47","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"**The frame**: `ui/status.html` calls `status`, which the backend answers with `servers.status` for the instance (so it needs `permissions.instances = \"own-types\"`).","locale":"en"},"5523":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-48","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#how-it-works","content":"**The UI state**: the backend's state is the greetings sent, `{ \"greetings\": { \"rows\": [...] } }`. **Greet** in the **Greetings** panel sends `ui.panel.action`; the backend keeps the greeting and pushes the new state with `emit_state`, and the panel's table, whose block names `\"source\": \"state\"` and `\"path\": \"greetings\"`, changes without a query. The frame follows the same state with `state()` and `onState()`.","locale":"en"},"5524":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-49","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"In the unpacked `greeter/`, build the program for the current operating system:","locale":"en"},"5525":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-50","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"`target/release/greeter` (`greeter.exe` on Windows) is both the backend and the instance's server. The package is `package/`: copy the program to `package/bin/`, then pack the contents of `package/` so that `hanafubuki-extension.toml` sits at the archive's root or inside its one directory. Either the folder or the archive installs from **Settings → Extensions**.","locale":"en"},"5526":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-51","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"That is the binary for one platform. When publishing a native backend, supply a matching binary for each OS and architecture you support. In `latest.json`, use the host's platform and architecture names, such as `windows` and `x86_64` for Windows x64, or `macos` and `aarch64` for Apple silicon, and keep each archive's actual filename in its download URL. See Publishing updates.","locale":"en"},"5527":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-52","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"When you package an extension of your own, check that:","locale":"en"},"5528":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-53","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"the manifest says `engines.api = 1`;","locale":"en"},"5529":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-54","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"every path in `[backend].command` has its program, with the executable bit kept on Linux and macOS;","locale":"en"},"5530":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-55","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#building-and-packaging","content":"the archive is a `.zip`, `.tar`, `.tar.gz`, `.tar.xz`, or `.tar.bz2` with the manifest at its root or inside its one directory, and holds no symbolic links.","locale":"en"},"5531":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-56","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#the-program-on-its-own","content":"runs `tests/greeter.rs`: it starts the `greeter` program, sends `initialize`, `provider.validateSpec`, and `provider.installPlan` as protocol frames and checks the answers, then starts it in `serve` mode on a free port and checks `/health`, the greeting page, and a 404. Tests like these need no application and belong in the extension's own repository.","locale":"en"},"5532":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-57","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#the-program-on-its-own","content":"A backend on the Rust SDK can also be tested without a process, with `run_on(handler, reader, writer)` over in-memory streams. A Python backend can be run as a subprocess with the unpacked Python SDK on its `PYTHONPATH` and spoken to with protocol frames.","locale":"en"},"5533":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-58","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"The application's suite holds `src-tauri/src/api_server/declared/tests/greeter.rs`. It lays the package out as `bun run example:extension` does, then:","locale":"en"},"5534":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-59","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"prepares and installs it from the folder through the extension store, turns it on, and mounts it;","locale":"en"},"5535":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-60","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"writes the `signature` setting and starts the backend, then presses the panel's **Greet** and checks the backend pushes its new UI state (another test mounts the extension as the application does and checks the panel's table, read through the application, follows that push);","locale":"en"},"5536":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-61","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"creates an instance with a greeting that is too long and checks the backend refuses it, then creates, installs, and starts one with a good greeting;","locale":"en"},"5537":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-62","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"checks the `ui` role runs and that `/health` and the greeting page (with the signature) answer;","locale":"en"},"5538":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-63","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"checks the frame's page and the frame client are served from the package, and that the frame's `status` call answers with the role;","locale":"en"},"5539":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-64","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"stops the instance and the backend, then uninstalls the extension with its data.","locale":"en"},"5540":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-65","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"It runs with `bun run test:rust`, which also builds the workspace's `greeter`. Before the first build of the application tests, prepare the runtime assets, MCP sidecar, and frame component bundle from the repository root. To run this test on its own, build the Greeter program as well.","locale":"en"},"5541":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-66","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#end-to-end-in-the-applications-suite","content":"`editing_the_linked_greeters_panel_shows_on_reload_with_no_reinstall` (in `src-tauri/src/extensions/tests/link.rs`) links a temporary copy of the same package instead, edits its panel in the folder, and checks that the panel the extension serves changes on **Reload** and not before.","locale":"en"},"5542":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-67","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#by-hand-in-the-application","content":"Open the **Extensions** section of the Settings window, click **Install extension**, choose the\n`package/` folder (with the program in `package/bin/`) or the archive you packed, click\n**Check**, then **Install**.","locale":"en"},"5543":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-68","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#by-hand-in-the-application","content":"Create an instance of the **Greeter** type, install it, and start it; the greeting page opens in\nthe WebUI tab.","locale":"en"},"5544":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-69","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#by-hand-in-the-application","content":"Open the **Greeter status** frame under the **Extensions** group of the instance's management\npage; change **Signature** in the **Greeter** section of the Settings window, which takes effect\nat the instance's next start; press **Greet** in the **Greetings** section and watch its table\nchange.","locale":"en"},"5545":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-70","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"An installed extension is a copy: editing its source changes nothing until you install it again. While you work on one, link its folder instead:","locale":"en"},"5546":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-71","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"Open the **Extensions** section of the Settings window, click **Install extension**, choose\n**Linked folder**, and pick the folder that holds the manifest. For the sample that is\n`package/`, since a command backend needs its program in `package/bin/`; a data-only extension\ncan link its source folder as it is.","locale":"en"},"5547":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-72","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"Click **Check**, then **Install**: the folder is checked as a folder install checks it and\nconfirmed as any package, but it is not copied. Its card says **Development · linked to** the\nfolder.","locale":"en"},"5548":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-73","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"Turn it on. After you change a file in the folder (a panel, a string, a type, the manifest, or a\nrebuilt program in `bin/`), press **Reload** on its card: the application reads the folder again\nand mounts the extension, restarting its backend, with no reinstall.","locale":"en"},"5549":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-74","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"When reloading a linked folder, keep the following in mind.","locale":"en"},"5550":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-75","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"A symbolic link anywhere in the folder is refused, when you link it and at every Reload, as a folder install refuses one. A build that leaves links behind (`node_modules/.bin`, for one) belongs outside the folder you link.","locale":"en"},"5551":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-76","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"A file that no longer reads, such as a manifest with a typo or a file you saved halfway, fails the Reload with its issues on the card; fix it and press **Reload** again.","locale":"en"},"5552":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-77","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"You can keep the same version while editing the manifest and contributions. Keep the extension ID the same. To change the ID, install the folder as a new extension.","locale":"en"},"5553":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-78","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"If the extension is active and instances of its types are running, **Reload** lists their names. Stop those instances, then click **Reload** again.","locale":"en"},"5554":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-79","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"Its settings and data are the application's, as for any extension, and stay across Reloads.","locale":"en"},"5555":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-80","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"A linked extension is never updated, and an id installed as a copy cannot also be linked, nor the reverse: uninstall the one to install the other. Uninstalling a link removes only what the application recorded; your folder stays as it is.","locale":"en"},"5556":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-81","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#linking-a-folder-while-you-work","content":"Linked folders are checked on Linux; on Windows and macOS their paths have not been verified yet.","locale":"en"},"5557":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-82","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"**Read the log**: what the backend writes to stderr, and `log.write`, go to the extension's log; click **View log** on its card. Never write to stdout: that breaks the protocol's frames and the backend is treated as faulted.","locale":"en"},"5558":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-83","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"**The install fails**: the error lists each problem with its place, such as `types/greeter.toml: servers[0].readiness`; compare it with Manifest keys and Instance types.","locale":"en"},"5559":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-84","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"**Can't run**: the card says why; most often `engines.api` is missing or there is no program for this operating system.","locale":"en"},"5560":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-85","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"**Repeated crashes**: a backend that exits before it has run for 30 seconds three times in a row is not started again by itself. Fix it, then click **Retry**.","locale":"en"},"5561":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-86","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"**Updating what is installed**: an installed extension is a copy in the application's store, so editing the source files does not change it. Updating to the same version is refused, so either raise `version` and use **Update**, or uninstall (keeping settings and data) and install again. While iterating, link the folder instead and press **Reload**.","locale":"en"},"5562":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-87","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#debugging-and-iterating","content":"**Repeated crashes of a linked extension**: **Reload** clears the crash marker as **Retry** does, so a backend that still crashes stops again after three starts.","locale":"en"},"5563":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-88","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#copying-it-out","content":"Replace `com.example.greeter` everywhere (the manifest's `id`, the text keys in `types/` and\n`schemas/`) with an id of your own.","locale":"en"},"5564":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-89","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#copying-it-out","content":"Keep `vendor/`, which holds the SDK and protocol crates `Cargo.toml` depends on by path.","locale":"en"},"5565":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing-90","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-testing#copying-it-out","content":"Write a packaging script of your own: build the program, put it in `package/bin/`, and pack\n`package/` as above.","locale":"en"},"5566":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"page","content":"Interface","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Extension Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","locale":"en"},"5567":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-0","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"An extension's settings form, panels (info, table, log, actions, progress, status, list, markdown, empty, loading), its UI state pushed to panels and frames, frames - how they load, the client API, theme variables, and security limits - and text in several languages.","locale":"en"},"5568":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-1","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#writing-text","content":"Writing text","locale":"en"},"5569":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-2","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Settings","locale":"en"},"5570":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-3","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Panels","locale":"en"},"5571":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-4","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"UI state","locale":"en"},"5572":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-5","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#blocks-from-the-ui-state","content":"Blocks from the UI state","locale":"en"},"5573":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-6","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#frames","content":"Frames","locale":"en"},"5574":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-7","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"How a page loads","locale":"en"},"5575":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-8","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The frame client","locale":"en"},"5576":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-9","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"The UI kit","locale":"en"},"5577":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-10","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"The component bundle","locale":"en"},"5578":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-11","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Theme variables","locale":"en"},"5579":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-12","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"Security limits","locale":"en"},"5580":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-13","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#read-and-save-this-extensions-settings","content":"Read and save this extension's settings","locale":"en"},"5581":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-14","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#open-host-settings-and-external-links","content":"Open host settings and external links","locale":"en"},"5582":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-15","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-tokens-and-local-motion","content":"Theme tokens and local motion","locale":"en"},"5583":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-16","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#text-and-languages","content":"Text and languages","locale":"en"},"5584":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-17","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"An extension can appear in the application's interface in four ways. The settings form and panels are rendered by the application with its own components, from the extension's descriptions and data; a frame is the extension's own HTML page, running in a sandboxed iframe; text is referenced by all of these and by instance type descriptors. Every frame message, UI kit class, panel block, and form field is listed in the Interface Reference.","locale":"en"},"5585":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-18","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Way","locale":"en"},"5586":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-19","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Rendered by","locale":"en"},"5587":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-20","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Data from","locale":"en"},"5588":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-21","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Needs a backend","locale":"en"},"5589":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-22","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Settings","locale":"en"},"5590":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-23","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"The application","locale":"en"},"5591":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-24","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"The extension's settings store","locale":"en"},"5592":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-25","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"No","locale":"en"},"5593":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-26","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Panels","locale":"en"},"5594":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-27","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"The application","locale":"en"},"5595":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-28","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"`ui.panel.query`, `ui.panel.action`, or the UI state","locale":"en"},"5596":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-29","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"5597":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-30","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Frames","locale":"en"},"5598":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-31","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"The extension page","locale":"en"},"5599":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-32","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"`ui.frame.call`, `ui.frame.emit`, the UI state","locale":"en"},"5600":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-33","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"For its calls","locale":"en"},"5601":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-34","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"Text","locale":"en"},"5602":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-35","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"The application","locale":"en"},"5603":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-36","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"The `locales` files","locale":"en"},"5604":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-37","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"No","locale":"en"},"5605":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-38","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","content":"In a `contributes.ui` entry for a management panel or frame, use `types = [\"notes\"]` to show it only for the named local instance types. Omit the field to show it for all of your types.","locale":"en"},"5606":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-39","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#writing-text","content":"The settings form and panels are JSON files, where each text takes one of two forms:","locale":"en"},"5607":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-40","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#writing-text","content":"`literal` uses the current language, then English, then the first entry in the table. A `key` must start with `ext.<extension id>.` and can pass string substitutions in `params`. For example, `\"params\": { \"name\": \"Greeter\" }` supplies the value of `{name}` in the translated message. See Text and languages.","locale":"en"},"5608":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-41","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"The manifest's `contributes.settings` names a JSON array, each element a form field. Once the extension is on, the Settings window shows a section named after the extension.","locale":"en"},"5609":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-42","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"5610":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-43","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5611":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-44","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`key`","locale":"en"},"5612":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-45","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Required; of `A-Z`, `a-z`, `0-9`, `_`, `-`, not repeated","locale":"en"},"5613":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-46","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`kind`","locale":"en"},"5614":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-47","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Required: `text`, `number`, `boolean`, `select`, `multiselect`, `path`, `secret`, `slider`, `textarea`","locale":"en"},"5615":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-48","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`label`","locale":"en"},"5616":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-49","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Required, a text","locale":"en"},"5617":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-50","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`help`","locale":"en"},"5618":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-51","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Help text","locale":"en"},"5619":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-52","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`options`","locale":"en"},"5620":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-53","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Required for `select` and `multiselect`: a list of `{ \"value\": \"…\", \"label\": text }`","locale":"en"},"5621":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-54","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`min`, `max`, `step`","locale":"en"},"5622":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-55","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"A number's bounds and step; a `slider` needs both `min` and `max`","locale":"en"},"5623":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-56","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`pathKind`","locale":"en"},"5624":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-57","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"A `path` field's `directory` or `file`","locale":"en"},"5625":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-58","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`nullable`, `unsetLabel`","locale":"en"},"5626":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-59","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"\"Not set\" is a value to choose, labelled by `unsetLabel`","locale":"en"},"5627":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-60","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`required`, `default`","locale":"en"},"5628":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-61","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Whether it must have a value; its default","locale":"en"},"5629":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-62","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`visibleWhen`, `requiredWhen`, `disabledWhen`, `disabledReason`","locale":"en"},"5630":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-63","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Conditions, written as for instance type parameters","locale":"en"},"5631":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-64","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`advanced`","locale":"en"},"5632":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-65","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"A secondary field with a working default","locale":"en"},"5633":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-66","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`commit`","locale":"en"},"5634":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-67","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`change`, `blur`, or `manual`; a `manual` field is submitted only with Save","locale":"en"},"5635":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-68","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`patchGroup`","locale":"en"},"5636":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-69","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Fields of one group are submitted together","locale":"en"},"5637":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-70","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"`optionsSource` is refused: it is for the application's own forms only.","locale":"en"},"5638":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-71","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"The values are stored with the extension (`extensions/<id>/settings.json`), not in the application's settings. The section reads and saves them only while the extension runs; the application checks a change against the whole form and writes nothing that does not read. The backend reads the values with `settings.get`, and once subscribed to `settings` events hears of every save. A value whose field was removed, or that its field no longer takes, is ignored, and the section shows the default.","locale":"en"},"5639":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-72","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#settings","content":"Use `[[contributes.settingsGroups]]` to group field keys in display order. Supply a localized title and optionally a built-in scrolling Settings category such as `automation` or `runtime`. The categories are `language`, `paths`, `network`, `mirrors`, `runtime`, `environmentTools`, `logs`, `webview`, `automation` and `about`; `modules` and `extensions` keep a bounded page and take no groups, and any other value is reported where the group is declared. The extension's own section also lists these groups and any ungrouped fields. Edits use the extension's settings store from either page. An open form refreshes after the backend or another window writes and preserves edits the user has not submitted.","locale":"en"},"5640":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-73","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Use `slot = \"home.sections\"` in a schema panel's manifest entry to show it below the Home tile grid, or `slot = \"taskCenter.tabs\"` to add a Task Center tab. Both receive an empty instance context. When the selected extension tab is removed, Tasks opens. Set `home = true` on a `pages` frame to open the same page from a Home tile and the title bar.","locale":"en"},"5641":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-74","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Set `\"cardMenu\": true` on a management or diagnostics panel or a standalone button in its `actions` block to add it to matching instance card menus. It uses the same fields, confirmation and maintenance operation. Set `toolbar` as well to share one action between both placements.","locale":"en"},"5642":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-75","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Use `slot = \"management.overview\"` on a schema panel to put read-only `info`, `status`, `table` or `progress` blocks on the instance overview. Scope it with the same optional `types` list as a management section. Queries and pushed state work in both places. In a `management.sections` actions block, a button such as `{\"id\":\"repair\",\"operation\":\"repair-index\",\"label\":{\"kind\":\"literal\",\"text\":{\"en\":\"Repair index\"}}}` uses the selected type’s `management.forms.repair-index` and runs under exclusive maintenance. A type without that operation omits the button. Reloading a linked extension also refreshes its panels and translations at the same version.","locale":"en"},"5643":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-76","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Set the slot to `management.diagnostics` for an interactive instance check. Display results using the usual status or list blocks and reference the existing maintenance operation for a repair. Use `diagnostics.collectInstance` for documents that should travel with an exported diagnostic bundle.","locale":"en"},"5644":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-77","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"On a management or diagnostic schema panel, set `\"toolbar\": \"button\"` to open the panel from its instance's title bar. The same property on a standalone button in an `actions` block exposes that action directly with its label and confirmation. Use `\"toolbar\": \"externalBrowser\"` for a shortcut that takes the place of the external-browser button while the WebUI is showing. The WebUI tabs context menu can still open the current page.","locale":"en"},"5645":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-78","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Declare the slot in `[contributes]` and point `source` to the panel JSON in the package.","locale":"en"},"5646":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-79","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"A panel has an `id`, a `title`, and `blocks`. Panel and frame IDs must be unique across the extension, even when contributed to different slots. Each block has a `kind`, an `id` unique within its panel (letters A–Z or a–z, digits, `_`, or `-`), and an optional `title`. Action IDs are shared across all `actions` and `list` blocks in that panel.","locale":"en"},"5647":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-80","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`kind`","locale":"en"},"5648":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-81","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Other keys","locale":"en"},"5649":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-82","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"The backend answers `ui.panel.query` with","locale":"en"},"5650":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-83","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`info`","locale":"en"},"5651":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-84","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"None","locale":"en"},"5652":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-85","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"rows\": [{ \"label\": …, \"value\": … }] }`","locale":"en"},"5653":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-86","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`table`","locale":"en"},"5654":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-87","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`columns`: at least one, each a `key` (unique) and a `label`","locale":"en"},"5655":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-88","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"rows\": [{ \"<column key>\": value }] }`","locale":"en"},"5656":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-89","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`log`","locale":"en"},"5657":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-90","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`follow`: `true` keeps it at its end as lines arrive, until the user scrolls up","locale":"en"},"5658":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-91","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"lines\": [\"…\"] }`","locale":"en"},"5659":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-92","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`actions`","locale":"en"},"5660":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-93","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`actions`: at least one, each an `id` (unique), a `label`, an optional `confirm` (text asked before it runs), and `fields` (a form, written as the settings are)","locale":"en"},"5661":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-94","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"No data","locale":"en"},"5662":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-95","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`progress`","locale":"en"},"5663":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-96","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"None","locale":"en"},"5664":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-97","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"value\": 0.42, \"label\": \"…\" }`: `value` from 0 to 1; without a number the bar sweeps","locale":"en"},"5665":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-98","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`status`","locale":"en"},"5666":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-99","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`inline`: `true` shows a badge beside the message instead of a bar","locale":"en"},"5667":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-100","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"severity\": \"warning\", \"title\": \"…\", \"message\": \"…\" }`: `info`, `success`, `warning`, or `error`","locale":"en"},"5668":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-101","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`list`","locale":"en"},"5669":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-102","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`actions`: buttons each row may offer, written as an actions block's but without `fields`","locale":"en"},"5670":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-103","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"rows\": [{ \"id\": \"…\", \"title\": \"…\", \"description\": \"…\", \"status\": { \"label\": \"…\", \"severity\": \"success\" }, \"actions\": [\"<action id>\"] }] }`","locale":"en"},"5671":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-104","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`markdown`","locale":"en"},"5672":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-105","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"None","locale":"en"},"5673":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-106","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"text\": \"## Markdown\" }`","locale":"en"},"5674":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-107","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`empty`","locale":"en"},"5675":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-108","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"None","locale":"en"},"5676":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-109","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"title\": \"…\", \"text\": \"…\" }`: the \"nothing here\" state","locale":"en"},"5677":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-110","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`loading`","locale":"en"},"5678":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-111","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"None","locale":"en"},"5679":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-112","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`{ \"text\": \"…\" }`: a spinner","locale":"en"},"5680":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-113","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"A list of models, each with its state and the buttons it offers:","locale":"en"},"5681":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-114","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"An `info` row needs a `label`, and a `list` row needs a `title`. A `table` accepts object rows and displays the declared columns, leaving missing cells blank. Each block keeps the first 500 rows, except a log, which keeps the last 500 lines. Cells show `null` as blank and other non-string values as JSON, up to 2048 characters per cell. Markdown is limited to 65,536 characters. Progress values are clamped to 0–1, with non-numeric values shown as indeterminate. Unknown severities display as `info`.","locale":"en"},"5682":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-115","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"A list row offers the actions its `actions` names, or all of the block's without it; a row without an `id` offers none. Pressing one calls `ui.panel.action` with `row`, the row's `id`, after asking its `confirm`.","locale":"en"},"5683":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-116","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"A `progress`, `status`, `markdown`, `empty`, or `loading` block is not shown while its answer is not an object (`null`, or a state path to nothing), so the backend shows and hides it by its data: a `loading` block while it scans, an `empty` one when there is nothing.","locale":"en"},"5684":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-117","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Markdown is rendered without its HTML: a tag in the text shows as text, links (http, https, mailto) open in the browser, and fenced code has a copy button.","locale":"en"},"5685":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-118","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"A block of a kind this version of the application does not know says in its place that it can't be shown, and the rest of the panel works; raise `engines` when a panel needs a newer kind.","locale":"en"},"5686":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-119","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"When an action is pressed, the application checks its form and calls `ui.panel.action` with `panel`, `action`, `values`, `context`, and `row`. A regular button sends `row: null`. A list action sends `values: {}`. The backend may return `{ \"notice\": \"…\" }` to display a message.","locale":"en"},"5687":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-120","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"`context` is `{ \"instanceId\": \"…\" }` in instance management and `{ \"instanceId\": null }` in Settings. A `management.sections` panel handles only instances of the extension's own types.","locale":"en"},"5688":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-121","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Opening the panel, pressing Refresh, or finishing an action queries all blocks that use `ui.panel.query` concurrently. Each call has a 30 s bound. A failed query puts the whole panel into its retry view. A failed action shows its error in the panel and still refreshes the queried blocks.","locale":"en"},"5689":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-122","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"Any block but `actions` may name `\"source\": \"state\"` and a `\"path\"`: it is shown from the backend's UI state instead, and never queried (see Blocks from the UI state). A followed `log` or a `progress` from the state changes with each push.","locale":"en"},"5690":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-123","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#panels","content":"A panel action neither stops the instance nor holds its maintenance, so it must not change the instance's files. When it needs to, declare an operation of the type's own instead (see Types a backend provides).","locale":"en"},"5691":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-124","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"A backend that lists the hook `ui` in `initialize`'s `hooks` has one UI state: a JSON value its panels and frames show, which it pushes whenever it changes, so nothing polls it. A backend that does not list `ui` is unaffected.","locale":"en"},"5692":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-125","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Direction","locale":"en"},"5693":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-126","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"5694":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-127","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Params","locale":"en"},"5695":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-128","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"5696":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-129","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Application → backend","locale":"en"},"5697":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-130","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`ui.state`","locale":"en"},"5698":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-131","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`context`","locale":"en"},"5699":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-132","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"The state","locale":"en"},"5700":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-133","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Application → backend","locale":"en"},"5701":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-134","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`ui.call`","locale":"en"},"5702":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-135","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`action`, `args`, `context`","locale":"en"},"5703":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-136","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Anything, to that caller only","locale":"en"},"5704":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-137","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Backend → application","locale":"en"},"5705":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-138","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`ui.emit` (a notification)","locale":"en"},"5706":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-139","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`state`, optional `instanceId`","locale":"en"},"5707":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-140","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"None","locale":"en"},"5708":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-141","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`context` is `{ \"instanceId\": \"…\" }` in instance management (for instances of the extension's own types) and `{ \"instanceId\": null }` elsewhere. Set the optional `instanceId` on a state push to reach only views of that instance. Omitting it broadcasts to all subscribers.","locale":"en"},"5709":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-142","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"A panel with state-backed blocks reads `ui.state` when it opens, when the backend restarts, and after each push, so keep this method cheap. A frame page reads its initial snapshot by calling `state()` itself and listens for pushes with `onState(listener)`. Calling `ready()` starts the handshake and reports the page height. Both `ui.state` and `ui.call` have a 10 s bound.","locale":"en"},"5710":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-143","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"An error keeps its kind: `INVALID_PARAMS` is `invalid`, `PERMISSION_DENIED` is `forbidden`, any other is `failed`.","locale":"en"},"5711":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-144","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"Pushes are coalesced: the first goes out at once. During the next 100 ms the host keeps the latest broadcast and the latest following state for each instance. A state larger than 256 KiB as JSON is not sent.","locale":"en"},"5712":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-145","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"`ui.emit` is a notification only: sent as a request, it is answered `METHOD_NOT_FOUND`.","locale":"en"},"5713":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-146","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"A `ui.emit` sent before the backend's UI is up, such as during `activate`, is dropped. Keep the latest snapshot available through `ui.state` for panels and frames that open later.","locale":"en"},"5714":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-147","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#ui-state","content":"The SDKs: in Rust, return a `Ui` from `Handler::ui` and push with `Host::emit_state`; in Python, override `ui_state` (and `ui_call`) and push with `host.emit_state` (see SDKs).","locale":"en"},"5715":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-148","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#blocks-from-the-ui-state","content":"A panel block names where its data comes from:","locale":"en"},"5716":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-149","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#blocks-from-the-ui-state","content":"`\"source\": \"state\"` shows the block from the UI state; without it (or with `\"query\"`, the default) the block is queried with `ui.panel.query`. Any other value is an error at install.","locale":"en"},"5717":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-150","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#blocks-from-the-ui-state","content":"`path` is a dotted path of object keys into the state (`\"greetings\"`, `\"queue.jobs\"`); without it the block shows the whole state. A `path` without `\"source\": \"state\"` is an error at install.","locale":"en"},"5718":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-151","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#blocks-from-the-ui-state","content":"What is at the path is written as `ui.panel.query` would answer for the block (`{ \"rows\": [...] }`, `{ \"lines\": [...] }`) and read by the application as tolerantly, within the same bounds. Here the state is `{ \"greetings\": { \"rows\": [{ \"to\": \"world\" }] } }`.","locale":"en"},"5719":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-152","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#blocks-from-the-ui-state","content":"The block follows every push without a query: the application reads `ui.state` again and shows what is at the path. When the state cannot be read, the block says why in its place until a state arrives; while the backend is not running, or does not list `ui`, it shows no rows.","locale":"en"},"5720":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-153","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#frames","content":"A `ui` entry of `kind = \"frame\"` is a frame, its `entry` an HTML page of the package. Its section is named by its `title` (or the extension's name); a `management.sections` frame shows only for instances of the extension's own types.","locale":"en"},"5721":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-154","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#frames","content":"A frame in the `pages` slot is a page of its own in the application rather than a section, for an interface that belongs to no instance and is larger than a Settings section (a downloader, a model library). Only frames go there. Its calls and state are a Settings frame's: no instance.","locale":"en"},"5722":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-155","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#frames","content":"The title bar shows an **Extension pages** button while some extension has a page; its menu lists each page by its `title` (or the extension's name), and choosing one opens it at `/extensions/<extension id>/<frame id>`.","locale":"en"},"5723":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-156","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#frames","content":"The page fills the window's content area under the title bar, which shows its title. It has no header and no height of its own: the frame takes the whole area whatever height the page reports, so a page scrolls its own content.","locale":"en"},"5724":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-157","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#frames","content":"While the extension is off, or has failed, its page says so in its place.","locale":"en"},"5725":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-158","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"A frame's page is served read-only from the extension's **active** version's directory, through the `hfext` scheme the application registers:","locale":"en"},"5726":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-159","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"Platform","locale":"en"},"5727":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-160","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"Page address","locale":"en"},"5728":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-161","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"Linux, macOS","locale":"en"},"5729":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-162","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"`hfext://<extension id>/<path>`","locale":"en"},"5730":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-163","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"5731":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-164","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"`http://hfext.localhost/<extension id>/<path>`","locale":"en"},"5732":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-165","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"On Windows the package's root is `/<extension id>/`, not `/`. An absolute path starting with `/` points to the wrong place there, so refer to scripts, styles, and images by relative URLs (`./status.js`, `../__hanafubuki/frame.js`).","locale":"en"},"5733":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-166","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#how-a-page-loads","content":"Only regular files of the package load; `..`, a backslash, a link that leads out of the package, a directory, or a missing file is a 404, as is any file of an extension that is not running. The content type follows the file's extension (`html`, `js`/`mjs`, `css`, `json`, `svg`, `png`, `jpg`, `gif`, `webp`, `avif`, `ico`, `woff`/`woff2`, `ttf`, `otf`, and so on).","locale":"en"},"5734":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-167","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The application serves the frame client at the reserved path `__hanafubuki/frame.js` of every package's root (a file of that name in the package is replaced by it). It is an ES module, imported by a relative URL:","locale":"en"},"5735":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-168","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Function","locale":"en"},"5736":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-169","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5737":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-170","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`ready()`","locale":"en"},"5738":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-171","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Tells the application the page is ready; from then on it sends the theme, follows the page's height, and pings it. A frame that does not call it within 10 s shows **Unavailable**","locale":"en"},"5739":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-172","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`call(method, params)`","locale":"en"},"5740":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-173","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Calls the backend, which receives `ui.frame.call` with `frame`, `method`, `params`, and `context` (`{instanceId}` in an instance's management, `instanceId` null in Settings and on a page); the promise resolves with the backend's answer or rejects with a `FrameError`","locale":"en"},"5741":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-174","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`on(event, listener)`","locale":"en"},"5742":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-175","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Listens to the events the backend sends this frame with `ui.frame.emit`; returns how to stop listening","locale":"en"},"5743":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-176","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`state()`","locale":"en"},"5744":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-177","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Reads the UI state (`ui.state` with the frame's context); resolves with the state or rejects with a `FrameError` (`unavailable` without the hook `ui`)","locale":"en"},"5745":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-178","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`onState(listener)`","locale":"en"},"5746":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-179","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Listens to each state the backend pushes (`ui.emit`); returns how to stop listening. A state pushed before it listened is not sent again, so read `state()` once as well","locale":"en"},"5747":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-180","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`getSettings()`, `patchSettings(patch)`","locale":"en"},"5748":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-181","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Read and save this extension’s settings through the host, including in a data-only frame. Settings example","locale":"en"},"5749":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-182","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`openSettings(section)`, `openExternal(url)`","locale":"en"},"5750":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-183","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Open a registered Settings section or an HTTP(S) link. Navigation example","locale":"en"},"5751":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-184","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`pickDirectory({ title }?)`","locale":"en"},"5752":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-185","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Opens the application's folder dialog (its `title` cut at 200 characters) and resolves with the native path the user chose, or `null` when they cancelled. The page gets the path alone and cannot read the folder: pass it to the backend, which acts on it","locale":"en"},"5753":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-186","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`updateInstance(values, mode?)`","locale":"en"},"5754":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-187","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Confirms and runs `\"update\"` or an in-place `\"reinstall\"` with the supplied install values (up to 64). The default is update for a ready type offering it, otherwise reinstall. The host offers unchecked rebuild switches for eligible components during reinstall. Update keeps their directories.","locale":"en"},"5755":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-188","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`navigateInstance(instanceId)`","locale":"en"},"5756":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-189","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Takes the user to an instance's page, as a downloader does after registering one; resolves once the application is on its way there, which may close the frame","locale":"en"},"5757":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-190","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`locale()`","locale":"en"},"5758":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-191","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The application's language (`en`, `zh`), or `null` until the first theme arrives after `ready()`; the client also sets it as the root's `lang`","locale":"en"},"5759":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-192","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`onLocale(listener)`","locale":"en"},"5760":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-193","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Listens to the application's language: called when it first arrives and on each change; returns how to stop listening","locale":"en"},"5761":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-194","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The client's typings are `sdk/frame/frame.d.ts`, in the frame typings download below, beside the component bundle's. A page imports the runtime by the relative URL `__hanafubuki/frame.js`, and `paths` does not resolve a relative import: declare those two URLs in your own repository, and map the names the declaration re-exports to the archive. Do not write your own typings.","locale":"en"},"5762":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-195","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The archive's README gives the declaration and the `tsconfig.json` in full. The component bundle's typings take their Vue types from `vue`, so that mapping points at the Vue version your page runs.","locale":"en"},"5763":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-196","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"A `FrameError`'s `kind` is one of:","locale":"en"},"5764":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-197","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`kind`","locale":"en"},"5765":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-198","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"5766":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-199","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`unavailable`","locale":"en"},"5767":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-200","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"No backend (a data-only extension), or it is not running","locale":"en"},"5768":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-201","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`timeout`","locale":"en"},"5769":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-202","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The backend did not answer within 30 s (10 s for `state()`)","locale":"en"},"5770":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-203","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`invalid`","locale":"en"},"5771":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-204","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The call itself is not valid, such as an instance not of its types, or `updateInstance` outside an instance's management","locale":"en"},"5772":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-205","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`forbidden`","locale":"en"},"5773":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-206","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"Only for `state()`: the backend refused (`PERMISSION_DENIED`)","locale":"en"},"5774":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-207","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"`failed`","locale":"en"},"5775":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-208","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The backend answered with an error; for `updateInstance`, the user declined, another update is waiting for an answer, or the application refused it (with its reason)","locale":"en"},"5776":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-209","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"When the backend sends the `ui.frame.emit` notification (`frame`, `event`, `payload`), every open frame of that extension with the id `frame` hands `payload` to its listeners of `event`; no other extension's frame hears it. It is a notification only: sent as a request, it is answered `METHOD_NOT_FOUND`. Supply the optional `instanceId` to reach only frames for that instance. In Rust use `emit_frame_for(Some(id), frame, event, payload)`; in Python pass `instance_id=id` to `emit_frame`.","locale":"en"},"5777":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-210","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"The client also:","locale":"en"},"5778":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-211","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"reports the height of the root element (`<html>`) with a `ResizeObserver`; the frame follows it within 96 to 4096 pixels (240 until it is ready), so a page does not size its root to the frame (a page in the `pages` slot ignores it and takes the whole area);","locale":"en"},"5779":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-212","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"moves focus out of the frame when Escape is pressed in the page and the page did not prevent it;","locale":"en"},"5780":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-213","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-frame-client","content":"answers the application's pings; a frame that answers none for 12 s shows **Unavailable**, and **Reload** recreates it.","locale":"en"},"5781":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-214","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"The application also serves its own look to every frame: `__hanafubuki/ui.css` beside the frame client, and the fonts it loads under `__hanafubuki/fonts/`. Link it by a relative URL, as above. It is generated from the application's stylesheets, so a page that links it gets the application's buttons, fields, cards, lists, tabs, messages, progress bars, scrollbars, and typeface, in both themes, following the user's accent. It sets the body's text and colour but nothing of the page's height, so the frame still follows the page's content.","locale":"en"},"5782":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-215","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Its classes are **class API 1**: a later version may add classes, and renaming or removing one is a new version.","locale":"en"},"5783":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-216","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"5784":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-217","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Classes","locale":"en"},"5785":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-218","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Buttons","locale":"en"},"5786":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-219","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"`btn` (default), `btn-primary` (at most one per view), `btn-subtle`, `btn-danger` (only to confirm something destructive); sizes `btn-sm` (24px), default (32px), `btn-lg` (40px); `btn-icon` for a square icon button. Unavailable: `disabled`, or `aria-disabled=\"true\"` to stay focusable","locale":"en"},"5787":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-220","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Fields","locale":"en"},"5788":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-221","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"`text-input` (on an `<input>`, a `<textarea>`, or a box wrapping one), `form-grid` (`span-all` for a full row), `field-help`, `field-error`, `panel-actions` (a row of buttons for a form), `checkbox` (on `<input type=\"checkbox\">`) in a `check-row` beside its words","locale":"en"},"5789":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-222","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Surfaces","locale":"en"},"5790":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-223","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"`surface-card`, `surface-well`, `surface-floating`, `surface-layer`","locale":"en"},"5791":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-224","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Lists and navigation","locale":"en"},"5792":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-225","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"`card-list` of `card-row`s, each with an optional `card-row__icon`, `card-row__text` (`card-row__title`, `card-row__description`), and `card-row__control`; `menu-item` (`is-active`, `is-danger`); `tabs` of `tab` buttons, the selected one being the one whose `aria-selected` (a tab list) or `aria-checked` (a radio group) is `true`","locale":"en"},"5793":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-226","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Messages and progress","locale":"en"},"5794":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-227","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"`info-bar` with `data-severity` `error`, `warning`, `success`, or none for information, holding `info-bar__icon` (a 20px glyph of your own), `info-bar__text` (`info-bar__title`, `info-bar__message`), `info-bar__action`, and `info-bar__dismiss`; `progress-bar` (`role=\"progressbar\"`) holding `progress-bar__fill` whose `width` is the percentage, with `data-size=\"lg\"`, `data-tone` (`success`, `warning`, `danger`, `muted`), `indeterminate`, and `stepped`","locale":"en"},"5795":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-228","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"Helpers","locale":"en"},"5796":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-229","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"`focus-inset`, `spin`, `pulse`, `text-secondary`, `mono`","locale":"en"},"5797":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-230","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-ui-kit","content":"The kit has no script. A menu, a dropdown, a tooltip, or a dialog cannot leave the frame; the application's own are in the component bundle below.","locale":"en"},"5798":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-231","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"The application also serves its own Vue components to every frame, built from the same sources as the application itself, so they always match the version they run in:","locale":"en"},"5799":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-232","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`__hanafubuki/vue.js`: Vue's runtime. It has no template compiler and the frame's policy allows no `eval`, so render with `h()`, or ship templates your own build compiled.","locale":"en"},"5800":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-233","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`__hanafubuki/ui.js`: the components. It imports only `./vue.js`, so import Vue from `../__hanafubuki/vue.js` too and the page has one Vue.","locale":"en"},"5801":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-234","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`__hanafubuki/ui-components.css`: their own styles; link it after `ui.css`.","locale":"en"},"5802":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-235","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Install `frameUi(frame)` on each Vue app, with the frame client's module: it gives the components the application's language (following each change) and Browse through the application's folder dialog. `useUiStrings().t(key)` gives your page the same strings. `frameUi(frame, { teleportTo, openLink })` takes two options: where menus and tooltips are placed (`body` by default), and what a click on a `MarkdownDocument`'s link does with its address.","locale":"en"},"5803":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-236","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"The components, their props, events, and slots are listed on Interface Reference; their typings are `sdk/ui/ui.d.ts`, in the frame typings download. It is generated from the bundle's sources and covers every component's props, events and slots, `frameUi`, and the motion helpers. They are **UI API 1** (`UI_API_VERSION`): a later version may add components and optional props, and removing or renaming one is a new version. Raise `engines.hanafubuki` to the application version that added what you use.","locale":"en"},"5804":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-237","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"In a frame they behave as in the application, inside the frame. A `PathInput` picks folders only (a `kind: \"file\"` field opens nothing). A menu closes on a press outside it (in the page or in the application), Escape, Tab, a scroll around its trigger, and a resize of the frame: in a Settings section the frame follows your page's height, so keep that height steady while a menu may be open (a growing log belongs in a box of fixed height). A tooltip hides, and the tabs' overflow menu closes, on any scroll in the frame.","locale":"en"},"5805":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-238","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"The bundle holds every shared component of the application that can run in a frame:","locale":"en"},"5806":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-239","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"5807":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-240","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Components","locale":"en"},"5808":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-241","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Inputs","locale":"en"},"5809":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-242","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`BaseInput`, `BaseTextarea`, `BaseDropdown`, `BaseSwitch`, `BaseSlider`, `BaseSelectableList`, `ChoiceCard`, `RadioMarker`, `PathInput`, `BaseColorPicker`, `BaseColorPickerPopover`, `TokenListInput`","locale":"en"},"5810":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-243","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Forms","locale":"en"},"5811":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-244","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`FormField`, `FormSection`, `FormPage`, `SchemaFormFields`, `SchemaFieldControl`","locale":"en"},"5812":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-245","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Settings rows","locale":"en"},"5813":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-246","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`SettingsGroup`, `SettingsRow`, `SettingsSwitch`","locale":"en"},"5814":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-247","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Structure","locale":"en"},"5815":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-248","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`PanelHeader`, `CardHeader`, `DetailSummary`, `BaseTabs`, `BaseCollapsible`, `NavList`, `ToolbarSlot`","locale":"en"},"5816":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-249","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Menus and tooltips","locale":"en"},"5817":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-250","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`ContextMenu`, `Tooltip`, `TooltipBubble`, `InfoTooltip`, `NativeTooltipHost`","locale":"en"},"5818":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-251","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Status and feedback","locale":"en"},"5819":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-252","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`InfoBar`, `InfoBarDetails`, `StatusBadge`, `ProgressBar`, `CornerStatusStack`, `RemovableTokenGroups`, `UpdateDot`, `UpdateHint`, `IconSwap`","locale":"en"},"5820":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-253","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Loading","locale":"en"},"5821":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-254","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`AsyncRegion`, `LoadingState`, `EmptyState`, `Skeleton`, `LoadMoreSentinel`, `RefreshButton`","locale":"en"},"5822":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-255","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Text","locale":"en"},"5823":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-256","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"`MarkdownDocument`","locale":"en"},"5824":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-257","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"The Settings rows, schema form, `NavList`, `ContextMenu`, `CornerStatusStack`, `AsyncRegion`, and `MarkdownDocument` require application 0.3.35. Version 0.3.36 also includes `TokenListInput` for editing lists of strings and `DetailSummary` for a detail page's summary.","locale":"en"},"5825":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-258","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**A Settings section that looks like the application's** is a `SettingsGroup` of `SettingsRow`s, each with its control (`SettingsSwitch` for a boolean). A row stacks its control under its text when a container named `panel` is narrower than 480px: declare `container: panel / inline-size` on what holds the rows. `PanelHeader` and `BaseTabs` narrow the same way inside any container you declare.","locale":"en"},"5826":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-259","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**Schema forms.** `SchemaFormFields` lays out the same fields a schema panel declares, as `FormField`s inside your `.form-grid`, and evaluates `visibleWhen` and `disabledWhen`. Write texts as `{ kind: \"literal\", text: { en, zh } }`: a `{ kind: \"key\" }` text only finds the application's `common` messages. Your backend validates the values. A `path` field picks folders only.","locale":"en"},"5827":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-260","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**Links.** A click on a `MarkdownDocument`'s link never navigates the frame and opens nothing by itself: pass `openLink` to `frameUi` to handle the address (http, https, or mailto). For HTTP(S) links, call the frame client's `openExternal(url)` to open the system browser. HTML in the Markdown source is shown as text. The Copy button on a code block writes the clipboard, which a sandboxed frame may be refused; the button then stays as it is. An image in the source does not load: the frame's policy only loads images from your package.","locale":"en"},"5828":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-261","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**`CornerStatusStack`** docks to the bottom-end corner of its nearest positioned ancestor: give the region it reports for `position: relative`.","locale":"en"},"5829":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-262","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**`NativeTooltipHost`** is mounted once per page; from then on every `title` attribute in it is drawn as the application's tooltip.","locale":"en"},"5830":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-263","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**`ContextMenu` and `BaseColorPickerPopover`** stay mounted and take `open`; you place the menu with `x` and `y` (a `contextmenu` event's `clientX` and `clientY`).","locale":"en"},"5831":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-264","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"**Icons.** The bundle exports no icons. An `icon` prop takes a component of your own that renders an `<svg>` and accepts `size`.","locale":"en"},"5832":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-265","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#the-component-bundle","content":"Dialogs are not in the bundle: the application's belong to its window. Ask inside your page, or use a host request that confirms in the application (`updateInstance`).","locale":"en"},"5833":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-266","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Once the page is ready, and on every change of the application's theme or language, the client sets `data-theme` (`light` or `dark`), `color-scheme`, `lang`, and these CSS variables on the page's root, plus every variable the application sets at run time (the whole accent ramp, such as `--accent-indicator` and `--accent-text-hover`, the surface opacity, and the scrollbar's arrows). A page that links the kit has every token from the start; one that does not has only these:","locale":"en"},"5834":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-267","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"5835":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-268","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Variables","locale":"en"},"5836":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-269","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Text","locale":"en"},"5837":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-270","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`, `--text-tertiary`, `--text-disabled`, `--text-on-accent`","locale":"en"},"5838":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-271","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Accent","locale":"en"},"5839":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-272","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--accent-fill`, `--accent-fill-hover`, `--accent-fill-pressed`, `--accent-text`","locale":"en"},"5840":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-273","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Fill","locale":"en"},"5841":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-274","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--fill-card`, `--fill-layer`, `--fill-control`, `--fill-control-hover`, `--fill-control-pressed`, `--fill-subtle-hover`, `--fill-well`","locale":"en"},"5842":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-275","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Stroke","locale":"en"},"5843":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-276","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--stroke-card`, `--stroke-control`, `--stroke-divider`, `--focus-stroke-outer`","locale":"en"},"5844":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-277","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Status","locale":"en"},"5845":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-278","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--danger`, `--success`, `--warning`, `--info`","locale":"en"},"5846":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-279","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Radius","locale":"en"},"5847":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-280","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--radius-small`, `--radius-control`, `--radius-overlay`","locale":"en"},"5848":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-281","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Type","locale":"en"},"5849":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-282","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--font-text`, `--font-mono`, `--font-size-caption`, `--font-size-body`, `--font-size-subtitle`, `--font-size-title`, `--line-height-caption`, `--line-height-body`, `--line-height-subtitle`, `--line-height-title`, `--weight-regular`, `--weight-semibold`","locale":"en"},"5850":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-283","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Spacing","locale":"en"},"5851":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-284","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--space-1`, `--space-2`, `--space-3`, `--space-4`, `--space-5`, `--space-6`, `--space-8`","locale":"en"},"5852":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-285","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Control heights","locale":"en"},"5853":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-286","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"`--control-height-sm`, `--control-height-md`","locale":"en"},"5854":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-287","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-variables","content":"Without the kit the variables are not set before `ready()`, so give fallbacks in styles, such as `var(--space-3, 12px)`.","locale":"en"},"5855":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-288","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"A frame is untrusted content. It runs in an iframe with `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` (no `allow-same-origin`), so its origin is the opaque `null`. Every response carries this content security policy:","locale":"en"},"5856":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-289","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"where `<self>` is the extension's own address (`hfext://<extension id>`, or `http://hfext.localhost/<extension id>/` on Windows). So a frame has:","locale":"en"},"5857":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-290","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"**No network**: `connect-src 'none'` blocks `fetch`, XHR, and WebSockets; ask the backend for data through `call`.","locale":"en"},"5858":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-291","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"**No inline script**: scripts are files of the package; inline styles are allowed.","locale":"en"},"5859":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-292","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"**Only its own package's resources**: images may also be `data:` and `blob:`.","locale":"en"},"5860":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-293","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"**No popups or dialogs**: the sandbox opens no new windows and allows no `alert`, `confirm`, or `prompt`, and no form submission. The folder dialog is the application's, through `pickDirectory`.","locale":"en"},"5861":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-294","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"**No application interface**: the frame has no Tauri script or invoke key and reaches no command of the application; it speaks only to its host component through the frame client.","locale":"en"},"5862":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-295","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#security-limits","content":"A frame that throws, never becomes ready, stops answering, or whose calls hang affects only itself; other frames and panels carry on. But in WebKitGTK and WKWebView a frame runs in the window's own process, so a page that blocks its main thread for long freezes the whole window.","locale":"en"},"5863":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-296","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#read-and-save-this-extensions-settings","content":"The frame client can read and update its own declared settings even when the extension has no backend:","locale":"en"},"5864":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-297","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#read-and-save-this-extensions-settings","content":"On a fresh install, `getSettings()` may return `{ values: {} }` even for fields with defaults. A successful patch returns the validated values, which can include defaults applied by the form. Sending `null` resets a field to its declared default if it has one. Unknown setting keys or invalid values reject the patch without a partial write. The host applies the same validation and persistence as the application's settings page and notifies the extension's subscribed backend after saving. The frame's mounted owner determines whose settings are used: no extension id is sent. Invalid message shapes receive `FrameError` with `kind: \"invalid\"`; host failures reject with their reason. The client has no invoke key or arbitrary Tauri command access. Do not log settings values, since declared secret fields may be present.","locale":"en"},"5865":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-298","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#open-host-settings-and-external-links","content":"`openSettings` accepts a registered Settings section ID. Use a built-in ID such as `network`, `extension:<extension id>` for an extension's settings form, or `extension:<extension id>:<panel or frame id>` for a contribution in `settings.sections`. The example opens Greeter's greetings panel while Greeter is enabled. An unknown section returns `invalid`. `openExternal` opens an HTTP(S) URL in the system browser and reports the reason if opening it fails. Both calls work in data-only extensions and return promises that resolve with `undefined` or reject with a `FrameError`.","locale":"en"},"5866":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-299","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-tokens-and-local-motion","content":"The complete dictionary retains selectors, light overrides, derived expressions, reduced-motion conditions and runtime writers. Shared stylesheet declarations establish the base; light selectors and local rules override where they match, while host theme messages apply projected values inline. Inspect each entry's actual conditions rather than treating all tokens as interchangeable global defaults. Public component-local properties only affect their documented component; implementation variables are not extension settings.","locale":"en"},"5867":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-300","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-tokens-and-local-motion","content":"Use frame-safe motion helpers from `__hanafubuki/ui.js`, with Vue from `__hanafubuki/vue.js`. Read timing roles from CSS, let helpers honor reduced motion, and release animations, pinned sizes and observers when their Vue scope ends. `useDeferredPresence` retains content through an exit but does not animate it: call `closed` when the owning transition finishes. The runnable examples demonstrate size/directional swaps, FLIP/indicators and deferred expansion in the existing linked gallery. No backend or additional permission is needed; this grants no native window or application-wide theme authority.","locale":"en"},"5868":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-301","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#theme-tokens-and-local-motion","content":"The dictionary records authored declarations and their conditions; only the running browser can compute the final value after inheritance and inline overrides. The gallery's theme inspector deliberately reads that live value. If you override a motion duration inline, it can outrank a stylesheet's reduced-motion declaration. Script-driven custom animations must check `prefersReducedMotion()` or use the shared helpers that do so; a timing number alone does not encode the user's preference. Avoid overriding shared timing roles merely to customize one transition.","locale":"en"},"5869":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-302","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#text-and-languages","content":"The manifest's `locales` names each language's file with `{locale}`: `locales/{locale}.json` means `locales/en.json` and `locales/zh.json`. A language code is of `A-Z`, `a-z`, `0-9`, `_`, `-`. Each file is a JSON object and may nest:","locale":"en"},"5870":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-303","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#text-and-languages","content":"Instance type descriptors, the settings form, and panels refer to this text as `ext.<extension id>.<key>`, a `.` in the key going one level down, such as `ext.com.example.greeter.type.name`. The application merges the text under `ext['<extension id>']`. A key of the application or of another extension is an error at install.","locale":"en"},"5871":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-304","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#text-and-languages","content":"A button for an operation of a backend-provided type's own takes its label from `ext.<extension id>.operations.<operation>`, or shows the operation's name without one.","locale":"en"},"5872":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui-305","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev-ui#text-and-languages","content":"The extension's `name`, `description`, and a frame's `title` are written in the manifest, as plain text or a table by language; they cannot refer to a text key.","locale":"en"},"5873":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"page","content":"Extension Development Overview","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Extension Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev","locale":"en"},"5874":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-0","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev","content":"What an extension can contribute, data-only versus backend extensions, the package layout, every key of hanafubuki-extension.toml, and what is checked at install.","locale":"en"},"5875":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-1","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"What an extension can contribute","locale":"en"},"5876":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-2","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#data-only-and-backend-extensions","content":"Data-only and backend extensions","locale":"en"},"5877":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-3","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#package-layout","content":"Package layout","locale":"en"},"5878":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-4","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#a-manifest","content":"A manifest","locale":"en"},"5879":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-5","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#manifest-keys","content":"Manifest keys","locale":"en"},"5880":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-6","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Identity","locale":"en"},"5881":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-7","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"`[engines]`","locale":"en"},"5882":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-8","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#dependencies","content":"`[dependencies]`","locale":"en"},"