e":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Backends","locale":"en"},"5920":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-46","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Agent content","locale":"en"},"5921":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-47","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Skills and MCP servers made available to the built-in Agent","locale":"en"},"5922":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-48","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Agent contributions","locale":"en"},"5923":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-49","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Management MCP tools","locale":"en"},"5924":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-50","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Individual backend methods published on the application's `hanafubuki` server for the Agent and external clients","locale":"en"},"5925":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-51","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"Publishing tools","locale":"en"},"5926":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-52","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-an-extension-can-contribute","content":"The backend runs in a separate process. A frame runs in a sandboxed iframe and uses the frame client to read extension settings, call its own backend, or ask the host to open an external link.","locale":"en"},"5927":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-53","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#data-only-and-backend-extensions","content":"A package can omit `[backend]` when its contributions are files the host reads. For example, a data-only preset can supply defaults for an existing instance type. Instance types can still declare commands that run during installation or launch, and the Agent can start a declared stdio MCP server.","locale":"en"},"5928":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-54","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#data-only-and-backend-extensions","content":"An extension **with a backend** declares a program in `[backend]`: one executable per operating system, or a script run on the application's managed Python. The backend runs while the extension is on. It can supply data and actions to panels and frames, call the application's host API, and plan the install steps and launch commands of `provider = \"backend\"` instance types.","locale":"en"},"5929":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-55","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#package-layout","content":"A package is a directory with `hanafubuki-extension.toml` at its root. In an archive, the files may sit at the archive's root or inside one wrapping directory. Where everything else goes is up to the manifest; a common layout:","locale":"en"},"5930":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-56","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#package-layout","content":"Every path in the manifest is relative to the package root, separated by `/`, and contains no `..`, no backslash, and no root. Symbolic links in a package are never followed.","locale":"en"},"5931":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-57","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#package-layout","content":"A copied installation puts each version in `extensions/<id>/<version>/` under the application's data directory. A development link reads the selected source directory in place. Both store persistent data in `extensions/<id>/data/` and settings in `extensions/<id>/settings.json`. These survive updates and reloads.","locale":"en"},"5932":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-58","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#manifest-keys","content":"The manifest decodes tolerantly: a key this version does not know is ignored, so a manifest written for a newer application still reads as long as it uses nothing new. What each key holds is checked strictly; a problem refuses the install and is reported at its key (such as `dependencies.\"com.example.base\"`) or at a line and column.","locale":"en"},"5933":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-59","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"5934":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-60","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Required","locale":"en"},"5935":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-61","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5936":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-62","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`schema`","locale":"en"},"5937":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-63","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"No","locale":"en"},"5938":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-64","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"The manifest schema; `1` when absent, and only `1` is accepted","locale":"en"},"5939":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-65","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`id`","locale":"en"},"5940":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-66","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"5941":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-67","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"A reverse-DNS id: two or more labels of `a-z`, `0-9`, and `-`, joined by `.`, at most 128 bytes. It names the extension's store directory, the namespace of its instance types, and the prefix of its text keys","locale":"en"},"5942":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-68","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`name`","locale":"en"},"5943":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-69","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"5944":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-70","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"The display name: plain text (the same in every language), or a table by language, `{ en = \"…\", zh = \"…\" }`","locale":"en"},"5945":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-71","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`version`","locale":"en"},"5946":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-72","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"5947":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-73","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"A semantic version, such as `1.2.0`","locale":"en"},"5948":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-74","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`publisher`","locale":"en"},"5949":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-75","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"No","locale":"en"},"5950":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-76","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"The publisher's name, plain text","locale":"en"},"5951":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-77","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`license`","locale":"en"},"5952":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-78","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"No","locale":"en"},"5953":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-79","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"The license, plain text","locale":"en"},"5954":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-80","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"`description`","locale":"en"},"5955":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-81","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"No","locale":"en"},"5956":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-82","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"A description, written like `name`","locale":"en"},"5957":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-83","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#identity","content":"Text by language falls back to English when the current language is missing, and to the first language given when there is no English.","locale":"en"},"5958":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-84","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"5959":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-85","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5960":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-86","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"`hanafubuki`","locale":"en"},"5961":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-87","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"The application versions it runs on, a semver range (such as `\">=0.3, <0.5\"`); any version without one","locale":"en"},"5962":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-88","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"`api`","locale":"en"},"5963":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-89","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"The host API version it speaks; it must be `1`","locale":"en"},"5964":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-90","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#engines","content":"An extension without `engines.api` still installs, but shows **Can't run** because it does not say\nwhich host API it speaks.","locale":"en"},"5965":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-91","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#dependencies","content":"Each key is the id of an extension it depends on, each value a semver range: `\"com.example.common\" = \"^1.1\"`. An extension cannot depend on itself. It cannot run when a dependency is not installed, is of another version, is turned off or cannot run itself, or when the dependencies form a cycle. Turned-on extensions start in dependency order, each after its dependencies.","locale":"en"},"5966":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-92","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"Exactly one of `command` and `python`.","locale":"en"},"5967":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-93","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"5968":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-94","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"5969":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-95","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"`command`","locale":"en"},"5970":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-96","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"A table of program paths by operating system: `linux`, `macos`, `windows` (any other key is ignored); at least one","locale":"en"},"5971":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-97","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"`python`","locale":"en"},"5972":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-98","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"A script run on the application's managed Python","locale":"en"},"5973":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-99","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"`requirements`","locale":"en"},"5974":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-100","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"Only with `python`: a pip requirements file, installed into its data directory when it is turned on","locale":"en"},"5975":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-101","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"`sdWebuiAllInOne`","locale":"en"},"5976":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-102","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#backend","content":"Only with `python`: `true` puts the application's `sd_webui_all_in_one` on its import path (see Python backends)","locale":"en"},"5977":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-10