/docs/extension-dev#what-makes-a-package-cant-run","content":"These do not stop the install, but the extension is listed as **Can't run** with the reason:","locale":"en"},"6048":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-174","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-makes-a-package-cant-run","content":"a `command` backend with no program for this operating system;","locale":"en"},"6049":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-175","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-makes-a-package-cant-run","content":"an `engines.api` other than `1`, or none;","locale":"en"},"6050":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-176","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-makes-a-package-cant-run","content":"an `engines.hanafubuki` range the application's version does not meet.","locale":"en"},"6051":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-177","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#what-makes-a-package-cant-run","content":"Once turned on, a dependency that is missing, of another version, turned off, or unable to run, and a dependency cycle, also keep it from running.","locale":"en"},"6052":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-178","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"The application checks each installed extension that names an `[update] url` once a day (and whenever the user clicks **Check for Updates**). It reads the `latest.json` there, and offers an update when its newest entry for the user's system is above the installed version. It never installs one by itself: the user clicks **Update** (or **Update to …**) on the card, which checks again, and confirms, as for any update.","locale":"en"},"6053":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-179","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`latest.json` is a list of entries, or a single entry:","locale":"en"},"6054":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-180","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"6055":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-181","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"6056":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-182","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`version`","locale":"en"},"6057":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-183","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"The package's semantic version, the same as its manifest's","locale":"en"},"6058":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-184","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`download_url`","locale":"en"},"6059":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-185","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"The package archive (`.zip`, `.tar`, `.tar.gz`, `.tar.xz`, or `.tar.bz2`), over `http` or `https`","locale":"en"},"6060":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-186","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`sha256`","locale":"en"},"6061":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-187","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"Optional: the archive's SHA-256. When given, a download with other bytes is refused","locale":"en"},"6062":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-188","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`platform`","locale":"en"},"6063":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-189","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`windows`, `linux`, `macos`, or `any`","locale":"en"},"6064":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-190","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`architecture`","locale":"en"},"6065":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-191","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"`x86_64`, `aarch64`, or `any`","locale":"en"},"6066":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-192","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"Both platform and architecture must match the host or be `any`. Among compatible entries, the highest version wins. For the same version, each exact match counts once: a `linux`/`x86_64` entry takes precedence over `linux`/`any`, which takes precedence over `any`/`any` on Linux x86-64. For a portable archive, publish one entry with both fields set to `any`.","locale":"en"},"6067":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-193","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"An entry that cannot be read (a missing field, a version that is not semantic, a bad URL or digest) is skipped and the others are used; the card's tooltip lists what was skipped. A file that is not JSON, or has no usable entry, shows **Check failed** with the reason.","locale":"en"},"6068":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-194","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#publishing-updates","content":"Unknown fields are ignored. The host reads at most 1 MiB of feed metadata, so list the packages you currently offer.","locale":"en"},"6069":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-195","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#on-github-releases","content":"A GitHub repository can publish everything as release assets. GitHub serves the newest release's asset named `latest.json` at a fixed address, so the manifest names it once:","locale":"en"},"6070":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-196","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#on-github-releases","content":"For each release:","locale":"en"},"6071":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-197","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#on-github-releases","content":"Compute each archive's SHA-256 (`sha256sum llama-0.3.0.zip` on Linux, `shasum -a 256` on macOS,\n`Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256` in PowerShell).","locale":"en"},"6072":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-198","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#on-github-releases","content":"Write `latest.json` with one entry per archive, each `download_url` the archive's release asset\naddress: `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/releases/download/<tag>/<file>`.","locale":"en"},"6073":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-199","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#on-github-releases","content":"The previous release's `latest.json` stays with it; only the latest release's is read. Draft and pre-releases are not \"latest\", so publishing one does not offer it.","locale":"en"},"6074":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-200","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"The application's **Marketplace** lists the extensions in the extension registry, licyk/hanafubuki-extension: one file, `extensions.json`. To be listed, add an entry for your extension there by pull request; the repository's README describes the checks a pull request must pass.","locale":"en"},"6075":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-201","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"6076":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-202","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Required","locale":"en"},"6077":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-203","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"6078":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-204","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`id`","locale":"en"},"6079":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-205","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"6080":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-206","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"The manifest's `id`. A package installed from the entry must have it, or the install is refused","locale":"en"},"6081":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-207","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`name`","locale":"en"},"6082":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-208","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"6083":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-209","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Text, or an object of language to text (`{ \"en\": \"…\", \"zh\": \"…\" }`), as in a manifest","locale":"en"},"6084":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-210","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`author`","locale":"en"},"6085":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-211","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"6086":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-212","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Text","locale":"en"},"6087":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-213","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`reference`","locale":"en"},"6088":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-214","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"6089":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-215","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"The source repository's address, `http` or `https`","locale":"en"},"6090":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-216","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`description`","locale":"en"},"6091":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-217","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"No","locale":"en"},"6092":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-218","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"Text, or an object of language to text","locale":"en"},"6093":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-219","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`download_url`","locale":"en"},"6094":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-220","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"No","locale":"en"},"6095":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-221","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"An installable archive (`.zip`, `.tar`, `.tar.gz`, `.tar.xz`, or `.tar.bz2`), over `http` or `https`","locale":"en"},"6096":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-222","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"`update_url`","locale":"en"},"6097":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-223","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"No","locale":"en"},"6098":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-224","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"The extension's `latest.json` (see Publishing updates), usually the same address as its `[update] url`","locale":"en"},"6099":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-225","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"**Track the latest release.** Set `update_url` to the latest release's `latest.json`. You can omit `download_url` from the registry entry. The Marketplace downloads the highest version for the user's platform and architecture from the feed and checks its `sha256` when provided. It ignores any old archive URL in the registry entry and reports an error if the feed fails or has no compatible package.","locale":"en"},"6100":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-226","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"**Pin a version or list the source.** Set only `download_url` to install directly from that archive. Omit both URLs to list just the source link.","locale":"en"},"6101":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-227","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"**Registry format.** The published document uses `schema: 1`. The app reads the `extensions` array and ignores other top-level fields, including `schema`. It skips malformed entries and keeps the first accepted entry for each id.","locale":"en"},"6102":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-228","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#listing-in-the-registry","content":"**The registry does not update an installed extension**: its updates come from its own manifest's `[update] url`.","locale":"en"},"6103":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-229","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Instance Types\" href=\"/docs/extension-dev-instance-types\" description=\"Write descriptors: parameters, steps, placeholders, and server roles.\" />","locale":"en"},"6104":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-230","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Backends\" href=\"/docs/extension-dev-backends\" description=\"The backend process, the protocol, the host API, and callbacks.\" />","locale":"en"},"6105":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-231","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"SDKs\" href=\"/docs/extension-dev-sdks\" description=\"Write a backend in Rust or Python.\" />","locale":"en"},"6106":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-232","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Interface\" href=\"/docs/extension-dev-ui\" description=\"The settings form, panels, frames, and text.\" />","locale":"en"},"6107":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-233","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Interface Reference\" href=\"/docs/extension-dev-reference\" description=\"Every method, class, panel block, and manifest key, generated from the application's exports.\" />","locale":"en"},"6108":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-234","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Testing and Packaging\" href=\"/docs/extension-dev-testing\" description=\"Build, test, and package an extension, using the sample as the worked example.\" />","locale":"en"},"6109":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-235","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#agent-contributions","content":"An extension can declare Skills and MCP servers under `contributes.agent`. Installation review displays these declarations and their requested permissions. They form an application-managed linked package, not arbitrary Agent configuration or dynamically loaded Rust plugins.","locale":"en"},"6110":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-236","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#agent-contributions","content":"This is a manifest fragment: supply the usual extension identity and engine fields. A Skill path names a package directory containing `SKILL.md`. A stdio command is either `{kind=\"package\", path=\"bin/server\"}` inside the extension package or `{kind=\"runtime\", tool=\"python\"}` (also `git` or `micromamba`). Stdio needs `processes = true`; HTTP needs the fixed URL's host in `network`. Arguments, environment values and HTTP header values are strings or `{setting=\"key\"}` references to this extension's declared string-valued settings. For the example, declare `authorization` in `schemas/settings.json`, for example as a `secret` field, and let the user enter the complete header value such as `Bearer …`. No host token is inserted; permission and reference validation belongs to Rust.","locale":"en"},"6111":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-237","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#agent-contributions","content":"The stdio server starts in the extension's package root, so `server.py` in the example lives beside the manifest. For a setting reference, the host writes the current string value into the generated package's local `.mcp.json`, including the full value of a secret header. If a referenced setting has no string value, the host disables the managed Agent package and clears its previous MCP configuration. Supplying the missing value regenerates the package. Other extension features remain available.","locale":"en"},"6112":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-238","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#agent-contributions","content":"Skill and server ids use ASCII letters, digits, dots, underscores and hyphens and must be unique within their contribution kind. Exclude `.` and `..`, and start Skill ids with a character other than a dot. The host generates a linked package under the extension's managed `agent-package` directory. Its package id is `hanafubuki-extension-<extension-id>@hanafubuki-extensions` and MCP server ids are `hanafubuki-extension-<extension-id>-<local-id>`. The complete MCP server id must fit in 128 bytes. Conflicts with a package owned by the user are refused. The Agent retains its normal tool approval and exposure rules.","locale":"en"},"6113":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-239","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#agent-contributions","content":"Enabling the extension publishes its content; stopping, disabling or faulting withdraws it. Updates and successful referenced-setting changes regenerate content and reload the linked package. An independently user-disabled package stays disabled: the host restores only a disable it performed itself. Uninstall removes the managed Agent package without deleting user data. If the Agent is unavailable, other extension capabilities continue; the next ready transition reconciles current extension owners. Ordinary user packages are not touched. The generated manifest reference is the authority for nested field shapes.","locale":"en"},"6114":{"id":"/en/docs/extension-dev-240","page_id":"/en/docs/extension-dev","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/extension-dev#agent-contributions","content":"For field defaults, conditional requirements and validation stages, use the generated configuration reference. A JSON Schema `null` describes the JSON representation or omission behavior; TOML has no `null` literal. Do not copy it as `field = null`. A schema default and a domain effective default are shown separately; the website does not infer runtime values from nullable fields.","locale":"en"},"6115":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","type":"page","content":"Home and windows","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Workspace"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/home-workspace","locale":"en"},"6116":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-0","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace","content":"Open workspaces from instance cards, find tools in the title bar, and move panels to a second screen.","locale":"en"},"6117":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-1","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Find an instance on Home","locale":"en"},"6118":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-2","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#title-bar-and-separate-windows","content":"Title bar and separate windows","locale":"en"},"6119":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-3","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Search for part of an instance name, type ID, or installation path. For example, `comfyui` matches instances of type `builtin:comfyui`. The search ignores case. Press `Tab` to focus the grid, then use the arrow keys to move between cards. `Home` and `End` move to the first and last cards. Press `Enter` or Space to open the selected card.","locale":"en"},"6120":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-4","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"What you want to do","locale":"en"},"6121":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-5","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Where to go","locale":"en"},"6122":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-6","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Run an instance","locale":"en"},"6123":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-7","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Select a ready instance card. If it is already starting or running, its existing workspace opens.","locale":"en"},"6124":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-8","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Inspect configuration","locale":"en"},"6125":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-9","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Right-click the card or open **More actions** and choose **Manage…**. You can also select **Instance Management** in the title bar and pick an instance from the list.","locale":"en"},"6126":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-10","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Continue an unfinished installation","locale":"en"},"6127":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-11","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Open the card to see progress, or choose **Start installation** or **Retry installation** from its menu when available. Installation progress and troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"6128":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-12","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Check one instance for updates","locale":"en"},"6129":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-13","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Select **Check for updates** on a ready instance card. The card shows progress and available updates. Home displays a notice if the type does not support update checks. Versions","locale":"en"},"6130":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-14","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Add an existing WebUI","locale":"en"},"6131":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-15","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"Drop its folder on Home, or select **Add instance** to import or scan. On first use you may also be offered a system scan. Scan the system","locale":"en"},"6132":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-16","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#find-an-instance-on-home","content":"If a card says its type is unavailable, the instance record is still there. Check the extension providing its type under Extensions, or open the card's management menu to inspect the record. The **Hanafubuki documentation** card opens the guide in your system browser.","locale":"en"},"6133":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-17","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#title-bar-and-separate-windows","content":"Use Instance Management to maintain an instance. Use WebUI Tabs to open its running page or switch between instances.","locale":"en"},"6134":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-18","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#title-bar-and-separate-windows","content":"Task Center shows background activities and WebUI downloads. Agent opens your conversations. Settings controls the application and its runtime environment.","locale":"en"},"6135":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-19","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#title-bar-and-separate-windows","content":"When an enabled desktop extension provides a page, the **Extension pages** menu appears in the title bar. Choose a page there, then use the back button to return to Home.","locale":"en"},"6136":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-20","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#title-bar-and-separate-windows","content":"**Report an issue** opens the project's issue list in your system browser. To include relevant logs, follow Logs, diagnostics, and reporting issues.","locale":"en"},"6137":{"id":"/en/docs/home-workspace-21","page_id":"/en/docs/home-workspace","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/home-workspace#title-bar-and-separate-windows","content":"Choose **Open in a separate window** in the title bar of Settings, Instance Management, Agent, Task Center, or WebUI Tabs to move that panel to another screen. For example, detach Task Center to watch installation logs while managing an instance in the main window. Selecting the same tool in the main window brings its separate window to the front. Select **Return to the main window** to dock it again.","locale":"en"},"6138":{"id":"/en/docs","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"page","content":"Hanafubuki","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs","locale":"en"},"6139":{"id":"/en/docs-0","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Install, run, and manage local generative AI WebUIs in one place.","locale":"en"},"6140":{"id":"/en/docs-1","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Hanafubuki is a Tauri-based desktop manager for installing, importing, running, and maintaining local generative AI WebUIs. It brings Python, Git, launch arguments, models, extensions, snapshots, and diagnostics together in one place, and includes an Agent that can connect to local tools.","locale":"en"},"6141":{"id":"/en/docs-2","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Built-in types include Stable Diffusion WebUI, ComfyUI, InvokeAI, Fooocus, SD Trainer, Qwen TTS WebUI, RVC Next WebUI, and Mizuoto TTS WebUI. Enabled desktop extensions can add instance types. See Installation methods and Instance Management for the actions available for each type.","locale":"en"},"6142":{"id":"/en/docs-3","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Home and windows\" href=\"/docs/home-workspace\" description=\"Find instances, use card menus, and move tool panels to another screen.\" />","locale":"en"},"6143":{"id":"/en/docs-4","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"First-time setup\" href=\"/docs/quick-start\" description=\"Install the app and launch your first WebUI.\" />","locale":"en"},"6144":{"id":"/en/docs-5","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Install the app\" href=\"/docs/installation\" description=\"Choose an installer or portable package and complete the first launch.\" />","locale":"en"},"6145":{"id":"/en/docs-6","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Use the Agent\" href=\"/docs/agent\" description=\"Configure a model and start a session in the project environment.\" />","locale":"en"},"6146":{"id":"/en/docs-7","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Troubleshooting\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting\" description=\"Diagnose problems using task output, logs, and diagnostic bundles.\" />","locale":"en"},"6147":{"id":"/en/docs-8","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Hanafubuki is still under development and testing. Create snapshots or your own backups of\nimportant instances and configuration regularly.","locale":"en"},"6148":{"id":"/en/docs/installation","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"page","content":"Install Hanafubuki","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation","locale":"en"},"6149":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-0","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Choose an installer or portable package on the download page, then complete the first launch.","locale":"en"},"6150":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-1","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Choose one first","locale":"en"},"6151":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-2","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#download-from-the-website","content":"Download from the website","locale":"en"},"6152":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-3","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Installer formats","locale":"en"},"6153":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-4","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"Install by platform","locale":"en"},"6154":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-5","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"Portable package","locale":"en"},"6155":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-6","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"First launch","locale":"en"},"6156":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-7","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Hanafubuki is available in two forms: an **installer** installs the app into your system, while the **portable package** is a Launcher that runs after extraction. Both are available from the download page, which automatically detects your current system.","locale":"en"},"6157":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-8","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Installer","locale":"en"},"6158":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-9","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Portable package","locale":"en"},"6159":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-10","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"How to use","locale":"en"},"6160":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-11","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Install it, then launch from the desktop or Start menu","locale":"en"},"6161":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-12","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Extract it and run the Launcher directly","locale":"en"},"6162":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-13","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Application files","locale":"en"},"6163":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-14","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Included in the installer","locale":"en"},"6164":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-15","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Downloaded and verified by the Launcher, and repaired if damaged","locale":"en"},"6165":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-16","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Data location","locale":"en"},"6166":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-17","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"The system application-data directory","locale":"en"},"6167":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-18","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"The `.hanafubuki-launcher` directory beside the program","locale":"en"},"6168":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-19","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Updates","locale":"en"},"6169":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-20","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Recommended formats support checking and installing updates in the app","locale":"en"},"6170":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-21","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"See About & Updates","locale":"en"},"6171":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-22","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Best for","locale":"en"},"6172":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-23","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Long-term use on one computer","locale":"en"},"6173":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Removable drives, or multiple independent environments","locale":"en"},"6174":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#choose-one-first","content":"Every link on the download page points to the project's release repositories on ModelScope and\nHugging Face. The page automatically selects the source that responds first. Do not download\ninstallers from third-party mirrors or reposts.","locale":"en"},"6175":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#download-from-the-website","content":"The page has separate Installer and Portable screens. The indicator on the right shows your\ncurrent position, and the version switcher at the top lets you move between them.","locale":"en"},"6176":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#download-from-the-website","content":"Select “Download Now.” The page detects your current system and starts downloading the\ncorresponding file.","locale":"en"},"6177":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#download-from-the-website","content":"For another platform or format, select “Choose Manually” to open the full list, which includes\nfile names and sizes.","locale":"en"},"6178":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#download-from-the-website","content":"Windows is available only for x86_64. macOS and Linux are available for both x86_64 and ARM64. Choose “macOS (Apple Silicon)” for a Mac with Apple silicon.","locale":"en"},"6179":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-30","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Each release includes several formats. If you are unsure, choose the one marked Recommended.","locale":"en"},"6180":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-31","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Platform","locale":"en"},"6181":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-32","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Format","locale":"en"},"6182":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-33","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"6183":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-34","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"6184":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-35","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Installer (`.exe`)","locale":"en"},"6185":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-36","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Recommended. Standard installation workflow with in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6186":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-37","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"6187":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-38","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"MSI package","locale":"en"},"6188":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-39","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Suitable for managed deployment; does not participate in in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6189":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-40","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Windows","locale":"en"},"6190":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-41","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Standalone archive","locale":"en"},"6191":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-42","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Extract and run; does not participate in in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6192":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-43","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"6193":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-44","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Disk image (`.dmg`)","locale":"en"},"6194":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-45","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Recommended. Open it and drag the app to Applications; supports in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6195":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-46","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"macOS","locale":"en"},"6196":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-47","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"App archive (`.app.tar.gz`)","locale":"en"},"6197":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-48","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"A compressed copy of the same `.app`","locale":"en"},"6198":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-49","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"6199":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-50","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"AppImage","locale":"en"},"6200":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-51","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Recommended. Runs as a single file and supports in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6201":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-52","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"6202":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-53","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Debian package (`.deb`)","locale":"en"},"6203":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-54","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Installed through the system package manager; does not participate in in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6204":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-55","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Linux","locale":"en"},"6205":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-56","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"RPM package (`.rpm`)","locale":"en"},"6206":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-57","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Installed through the system package manager; does not participate in in-app updates","locale":"en"},"6207":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-58","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#installer-formats","content":"Formats that do not participate in in-app updates can still check for updates. The app will offer a manual installer for the current platform instead.","locale":"en"},"6208":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-59","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"Download the installer and follow its prompts, then launch Hanafubuki from the desktop or Start menu.","locale":"en"},"6209":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-60","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"If you choose the standalone archive, extract it to a writable directory before running the executable inside.","locale":"en"},"6210":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-61","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"The current Windows package is unsigned. If the installer or standalone build opens a **Windows protected your PC** prompt saying that Microsoft Defender SmartScreen prevented an unrecognized app from starting, first confirm that the file came from this site. Select **More info**, then select **Run anyway**.","locale":"en"},"6211":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-62","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"Open the disk image and drag Hanafubuki to Applications. Extracting the app archive produces the same `.app`; place it in Applications as well.","locale":"en"},"6212":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-63","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"The current macOS package is unsigned. If the first launch says `“Hanafubuki” is damaged and can't be opened. You should move it to the Trash.`, confirm that the package came from this site, then open Terminal and remove the quarantine attribute from the app:","locale":"en"},"6213":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-64","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"Terminal does not display characters while you enter your macOS password. When the command finishes, open Hanafubuki again. For other security prompts, use **System Settings → Privacy & Security** to confirm that you want to open the app.","locale":"en"},"6214":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-65","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"Make the AppImage executable, then run it directly:","locale":"en"},"6215":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-66","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"You can also install the `.deb` or `.rpm` with your system package manager, then launch Hanafubuki from the application menu:","locale":"en"},"6216":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-67","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#install-by-platform","content":"The Windows standalone archive only skips the installation step. Data is still written to the\nsystem application-data directory. If the data must travel with the program, use the portable\nLauncher described below.","locale":"en"},"6217":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-68","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"The portable package uses a standalone Launcher. Beside it, `.hanafubuki-launcher/core/` holds the application, `.hanafubuki-launcher/data/` holds application settings and the default instance directory, and `.hanafubuki-launcher/logs/` holds the Launcher's own logs. Existing WebUIs registered by the first scan stay in their original directories.","locale":"en"},"6218":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-69","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"Download the Launcher archive for your platform and extract it to a writable directory. Do not\nplace it on read-only media or in a system directory.","locale":"en"},"6219":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-70","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"Run the Launcher. On its first launch, it downloads and verifies Hanafubuki according to the\nmanifest, then opens the app automatically.","locale":"en"},"6220":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-71","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"To move the environment, exit the application and copy the Launcher, `.hanafubuki-launcher`, and\nany WebUI directories registered by the first scan. Keep their relative layout.","locale":"en"},"6221":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-72","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"The current Windows portable package is also unsigned. If Microsoft Defender SmartScreen shows\n**Windows protected your PC** when you first run the Launcher, confirm that the archive came from\nthis site, select **More info**, and then select **Run anyway**. The **Run anyway** button appears\nonly after you expand **More info**.","locale":"en"},"6222":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-73","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"The current macOS portable package is also unsigned. After confirming that the archive came from\nthis site, type `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine` followed by a space in Terminal, drag the extracted\n`Hanafubuki Launcher.app` from Finder into the Terminal window, and press Return. The complete\ncommand will look like this:","locale":"en"},"6223":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-74","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"Open the Launcher again when the command finishes. The command must point to the actual `.app`;\ndo not copy the example path literally.","locale":"en"},"6224":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-75","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"The Launcher also handles the following cases:","locale":"en"},"6225":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-76","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"On its first run, the Launcher scans its directory for built-in WebUI layouts. If it finds only the Core, it registers the instance so you can finish installing it in the app. For WebUIs added later, open **Add instance** and use Scan system.","locale":"en"},"6226":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-77","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"At each launch, it resets the artifact cache, default instance installation directory, and embedded WebUI download directory to their defaults inside the portable workspace. Registered instances continue to use their own directories.","locale":"en"},"6227":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-78","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"During online verification it removes files in `core/` that are absent from the manifest and repairs missing or damaged files from the release package. Keep models and personal files in an instance directory or your own data directory.","locale":"en"},"6228":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-79","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"If the release sources are unavailable, the Launcher tries the installed application. First installation or an unusable local copy requires connectivity. If preparation fails, you can open the current Launcher log.","locale":"en"},"6229":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-80","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"It reads the system proxy configuration for its own download requests.","locale":"en"},"6230":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-81","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#portable-package","content":"On Windows, the Launcher requires long-path support and the Visual C++ Runtime. If either is\nmissing, it requests administrator permission once to update the registry or install the runtime.\nIt continues to run as a standard user afterward. Rejecting either request leaves the Launcher on\na retry screen.","locale":"en"},"6231":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-82","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"The app prepares runtime components including Python, Micromamba, and Git. Keep the network connected and wait for preparation to finish.","locale":"en"},"6232":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-83","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"If preparation fails, go to “Settings → Runtime Environment” to retry or change download sources. You can also read Runtime Environment Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"6233":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-84","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"After preparation completes, continue to Quick Start to install or import your first WebUI.","locale":"en"},"6234":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-85","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"<Card title=\"Quick start\" href=\"/docs/quick-start\" description=\"Create and launch your first WebUI instance.\" />","locale":"en"},"6235":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-86","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"<Card title=\"About & Updates\" href=\"/docs/settings-about-updates\" description=\"View the version, check for updates, and install a new release.\" />","locale":"en"},"6236":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-87","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"<Card title=\"Runtime environment\" href=\"/docs/settings-runtime\" description=\"Configure Python, Git, and download sources.\" />","locale":"en"},"6237":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-88","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#first-launch","content":"<Card title=\"Runtime environment troubleshooting\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting-app-runtime\" description=\"Resolve preparation failures or missing components.\" />","locale":"en"},"6238":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"page","content":"Instance Diagnostics","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","locale":"en"},"6239":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","content":"Collect the current instance's environment, tasks, logs, and configuration, then safely export a diagnostic bundle.","locale":"en"},"6240":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#collect-a-diagnostic-bundle","content":"Collect a diagnostic bundle","locale":"en"},"6241":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#reproduce-and-record-the-problem","content":"Reproduce and record the problem","locale":"en"},"6242":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#start-collection","content":"Start collection","locale":"en"},"6243":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#check-completion-status","content":"Check completion status","locale":"en"},"6244":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-and-export","content":"Inspect and export","locale":"en"},"6245":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"What a diagnostic bundle may contain","locale":"en"},"6246":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"Inspect before sharing","locale":"en"},"6247":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","content":"Instance Diagnostics collects environment and runtime information related to a problem into a ZIP archive. It does not repair the instance automatically. Use it after reproducing a launch, extension, hotpatch, or environment problem to provide troubleshooting material.","locale":"en"},"6248":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#reproduce-and-record-the-problem","content":"Record the steps, approximate time, and visible error. Do not retry continuously until new task output obscures the old task.","locale":"en"},"6249":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#start-collection","content":"Open “Maintenance → Diagnostics” and select “Collect Diagnostic Information.” Progress appears in the bottom-right corner of Instance Manager. Leaving the Diagnostics page does not cancel collection.","locale":"en"},"6250":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#check-completion-status","content":"Refresh the diagnostic-bundle list after collection finishes. It shows the file name, creation time, size, and number of collection issues. If an individual source cannot be read, other content may still be written to the archive successfully.","locale":"en"},"6251":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-and-export","content":"Select “Open Diagnostic Bundle Directory” to locate the original, or use “Save a Copy” to save it elsewhere. Extract and inspect it yourself before sending it to a trusted maintainer.","locale":"en"},"6252":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-and-export","content":"You can also collect diagnostics directly from a failed installation or launch. When collection succeeds, the workspace offers to save a copy. If you dismiss the prompt, the original remains in the list under **Maintenance → Diagnostics**.","locale":"en"},"6253":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"Environment-collection results for the current WebUI;","locale":"en"},"6254":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"instance snapshots, persisted records, and component paths;","locale":"en"},"6255":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"currently retained instance tasks, launch phases, and task output;","locale":"en"},"6256":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"persisted and effective hotpatch configuration, status, events, and logs;","locale":"en"},"6257":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"application settings, identity, and diagnostic information required for troubleshooting;","locale":"en"},"6258":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"collection scope, issues, file sizes, and SHA-256 values in `manifest.json`.","locale":"en"},"6259":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"This page collects diagnostics for the current instance. To investigate several instances together, open **Settings → Diagnostics** and choose the scope for an application bundle. See Diagnostics Settings.","locale":"en"},"6260":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-may-contain","content":"Collected content is retained as-is and may contain credentials, tokens, environment variables,\nlocal paths, command arguments, and task output. Although some dedicated credential files are\nexcluded in their entirety, that does not make the archive safe to share publicly.","locale":"en"},"6261":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"Copy the ZIP to a temporary location and extract it. Do not modify the original bundle saved by\nthe app.","locale":"en"},"6262":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"Search for user names, home directories, tokens, proxy addresses, remote-repository credentials,\nand custom environment variables.","locale":"en"},"6263":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"Check the scope and collection issues in `manifest.json`, then remove files you do not intend to\nshare or create a redacted copy.","locale":"en"},"6264":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"Send it only through a trusted channel, and delete originals and copies you no longer need after\nthe issue is resolved.","locale":"en"},"6265":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"Diagnostic bundles have no automatic expiration or deletion policy. The page currently has no Delete button. Use “Open Diagnostic Bundle Directory” to manage the files yourself.","locale":"en"},"6266":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-diagnostics#inspect-before-sharing","content":"<Card title=\"Logs, diagnostics, and getting help\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting-reporting\" description=\"Choose a diagnostic scope and submit a reproducible issue report.\" />","locale":"en"},"6267":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","type":"page","content":"Extension Management","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","locale":"en"},"6268":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","content":"Install, update, enable, disable, switch versions, or uninstall extensions supported by the current WebUI.","locale":"en"},"6269":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Install an extension","locale":"en"},"6270":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Manage local extensions","locale":"en"},"6271":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"Update or switch versions","locale":"en"},"6272":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","content":"Whether the “Extensions” page is available, and which actions it offers, depends on the management capabilities of the current WebUI. The page usually has “Local Extensions” and “Extension Marketplace” views. An instance without marketplace support may still be able to manage extensions already installed.","locale":"en"},"6273":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Open “Extension Marketplace” and use the search box to filter the index already loaded.","locale":"en"},"6274":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Review the extension name, author, source, and installation status. An entry marked “Cannot\nInstall” cannot be forcibly installed.","locale":"en"},"6275":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Select Install, wait for the task in Task Center to complete, then switch to “Local\nExtensions” and confirm that the entry appears.","locale":"en"},"6276":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Confirm that the repository is compatible with the current WebUI type and version, then copy\nthe complete Git repository URL.","locale":"en"},"6277":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Wait for the task to finish. If it fails, check repository access, the GitHub mirror, and\ntask output.","locale":"en"},"6278":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#install-an-extension","content":"Marketplace search matches names, descriptions, authors, and tags in the loaded index. Local Extensions searches installed names, source URLs, and branches. Refresh updates the current tab. Select a repository link to open the project in your system browser.","locale":"en"},"6279":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"6280":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Description","locale":"en"},"6281":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Enable / Disable","locale":"en"},"6282":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Change extension status, usually taking effect the next time the WebUI launches","locale":"en"},"6283":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Update","locale":"en"},"6284":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Pull updates for a Git extension or install the latest published version of a Comfy Registry node. File extensions have no Update button.","locale":"en"},"6285":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Update All","locale":"en"},"6286":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Process each currently updatable extension in sequence; inspect failed items in Task Center","locale":"en"},"6287":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Branch / Commit","locale":"en"},"6288":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Switch a Git-based extension to a specified branch or commit","locale":"en"},"6289":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Registry Version","locale":"en"},"6290":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Select a published version for ComfyUI nodes that support the Registry","locale":"en"},"6291":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Uninstall","locale":"en"},"6292":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"Delete the extension directory or have the current WebUI perform its corresponding uninstall operation","locale":"en"},"6293":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#manage-local-extensions","content":"When the last instance update check found updates, the page shows the count and marks the corresponding installed extensions. Git repositories usually offer branch and commit selection. Registry nodes use the published-version picker. Local file extensions have fewer actions.","locale":"en"},"6294":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"Create a snapshot and record the current branch, commit, or Registry version of important\nextensions.","locale":"en"},"6295":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"Update or switch one extension at a time. Use “Update All” only when a batch update is needed.","locale":"en"},"6296":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"Wait for the task to finish, refresh the Local Extensions list, and launch the WebUI again.","locale":"en"},"6297":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"If launch fails, disable the most recently changed extension first, then inspect its task output\nand compatibility notes.","locale":"en"},"6298":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"The uninstall confirmation explicitly states that extension files will be deleted from the\ninstance. Whether the extension's own configuration, models, or outputs are also removed depends\non where they are actually stored. Inspect and back them up before uninstalling.","locale":"en"},"6299":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-extensions#update-or-switch-versions","content":"If an extension download fails, check Network & Proxy and Mirrors. To roll back the environment as a whole, use Snapshot Management.","locale":"en"},"6300":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","type":"page","content":"Hotpatch","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","locale":"en"},"6301":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","content":"Configure hotpatches, control patches and features in a running WebUI, and inspect runtime logs.","locale":"en"},"6302":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#configuration-editors","content":"Configuration editors","locale":"en"},"6303":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Save versus apply","locale":"en"},"6304":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"Runtime control","locale":"en"},"6305":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"Change hotpatch configuration","locale":"en"},"6306":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","content":"Hotpatch capabilities are supplied by the current WebUI and appear only when the backend detects a configuration or runtime capability. Use the Hotpatch page to edit configuration, read logs, and control live patches on supported instances. A runtime status summary appears under “Hotpatch Runtime” in Instance Information.","locale":"en"},"6307":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#configuration-editors","content":"The form is generated from the current hotpatch catalog. After you change a Boolean, integer,\noption, list, or object, it saves the complete configuration automatically after briefly\ncombining consecutive input. “Restore Defaults” also saves automatically in form mode.","locale":"en"},"6308":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#configuration-editors","content":"The raw editor provides precise control over the complete configuration object. Input must be a\nvalid JSON object. Changes create only a draft until you select Save. Incomplete or malformed\nJSON is not written to the instance.","locale":"en"},"6309":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#configuration-editors","content":"“Normalize” asks the backend to reconcile the draft with the current catalog, such as filling in, converting, or rejecting values that violate field constraints. It is not the same as applying the configuration to a running WebUI.","locale":"en"},"6310":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"6311":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"6312":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Save Configuration","locale":"en"},"6313":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Persist the current instance's hotpatch configuration","locale":"en"},"6314":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Apply locally","locale":"en"},"6315":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Ask a WebUI that supports this operation to update its local patch configuration","locale":"en"},"6316":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Apply remotely","locale":"en"},"6317":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"Send the normalized configuration to the currently running hotpatch session","locale":"en"},"6318":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#save-versus-apply","content":"“Apply remotely” is unavailable while the runtime is not running. Save the configuration first and then launch the WebUI. Confirm runtime status in “Instance Information.”","locale":"en"},"6319":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"If the **Runtime control** tab appears, open it to check the current WebUI's hotpatcher. For **Not running**, launch the WebUI and wait for the runtime to connect. For **Not answering**, the app retries in a few seconds, or you can select **Check again**. **Not supported** means the hotpatcher is too old. Update this WebUI's environment to use runtime control.","locale":"en"},"6320":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"When the status is **Available**, the actions depend on the commands supported by this session.","locale":"en"},"6321":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"**Patches, Patch sets, and Features** let you inspect and unload active patches and sets. To unload a set owned by a feature, turn off the feature. To load a new set, edit `control.patch_sets` in **Configuration** and restart the WebUI. Features that require importing code or loading a patch set also need a configuration change and a restart.","locale":"en"},"6322":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"**Inspect** accepts a Python module's import name to explain its patches, verify them, or show the patched source. Leave the name blank and select **Verify** to check every patched module.","locale":"en"},"6323":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"**Debug** shows runtime events and lets you adjust trace tags and strict mode. Enable `control.forward_events` in **Configuration** to receive forwarded events. **Connection** shows read-only details of the current desktop connection.","locale":"en"},"6324":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#runtime-control","content":"Actions that change the running session, such as unloading a patch or toggling a feature, create management tasks. Open Task Center to see their results.","locale":"en"},"6325":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"Find the target feature in the form. Keep the default when you are unsure what a field means.","locale":"en"},"6326":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"After making a change, wait for the bottom-right status area to report that the configuration\nwas saved. In JSON mode, correct every formatting error before saving manually.","locale":"en"},"6327":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"Select “Apply locally” or “Apply remotely,” depending on what the current WebUI supports.","locale":"en"},"6328":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"Open “Logs,” filter runtime feedback by level and source, and confirm that there are no loading\nor execution errors.","locale":"en"},"6329":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"If online application is unavailable, stop and relaunch the WebUI, then inspect hotpatch runtime\nstatus under “Instance Information.”","locale":"en"},"6330":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"The Logs page continuously reads retained records from the current runtime session. “Clear View” clears only the logs already displayed on the current page. It does not change configuration and must not be treated as resolving a problem.","locale":"en"},"6331":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-hotpatch#change-hotpatch-configuration","content":"Hotpatch fields are supplied dynamically by the current WebUI and version. Pasting complete JSON\nfrom another type or an older version can fail validation. Save a copy of the current\nconfiguration before making changes.","locale":"en"},"6332":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"page","content":"Launch Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch","locale":"en"},"6333":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch","content":"Configure WebUI launch arguments and instance environment variables, and handle pre-launch argument checks.","locale":"en"},"6334":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Two ways to edit arguments","locale":"en"},"6335":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#configure-launch-arguments","content":"Configure launch arguments","locale":"en"},"6336":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#stop-the-webui","content":"Stop the WebUI","locale":"en"},"6337":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#edit-the-raw-string","content":"Edit the raw string","locale":"en"},"6338":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#open-the-structured-editor-when-needed","content":"Open the structured editor when needed","locale":"en"},"6339":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#check-for-a-restart-notice","content":"Check for a restart notice","locale":"en"},"6340":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables","locale":"en"},"6341":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Incompatible arguments discovered at launch","locale":"en"},"6342":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch","content":"The “Launch” page saves the environment variables for the next launch of the current instance. Types that offer launch arguments also let you edit the command line here. Changes take effect the next time you start the WebUI.","locale":"en"},"6343":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch","content":"An extension can provide **Service launch options**, such as a listen address, context length or GPU layer count. Save the form to apply it the next time the service starts. The installed instance stays in place.","locale":"en"},"6344":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Editor","locale":"en"},"6345":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Best for","locale":"en"},"6346":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Saving and validation","locale":"en"},"6347":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Raw argument string","locale":"en"},"6348":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"You already know the syntax and want to paste a complete command line quickly","locale":"en"},"6349":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Parsed according to command-line syntax; unknown arguments produce warnings but are not silently removed","locale":"en"},"6350":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Structured editor","locale":"en"},"6351":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"You want to choose from arguments actually supported by the current WebUI","locale":"en"},"6352":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Checks argument counts, values, duplicates, required items, and mutually exclusive groups","locale":"en"},"6353":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"Enter only the arguments passed to the WebUI in the raw field. Do not include the Python executable or launch script. For example:","locale":"en"},"6354":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#two-ways-to-edit-arguments","content":"This is only an example of command-line syntax. Whether an argument exists, requires a value, or accepts particular values depends on the catalog loaded by the structured editor for the current instance.","locale":"en"},"6355":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#stop-the-webui","content":"A running WebUI does not restart automatically when its configuration changes. Stop the instance first so you do not forget to restart it and mistakenly assume the arguments are already active.","locale":"en"},"6356":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#edit-the-raw-string","content":"Enter arguments using command-line syntax. A single value containing spaces must be quoted. After submitting, inspect the parsing errors and unknown-argument warnings shown on the page.","locale":"en"},"6357":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#open-the-structured-editor-when-needed","content":"Select “Configure Launch Arguments,” enable options from the argument catalog, and fill in their values. The editor saves as you make changes. If it reports that the configuration is stale, reload it before continuing to edit.","locale":"en"},"6358":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#check-for-a-restart-notice","content":"When the page shows “Restart Required,” return to “Instance Information,” launch the WebUI, and confirm in the launch task that the final argument check passed.","locale":"en"},"6359":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#check-for-a-restart-notice","content":"If the structured catalog cannot be loaded, the page falls back to the raw editor. You can keep and save arguments in that mode, but automatic validation is more limited. Check the management API and Core environment, then use “Retry Discovery.”","locale":"en"},"6360":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#check-for-a-restart-notice","content":"In the structured editor you can search the catalog or type the start of a flag on the command line. When suggestions appear, use the arrow keys to select one, press `Tab` or `Enter` to complete it, or press `Esc` to dismiss the list. Unrecognized arguments are listed with their values. Remove groups individually or leave custom arguments in place.","locale":"en"},"6361":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables apply to managed processes for the current instance. Each name must be unique, and its value may be empty. If a name is missing or duplicated, the editor keeps the draft until you correct it. Use a row's remove button to delete a variable or discard pending changes to return to the saved values.","locale":"en"},"6362":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#environment-variables","content":"Add only variables explicitly required by the current WebUI, extension, or script.","locale":"en"},"6363":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#environment-variables","content":"Managed environment values such as `PATH`, `PYTHONPATH`, `MAMBA_*`, and `CONDA_*` may be reserved or recomposed by the app. Do not rely on them to override the desktop runtime environment.","locale":"en"},"6364":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#environment-variables","content":"Environment-variable values are shown normally and may also appear in task output or diagnostic bundles. Check for tokens and other sensitive values before sharing screenshots or diagnostics.","locale":"en"},"6365":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"The save step allows options not yet recognized by the current argument catalog to remain, accommodating branches, extensions, or future versions. At the actual launch, the backend checks the raw arguments again against the current catalog for unknown arguments, orphaned values, and other constraints, then offers these choices:","locale":"en"},"6366":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Choice","locale":"en"},"6367":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"6368":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Cancel","locale":"en"},"6369":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-36","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Do not create WebUI runtime resources; return to the configuration page and make changes","locale":"en"},"6370":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-37","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Ignore Once","locale":"en"},"6371":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-38","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Continue this launch with the raw arguments; do not change the saved configuration","locale":"en"},"6372":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-39","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Remove Incompatible Items and Launch","locale":"en"},"6373":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-40","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"Remove the invalid fragments precisely identified by the backend, save the complete cleaned argument string, and continue launching","locale":"en"},"6374":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-41","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"“Ignore Once” is appropriate when you have confirmed that a branch-specific argument is still\nvalid. If the launch still fails, return to this page and correct the arguments instead of\nrepeatedly ignoring the same warning.","locale":"en"},"6375":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-42","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"<Card title=\"Instance launch and access troubleshooting\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting-instance-start\" description=\"Resolve process exits, port conflicts, missing addresses, and inaccessible pages.\" />","locale":"en"},"6376":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-launch-43","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-launch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-launch#incompatible-arguments-discovered-at-launch","content":"<Card title=\"Upstream WebUI problems\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting-webui\" description=\"Resolve model, extension, node, and generation-stage errors.\" />","locale":"en"},"6377":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"page","content":"Instance Maintenance","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","locale":"en"},"6378":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","content":"Understand the file effects of renaming, migration, reinstallation, record-only deletion, and full deletion.","locale":"en"},"6379":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Prepare before an operation","locale":"en"},"6380":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#rename","content":"Rename","locale":"en"},"6381":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#migrate-an-instance","content":"Migrate an instance","locale":"en"},"6382":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#select-the-destination-parent","content":"Select the destination parent","locale":"en"},"6383":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#read-the-migration-preview","content":"Read the migration preview","locale":"en"},"6384":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#start-and-wait-for-migration","content":"Start and wait for migration","locale":"en"},"6385":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#verify-the-migration","content":"Verify the migration","locale":"en"},"6386":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"Reinstall an instance","locale":"en"},"6387":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"Delete an instance or only its record","locale":"en"},"6388":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#failures-and-recovery","content":"Failures and recovery","locale":"en"},"6389":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","content":"The “Maintenance” page does not depend on the WebUI management API and remains available when management features fail. Migration, reinstallation, and deletion are instance-lifecycle operations: the app first stops and confirms related runtime resources, then modifies files or records.","locale":"en"},"6390":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Stop the WebUI under “Instance Information,” and wait for current installation, management, and\nterminal tasks to finish.","locale":"en"},"6391":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Create an environment snapshot, and separately back up models, outputs, configuration, and\ncustom code.","locale":"en"},"6392":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Check the instance root, Python path, and Core path shown on the page. Pay particular attention\nto components outside the root.","locale":"en"},"6393":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"After starting an operation, continue watching the bottom-right status area and Task Center\nuntil the task explicitly completes or fails.","locale":"en"},"6394":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"6395":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Effect on directories","locale":"en"},"6396":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Rename","locale":"en"},"6397":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Updates the display name only","locale":"en"},"6398":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Migrate instance","locale":"en"},"6399":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Moves the entire root. Components outside the root stay in place.","locale":"en"},"6400":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Reinstall","locale":"en"},"6401":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Reuses existing components where possible. Forcing a rebuild deletes the selected component directory.","locale":"en"},"6402":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Delete record only","locale":"en"},"6403":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Keeps all directories","locale":"en"},"6404":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Delete instance","locale":"en"},"6405":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#prepare-before-an-operation","content":"Deletes the directories the instance owns, including owned components outside the root. Keeps components explicitly marked external.","locale":"en"},"6406":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#rename","content":"Renaming changes only the instance name displayed in Hanafubuki. The instance ID, identity, instance root, and all component paths remain unchanged. Submitting the same name does not create another configuration change.","locale":"en"},"6407":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#migrate-an-instance","content":"Migration moves the complete instance root; it does not merely update a path setting. The page requires an existing destination parent directory. The backend appends the current instance directory name and requires the final directory not to exist yet.","locale":"en"},"6408":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#migrate-an-instance","content":"Python, Core, models, and other files inside the instance root move with the complete directory. Components outside the root stay where they are. If the root itself is an external Core or contains a component marked external, the preview refuses the move.","locale":"en"},"6409":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#select-the-destination-parent","content":"The destination parent must exist, and the final instance directory must not. Migration does not merge with or overwrite an existing directory.","locale":"en"},"6410":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#read-the-migration-preview","content":"The app revalidates instance identity, configuration, path overlap, and external components, then shows the final directory and warnings in the confirmation dialog.","locale":"en"},"6411":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#start-and-wait-for-migration","content":"After confirmation, the app stops the WebUI, management service, WebView, and instance terminal in sequence. It then moves the files and updates configuration atomically. A migration between drives may require a complete copy, so its duration depends on the size of the instance.","locale":"en"},"6412":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#verify-the-migration","content":"Reopen the instance after completion and check the root and managed component paths. Then verify the environment using the Instance Terminal and one real launch.","locale":"en"},"6413":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#verify-the-migration","content":"Migration does not scan for or rewrite absolute paths inside `.pth` files, scripts, environment variables, or other files. If a third-party component recorded the old location, correct it after migration using that component's own procedure.","locale":"en"},"6414":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-36","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#verify-the-migration","content":"If “Migration Requires Recovery” appears, the instance remains closed to protect file consistency.\nDo not manually move or delete the source, destination, or temporary directory. Select the\noriginal destination parent and choose “Migrate Instance” again to continue recovery.","locale":"en"},"6415":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-37","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"Reinstallation keeps the instance record. The form starts with the saved install parameters. When editing is available, confirming and starting the reinstall saves the new values for future installs. If the Python environment already exists, turn on **Force Rebuild Python** to change its environment parameters.","locale":"en"},"6416":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-38","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"Choose **Reinstall** to repeat installation. Leaving all component switches off preserves their directories. Ready extension instances that support updates also offer **Update**, which runs the type’s update steps with no component rebuild. The last check can show versions, release notes and individual component results beside these actions.","locale":"en"},"6417":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-39","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"When a type offers only `update-check`, updates are managed externally. Reinstalling local components preserves the last reported update and its component details until the next check.","locale":"en"},"6418":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-40","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"Use this to restore missing dependencies or rerun the installation workflow. Existing Python and\nCore components are reused where possible, although the installer may still update dependencies\nor code state. When Core is outside the instance root, standard reinstallation may still reuse\nand update it as long as it remains the same existing directory recorded for the instance.","locale":"en"},"6419":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-41","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"Check the path beside each switch. A forced rebuild permanently deletes the selected owned\ndirectory first. This can include an owned Core on another drive. You cannot force-rebuild a\ncomponent marked external or a Core that is itself the instance root. The installer requires\nPython inside the instance root.","locale":"en"},"6420":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-42","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"Check the paths beside the selected switches, read the deletion warning in the confirmation\ndialog, and then select “Reinstall.”","locale":"en"},"6421":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-43","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"After the instance enters the installation workspace, follow the task through its installation\nphases and logs.","locale":"en"},"6422":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-44","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#reinstall-an-instance","content":"When it finishes, check launch arguments, versions, extensions, and PyTorch before launching the\nWebUI.","locale":"en"},"6423":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-45","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"Delete only the records bound to the current instance identity in Hanafubuki. No files are\ninspected, moved, or deleted. The instance root, external Python/Core, and every other\nconfigured path remain intact and can be imported again later.","locale":"en"},"6424":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-46","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"The app deletes the listed directories before removing the record. This usually includes the\nentire root with its models and outputs, plus any components the instance owns elsewhere. If the\nroot is itself a Core marked external, the app keeps the root and deletes only the individual\ncomponents that the instance owns.","locale":"en"},"6425":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-47","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"If you only want to hide the instance from the app while preserving every file, choose “Delete\nRecord Only.”","locale":"en"},"6426":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-48","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"When selecting **Delete instance**, check every directory listed for deletion and any external\ncomponents listed to be kept.","locale":"en"},"6427":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-49","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"Do not close the app or manually delete the directory after submission. Deletion progress\nremains visible in the bottom-right corner of Instance Manager.","locale":"en"},"6428":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-50","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"After full deletion succeeds, the instance details disappear. The final success or failure\nstatus remains available in Instance Manager and Task Center.","locale":"en"},"6429":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-51","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#delete-an-instance-or-only-its-record","content":"File deletion cannot be undone through Hanafubuki. If you pointed Core to an existing project on\nanother drive and want to keep all of its files, choose **Delete record only**.","locale":"en"},"6430":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-52","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#failures-and-recovery","content":"When a maintenance operation cannot confirm process shutdown, file state, or a configuration commit, it retains the original task and recovery obligation instead of pretending to have completed. In that situation:","locale":"en"},"6431":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-53","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#failures-and-recovery","content":"Open the failed item in the bottom-right corner or Task Center to inspect the exact phase and error;","locale":"en"},"6432":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-54","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#failures-and-recovery","content":"do not complete the remaining steps manually in a file manager;","locale":"en"},"6433":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-55","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#failures-and-recovery","content":"after fixing permissions, disk, or file-in-use problems, retry the same operation through the interface;","locale":"en"},"6434":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance-56","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-maintenance#failures-and-recovery","content":"while the instance remains locked for maintenance, do not create a replacement instance at the same path.","locale":"en"},"6435":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"page","content":"Instance Management","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management","locale":"en"},"6436":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management","content":"Learn about the Instance Management entry point, feature sections, and task status, and find the corresponding guides.","locale":"en"},"6437":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#management-sections","content":"Management sections","locale":"en"},"6438":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#complete-a-management-operation","content":"Complete a management operation","locale":"en"},"6439":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#check-instance-status","content":"Check instance status","locale":"en"},"6440":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#open-the-relevant-section","content":"Open the relevant section","locale":"en"},"6441":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#run-and-track-the-operation","content":"Run and track the operation","locale":"en"},"6442":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result","locale":"en"},"6443":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#general","content":"General","locale":"en"},"6444":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#run","content":"Run","locale":"en"},"6445":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#resources","content":"Resources","locale":"en"},"6446":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-management#maintenance","content":"Maintenance","locale":"en"},"6447":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management","content":"Instance Management lets you inspect and maintain WebUIs that have already been created or imported. Open Instance Manager from Home and select an instance. The management navigation and current feature page appear on the right.","locale":"en"},"6448":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management","content":"The backend determines which management items are available from the WebUI type, installation status, and current API capabilities. When an item is disabled, hover over it to see why. If the instance has not finished installing, return to its workspace and complete the installation first.","locale":"en"},"6449":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#management-sections","content":"Filter the instance list by name, type ID, or part of its installation path. The buttons below the list add an instance or scan for existing WebUIs. Up and Down in the instance list switch the detail view. In the section navigation, use the arrow keys to focus an icon and press `Enter` to open it. When a narrow window shows only icons, hover or move keyboard focus into the list to reveal the labels. When space permits, use the arrow at the bottom to keep the navigation expanded or collapsed.","locale":"en"},"6450":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#management-sections","content":"Extensions can add management sections for their own instance types. The list omits features the type does not declare. If switching sections or instances opens **Save changes before leaving?**, choose **Save and leave** to apply edits, **Leave without saving** to discard them, or **Cancel** to stay in the form.","locale":"en"},"6451":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#management-sections","content":"Category","locale":"en"},"6452":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#management-sections","content":"Main features","locale":"en"},"6453":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#management-sections","content":"General","locale":"en"},"6454":{"id":