"/en/docs/instance-management-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#open-the-relevant-section","content":"Select a feature from the management navigation. An unavailable item usually means the current WebUI does not support that feature, the instance is not ready, or the management API does not expose the required capability.","locale":"en"},"6463":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#run-and-track-the-operation","content":"Short operations such as saving configuration appear in the bottom-right corner of the current manager. Long operations such as installation, update, restore, and migration also enter Task Center. Switching sections does not cancel a backend task.","locale":"en"},"6464":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#verify-the-result","content":"Wait for the status to become “Completed,” refresh the current section, then check the environment and runtime state in “Instance Information.” If an operation fails, open its task output before attempting the same operation again.","locale":"en"},"6465":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#verify-the-result","content":"The bottom-right status area reports operations started from the current Instance Manager. Task\nCenter retains tasks across pages, along with detailed phases and output. Closing the page while a\nstatus is still “Running” does not end the task.","locale":"en"},"6466":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-management-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-management#general","content":"<Card title=\"Instance Information\" href=\"/docs/instance-overview\" description=\"View status, servic