import them into the current directory. After the task finishes, refresh the list and verify the file name, size, and target location.","locale":"en"},"6505":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#import-and-verify","content":"With focus in the list, use the arrow keys to select entries, hold `Shift` to extend the selection, press `Ctrl+A` (`Cmd+A` on macOS) to select all, or press `Esc` to clear the selection. `Enter` opens a single selected folder. `Delete` opens the deletion prompt.","locale":"en"},"6506":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#import-and-verify","content":"The toolbar's Paste and Download buttons target the current folder. For a URL download, you can set the file name and choose the current folder or an immediate subfolder as the destination. Starting the download from a folder's context menu preselects that folder. Use Task Center to follow long copies, moves, or imports.","locale":"en"},"6507":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#invokeai-registry","content":"“Install from URL” asks InvokeAI to download and register the model.","locale":"en"},"6508":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#invokeai-registry","content":"“Import Local Model,” or drag and drop, passes a local file to the InvokeAI registration workflow.","locale":"en"},"6509":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#invokeai-registry","content":"“Unregister” removes only the Registry record; the model file remains on disk.","locale":"en"},"6510":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#invokeai-registry","content":"“Delete” removes both the Registry record and the associated file and cannot be undone.","locale":"en"},"6511":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#invokeai-registry","content":"If you only want InvokeAI to stop using a model but keep the file, choose “Unregister.” Choose Delete only when you intend to free the disk space completely.","locale":"en"},"6512":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#built-in-model-library","content":"Open “Built-in Model Library” and filter by type, or search by name, description, or tag.","locale":"en"},"6513":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#built-in-model-library","content":"Check the model type and any listed installation path. Hover over a disabled install button to\nsee why it is unavailable.","locale":"en"},"6514":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#built-in-model-library","content":"Check the latest installation result and warnings at the top of the library, then refresh “Local\nModels” to verify the target directory or Registry.","locale":"en"},"6515":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#built-in-model-library","content":"The model library uses the download sources and automatic mirror strategy in current settings. If a download fails, check Mirror Settings, Network & Proxy, and available disk space.","locale":"en"},"6516":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-models-36","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-models","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-models#built-in-model-library","content":"Delete in the file browser and 