,"url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"Check the instance root, Core, and Python executable","locale":"en"},"6534":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"Environment","locale":"en"},"6535":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"View the Python version and current branch","locale":"en"},"6536":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"Services","locale":"en"},"6537":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"View the management API, launch phase, launch warnings, and browser connection status","locale":"en"},"6538":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"Hotpatch runtime","locale":"en"},"6539":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"Confirm whether the patch runtime started with the WebUI","locale":"en"},"6540":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"Captured WebUI address","locale":"en"},"6541":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"View the preferred access address actually captured by the app; with several pages, the main page's address","locale":"en"},"6542":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"History","locale":"en"},"6543":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"View recent failure phases, exit codes, and associated task output","locale":"en"},"6544":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"The installation lifecycle indicates whether the instance files are ready. Runtime status indicates whether the WebUI process is currently running. A new launch can start only when the lifecycle is “Ready” and the WebUI is not running.","locale":"en"},"6545":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#open-instance-directories-and-quick-paths","content":"In **Paths**, use the folder button beside the instance root, Core, or another component to open its directory. The button beside the Python executable opens the Python component directory.","locale":"en"},"6546":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#open-instance-directories-and-quick-paths","content":"To keep an output folder or a shared model library close at hand, select **Add quick path…** under **Quick paths**, choose a directory, and click its tile to open it. Drag the tile by its icon to reorder it. Right-click or use its menu to rename or remove it. Changes are saved automatically. Removing a shortcut leaves the directory on disk.","locale":"en"},"6547":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#check-readiness","content":"Confirm that the installation lifecycle is “Ready,” the component directories required by the type exist, and no task is currently reinstalling the instance, restoring PyTorch, or installing a model-library item.","locale":"en"},"6548":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#select-launch","content":"The launch task opens in Task Center. The app checks the environment, PyTorch, extension conflicts, and launch arguments. If a choice is required, a launch-decision dialog appears.","locale":"en"},"6549":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#handle-launch-decisions","content":"Check which instance and problem the dialog names. Pressing `Esc` cancels this launch. See Launch decisions for what each choice changes.","locale":"en"},"6550":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#wait-for-address-capture","content":"Built-in WebUIs report their address at startup. For extension-provided instance types, **Services** can also list other services, their addresses, whether they are optional, and any failure reason. When a service that provides a WebUI page is ready, the workspace can open it. Some types only provide services and have no address-capture section.","locale":"en"},"6551":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"After selecting “Stop,” wait for runtime status to return to “Not Running.” Do not repeatedly select Launch while the process is stopping.","locale":"en"},"6552":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"“View Launch Task” opens the phases and output of the current launch. “View Logs” in error history opens the exact task in which that error occurred.","locale":"en"},"6553":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"If the WebUI is running but has no address, inspect the launch output for the listening address, port conflicts, and browser connection status.","locale":"en"},"6554":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-36","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"When status is “Awaiting Launch Decision,” handle the current decision before creating another launch task.","locale":"en"},"6555":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-37","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"After the process enters the running state, the WebUI may still be loading models or initializing\nservices. Rely on the captured address and task output. Troubleshoot the launch logs only if the\nprocess exists but no address appears for an extended period.","locale":"en"},"6556":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-38","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"To change launch arguments, read Launch Configuration. To inspect Python or Git, use the Instance Terminal.","locale":"en"},"6557":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"page","content":"Component Paths","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","locale":"en"},"6558":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Understand the differences between the instance root, Python, and Core, and safely update component references.","locale":"en"},"6559":{"id":"/en/docs/in