nt":"Launch arguments, environment variables, hotpatch settings and live state, component paths","locale":"en"},"7242":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-37","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#what-the-server-offers","content":"Provisioning","locale":"en"},"7243":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-38","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#what-the-server-offers","content":"Manage user presets and create, import, scan for, install, reinstall, move and delete instances","locale":"en"},"7244":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-39","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#what-the-server-offers","content":"Modules","locale":"en"},"7245":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-40","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#what-the-server-offers","content":"List the app's modules and extensions with their state, restart one, and run an operation an extension's instance type adds","locale":"en"},"7246":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-41","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#what-the-server-offers","content":"Every built-in tool is listed with what it may do in the tool reference, which the server also serves to clients (below). Long operations, such as an installation, return a task to follow: the client reads its progress and log the way you do in the Task Center. Instance types are named by their id, such as `builtin:comfyui`, so a client can create an instance of any type you have, an extension's included.","locale":"en"},"7247":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-42","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#what-the-server-offers","content":"For example, a client can read the current managed runtime directories and call `preview_runtime_storage_migration` to check a destination and show where each component would move. You can start the move from Settings after reviewing the preview. For application updates, `get_app_update_status` reads the existing result. A fresh `check_app_update` may download and prepare an update. You install it and restart from the application. Built-in management tools and arguments","locale":"en"},"7248":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-43","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#built-in-assistant","content":"The built-in assistant reaches the server with a key of its own, renewed every time the server starts. You do not need to configure anything for it, and other clients never take its connections: it keeps its own budget whatever they do. Its connection is the `hanafubuki` entry in the Agent's MCP servers; turning that entry off, changing its policies and what happens if you delete it are described in MCP. Turning off the **management-mcp** module on the Modules page switches the whole server off, the assistant's instance tools included.","locale":"en"},"7249":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-44","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#let-other-clients-connect","content":"External access is **off** by default. On **Settings › API Servers**, the **Management MCP server** card has the switch **Let added clients connect** (the same settings are under the module's **Settings** on the Modules page). While it is off, a client's token is refused as if it did not exist. Turning it on or off applies at once, without restarting the server, and turning it off also closes the connections clients have open.","locale":"en"},"7250":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-45","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#let-other-clients-connect","content":"A client can read your instances and their tasks. Within the access you give it, it can also\nstart, change, install into or delete them. Its token works for any program that has it, so keep\nit private, and add only tools you trust.","locale":"en"},"7251":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-46","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#add-a-client","content":"Click **Create**. The client's token is shown with a **Copy** button, above the configurations\nthat already contain it. Copy one of them into your client.","locale":"en"},"7252":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-47","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#show-a-clients-token-again","content":"Click the key button on the client's row (**Show token**). The application shows the token again, with **Copy** and the same configurations filled in, so you can set up the client again or in another tool. It reads the token only while that window is open.","locale":"en"},"7253":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-48","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#show-a-clients-token-again","content":"A client added with an earlier version of the application, before tokens were kept, has only a fingerprint of its token stored: its row says its token can't be shown, and **Show token** explains why. It keeps working with the token it has. To get a token you can show again, revoke the client and add it again.","locale":"en"},"7254":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-49","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"7255":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-50","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"What the client may do","locale":"en"},"7256":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-51","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Read only","locale":"en"},"7257":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-52","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"List and read instances, tasks and logs. Every change is refused","locale":"en"},"7258":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-53","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Manage, asking each time","locale":"en"},"7259":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-54","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Everything, but every change waits until you allow it in the main window","locale":"en"},"7260":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-55","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Manage without asking","locale":"en"},"7261":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-56","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Changes run without asking; deleting, restoring a snapshot or replacing something still asks","locale":"en"},"7262":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-57","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Manage without asking, even to delete","locale":"en"},"7263":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-58","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Deletion runs directly. Extension tools and custom instance operations still ask","locale":"en"},"7264":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-59","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Full access","locale":"en"},"7265":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-60","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Run all management tools, including deletion and custom extension operations, without MCP confirmation","locale":"en"},"7266":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-61","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"Read-only clients can discover an extension's published tools. Clients granted full access can invoke published tools and custom instance operations directly. Changes still appear in the Task Center. Turning a module on or off is never a client's: only you do that, on the Modules page. A client cannot restart the server it is talking to (the **management-mcp** module), and the built-in assistant cannot restart the module it runs in.","locale":"en"},"7267":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-62","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#access","content":"You can change a client's access or its name at any time from its row; a new access applies to its next request.","locale":"en"},"7268":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-63","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"The card's **How to connect a client** section, and the token screen (after **Create**, or from **Show token**) with the token filled in, show the configurations:","locale":"en"},"7269":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-64","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"**Claude Code**:","locale":"en"},"7270":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-65","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"**Cursor** and other clients that read an `mcpServers` JSON file:","locale":"en"},"7271":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-66","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"**VS Code**: If you are editing `.vscode/mcp.json`, use the top-level key `servers`. Add a `hanafubuki` entry with `\"type\": \"http\"` and the `url` and `headers` from the card. For shared workspace configuration, an input variable can supply the token. VS Code MCP configuration reference","locale":"en"},"7272":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-67","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"**Claude Desktop** starts its MCP servers as programs, so it starts **hanafubuki-mcp**, the bridge program installed with the application. Its entry for `claude_desktop_config.json` names the bridge, with the token and the application's endpoint file in its environment; the card fills in the real paths:","locale":"en"},"7273":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-68","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"The address normally uses port 43761; the **Port** field on the **Management MCP server** card changes it (0 lets the system choose one at every start), and the server restarts on the new port at once. If that port is taken, the server uses another one, which the API Servers page shows; update the configuration of Claude Code, Cursor or VS Code to match. Claude Desktop's needs no change: the application writes the current address to the endpoint file whenever the server starts, and the bridge reads it each time Claude Desktop starts the bridge. The bridge reads it only then: if the server moved to another port while Claude Desktop was running, restart the server in Claude Desktop (or Claude Desktop itself) so that the bridge reads the new address.","locale":"en"},"7274":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-69","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"The bridge does not start the application. If the application is not running, or external access\nis off, Claude Desktop shows \"Hanafubuki is not running, or its external MCP access is off\"; if\nthe client was revoked, \"the token was refused\". Start the application, turn external access on\nand restart the server in Claude Desktop. The endpoint file (`data/mcp/endpoint.json` in the\napplication's data folder) holds only the address, never a token, and exists only while the server\nruns with external access on.","locale":"en"},"7275":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-70","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#connect-a-client","content":"When the application runs as an AppImage, its files, the bridge included, exist only while it\nruns, so Claude Desktop has no bridge it could start. The card then offers no Claude Desktop\nconfiguration; Claude Code, Cursor and VS Code connect as usual.","locale":"en"},"7276":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-71","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#confirmations","content":"When a client asks to change something that needs your approval, the main window asks, naming the client (**Allow Claude Code to do this?**), and shows what it would do, the instance and the tool. A destructive change carries a warning, and its **Allow** button is red.","locale":"en"},"7277":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-72","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#confirmations","content":"**Allow** runs it; **Deny** or Escape refuses it. Focus starts on **Deny**, so a key you meant for something else cannot allow it.","locale":"en"},"7278":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-73","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#confirmations","content":"You have **60 seconds**. A request nobody answers is refused, and the client is told it was not confirmed in time.","locale":"en"},"7279":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-74","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#confirmations","content":"Several requests queue: the dialog shows how many more are waiting.","locale":"en"},"7280":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-75","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#confirmations","content":"While a request waits, it is also listed in the **Task Center**, so you see it on returning to a hidden window. Cancelling it there denies it.","locale":"en"},"7281":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-76","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#confirmations","content":"If the main window is not open, the request is refused at once. Nothing is ever allowed without you.","locale":"en"},"7282":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-77","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#the-record-in-the-task-center","content":"Every change a client asked for appears in the **Task Center** with the kind **MCP client**, named after the client and what it did: completed, failed with its error, or cancelled with the reason (denied by you, not confirmed in time, or not allowed by its access). The Task Center keeps the latest 100 of these while the application runs; they are not kept after it quits. Reads are not listed one by one; each client's row on the settings card shows when it was last used.","locale":"en"},"7283":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-78","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#the-usage-guide-for-agents","content":"The server comes with a usage guide written for AI agents, the `hanafubuki-webui-management` Skill: which tool to use for what, how to take ids from `list_instances` instead of guessing them, how to follow a long operation through its task and log, and which tools need care. The built-in assistant has it installed as a Skill (Skills).","locale":"en"},"7284":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-79","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#the-usage-guide-for-agents","content":"An external client reads the same guide from the server as MCP resources, and the server's instructions point every client to them:","locale":"en"},"7285":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-80","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#the-usage-guide-for-agents","content":"`hanafubuki://skills/webui-management/SKILL.md`: the guide;","locale":"en"},"7286":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-81","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#the-usage-guide-for-agents","content":"`hanafubuki://skills/webui-management/references/tools.md`: the tool reference.","locale":"en"},"7287":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-82","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#the-usage-guide-for-agents","content":"A client that shows MCP resources lets you attach them to a conversation; otherwise ask the agent to read the `SKILL.md` resource of the `hanafubuki` server before it starts. If your agent has a Skill system of its own (Claude Code, Codex and others read the same `SKILL.md` format), you can download the Skill's folder and unpack it into it. The guide calls the server `hanafubuki`, the name the configurations above give it.","locale":"en"},"7288":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-83","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#revoke-a-client","content":"Click the client's **Revoke** button and confirm. Its token stops working at once and its open connections close. To connect it again, add it again and configure the new token. An entry the application could not read from its file is listed as **Unreadable client entry**, with **Remove**.","locale":"en"},"7289":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-84","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"**Only this computer.** The server listens on this computer only; other computers on your network cannot reach it. It refuses requests from web pages, so a site you open in a browser cannot use it either.","locale":"en"},"7290":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-85","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"**Nothing without a token.** Other clients get in only while external access is on, each with a token of its own that you can revoke at any time. The built-in assistant's key changes every time the server starts.","locale":"en"},"7291":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-86","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"**You stay in charge of changes.** Unless you chose to trust a client, every change waits for you, and deletions wait for you unless you also chose \"even to delete\". Every change a client makes is listed in the Task Center.","locale":"en"},"7292":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-87","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"**Keep tokens like passwords.** The application keeps each token, with a fingerprint it checks requests against, in its configuration folder (`config/mcp/clients.json`), so that you can show it again. On macOS and Linux only your account can read that file; on Windows it is protected like the rest of your profile folder. Anyone who can read your configuration folder can therefore read the tokens, as they can the assistant's provider keys stored there. Diagnostic bundles never include the file. A copy of a token in a client's own configuration is that client's to protect; the application cannot take a copy back, only revoke the client.","locale":"en"},"7293":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-88","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"**What it does not protect against.** Any program running under your own account can read your files, the clients file and client configurations included, so the tokens protect against other users and web pages, not against malware on your account.","locale":"en"},"7294":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-89","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"<Card title=\"API Servers\" href=\"/docs/settings-api-servers\" description=\"Where the MCP server's address and the external clients card are.\" />","locale":"en"},"7295":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-90","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"<Card title=\"Task Center\" href=\"/docs/task-center\" description=\"Follow the changes clients made and the requests waiting for you.\" />","locale":"en"},"7296":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server-91","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mcp-server#security-in-plain-words","content":"<Card title=\"MCP\" href=\"/docs/agent-mcp\" description=\"The built-in assistant's hanafubuki entry and its policies.\" />","locale":"en"},"7297":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","type":"page","content":"Mirrors","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","locale":"en"},"7298":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","content":"Configure Micromamba, PyPI, GitHub, Hugging Face, and model download sources.","locale":"en"},"7299":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Automatic and manual modes","locale":"en"},"7300":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Recommended configuration order","locale":"en"},"7301":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","content":"Mirrors can improve package and resource download speeds on particular networks, but their contents may be delayed or incomplete. Most users should begin with **Automatically select mirrors** and switch to manual settings only when a fixed source is required or while troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"7302":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"With **Automatically select mirrors** enabled, Hanafubuki checks connectivity using the current proxy settings when it prepares managed Git with Micromamba. A successful check selects the official channels. A failed check or timeout selects a mirror. The Python installation flow selects its own supported sources. Automatic mode disables manual controls and preserves their saved values.","locale":"en"},"7303":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"After disabling automatic selection, you can control:","locale":"en"},"7304":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"7305":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Main purpose","locale":"en"},"7306":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Micromamba mirror","locale":"en"},"7307":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Packages and channels for the Conda environment, Git, and other managed tools","locale":"en"},"7308":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"PyPI mirror","locale":"en"},"7309":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Installation of WebUI Python dependencies","locale":"en"},"7310":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"GitHub mirror","locale":"en"},"7311":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Core, extensions, and release resources","locale":"en"},"7312":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Hugging Face mirror","locale":"en"},"7313":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Hugging Face repositories and files","locale":"en"},"7314":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Model download source","locale":"en"},"7315":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Choose between ModelScope and Hugging Face","locale":"en"},"7316":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"To enter a custom GitHub or Hugging Face address, disable automatic selection and enable the corresponding manual mirror. Enter a complete address with `http://` or `https://` and a hostname.","locale":"en"},"7317":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"First verify the connection method under **Network and Proxy** so you do not mistake a proxy\nproblem for a mirror problem.","locale":"en"},"7318":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Keep automatic mirrors enabled and retry the failed task once, recording the destination source\nand error in task output.","locale":"en"},"7319":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"If you truly need a fixed source, disable automatic mirrors and change only the setting related\nto the failed resource.","locale":"en"},"7320":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Run the same task again and check whether the error changes and the actual source is available.","locale":"en"},"7321":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"If versions, commits, or checksums disagree, disable the relevant mirror and verify against the\nofficial source.","locale":"en"},"7322":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"The model download source affects only operations using the built-in model downloader. It does not move existing models or change the source from which extensions are downloaded through Git.","locale":"en"},"7323":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"A mirror may omit the latest commit, return a different file, or synchronize late. If an\ninstallation result is abnormal, retry from the official source and review task output. Do not\ndisable verification to accept a mismatched file.","locale":"en"},"7324":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"If every source fails to connect, inspect system time, DNS, proxy, and firewall first. If only one type of resource fails, inspect its corresponding mirror or change the model download source.","locale":"en"},"7325":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","type":"page","content":"Network and Proxy","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-network","locale":"en"},"7326":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network","content":"Configure the system proxy, a manual proxy, or a direct connection.","locale":"en"},"7327":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"Choosing a proxy mode","locale":"en"},"7328":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Configuring a manual proxy","locale":"en"},"7329":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network","content":"Proxy settings control how backend downloads, hosted services, and subsequently launched tasks and terminals access the network. They are independent of mirror settings: a proxy determines **how to connect**, while a mirror determines **which source to connect to**.","locale":"en"},"7330":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"Once the application API server is running, it checks the system proxy about every 30 seconds.\nThe page shows the effective address. If the system reports no proxy, connections go directly.\nIf detection fails, the application keeps the last successful result for the current settings.","locale":"en"},"7331":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"All relevant network operations use the proxy URL you enter. This is useful when the system\nproxy cannot be detected or when only Hanafubuki should use a particular proxy.","locale":"en"},"7332":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"Ignore both system and manual proxies and connect directly. Use this for a direct network or to\ndetermine whether a failure is caused by an incorrect proxy.","locale":"en"},"7333":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"The manual address must include a protocol, host, and explicit port, for example:","locale":"en"},"7334":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Supported protocols are `http`, `https`, `socks`, `socks4`, `socks4a`, `socks5`, and `socks5h`. An address containing only `127.0.0.1`, no port, or a protocol such as `ftp` is rejected.","locale":"en"},"7335":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Start the proxy application and confirm that it works, noting its listening protocol and port.","locale":"en"},"7336":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Select **Manual** and enter the complete proxy URL. The mode and address are validated together.","locale":"en"},"7337":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Wait for the save to succeed in the lower-right corner, then run a small update check or\ndownload task.","locale":"en"},"7338":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"If it fails, switch to **Disabled** for a direct-connection comparison before deciding whether\nto inspect the proxy or mirror.","locale":"en"},"7339":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Hanafubuki synchronizes the effective proxy with running application and instance API servers. New child processes also use the new settings. An existing WebUI, command, or ordinary terminal keeps its startup environment. Restart that process if it needs the new proxy.","locale":"en"},"7340":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"If the proxy URL contains a username or password, do not copy the complete address into public\nlogs, screenshots, or issue reports. Inspect a diagnostic bundle before sharing it as well.","locale":"en"},"7341":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"page","content":"Paths","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths","locale":"en"},"7342":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths","content":"Manage the artifact cache, default installation directory, and managed runtime storage.","locale":"en"},"7343":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Cache and default installation directory","locale":"en"},"7344":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"Managed runtime storage","locale":"en"},"7345":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#migrating-managed-runtime-storage","content":"Migrating managed runtime storage","locale":"en"},"7346":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#enter-a-new-directory","content":"Enter a new directory","locale":"en"},"7347":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#preview-component-locations","content":"Preview component locations","locale":"en"},"7348":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#schedule-migration","content":"Schedule migration","locale":"en"},"7349":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#exit-normally-and-restart","content":"Exit normally and restart","locale":"en"},"7350":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result","locale":"en"},"7351":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths","content":"The Paths page contains two kinds of locations: ordinary downloads and instance defaults, and runtime storage maintained by the application itself. They serve different purposes, and changing one does not automatically migrate another.","locale":"en"},"7352":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"7353":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"7354":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Artifact cache directory","locale":"en"},"7355":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Location where future installation and download tasks save and reuse downloaded artifacts","locale":"en"},"7356":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Default WebUI installation directory","locale":"en"},"7357":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Root directory prefilled when creating a new instance; does not move or rewrite existing instances","locale":"en"},"7358":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"WebUI download directory","locale":"en"},"7359":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Where files downloaded from an embedded WebUI are saved; see WebView","locale":"en"},"7360":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"These fields must be saved manually. The backend validates and prepares the directories during save, so do not press `Enter` before you have finished entering a path.","locale":"en"},"7361":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"In the portable edition, each Launcher startup restores all three settings to the current portable workspace's default directories. Existing instances keep their registered locations.","locale":"en"},"7362":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Enter a path or use the directory picker. Check that you did not select a system directory or\nanother instance's component directory.","locale":"en"},"7363":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Create an instance or rerun a download task and confirm that the page uses the new default\nlocation.","locale":"en"},"7364":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Changing the artifact cache does not move the old cache or delete its original directory. After confirming that new tasks work, use the system file manager to assess whether the old cache can be removed.","locale":"en"},"7365":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"Managed runtime storage is maintained by Hanafubuki itself and contains:","locale":"en"},"7366":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"The application's Standalone Python.","locale":"en"},"7367":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"The Micromamba executable.","locale":"en"},"7368":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"The Conda root directory and package cache.","locale":"en"},"7369":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"Verified Launcher Python code.","locale":"en"},"7370":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"It does not contain WebUI instances, models, the ordinary artifact cache, or diagnostic bundles. To change only where new instances are located, edit **Default WebUI installation directory** instead of migrating the managed runtime.","locale":"en"},"7371":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#migrating-managed-runtime-storage","content":"If you previously moved the runtime to a custom directory, **Move to default location** previews a migration back to the default root. Check the destination before scheduling the move.","locale":"en"},"7372":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#enter-a-new-directory","content":"The final destination must be a new directory that does not yet exist. It cannot overlap application data, an existing instance, or a component path, and its path cannot traverse a symbolic link. After using Browse to select a parent directory, you can append a new child-directory name in the input.","locale":"en"},"7373":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#preview-component-locations","content":"Click **Migrate** and inspect the Python, Micromamba, Conda, and Launcher Code destinations in the confirmation dialog. This creates only a plan and does not copy files yet.","locale":"en"},"7374":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-32","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#schedule-migration","content":"Click **Migrate on next restart**. The page records the pending destination. If you have not exited the application, you can use **Cancel scheduled migration** to withdraw this plan.","locale":"en"},"7375":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-33","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#exit-normally-and-restart","content":"Finish running instances, terminals, and maintenance tasks first, then exit the application normally. On restart, the startup page completes migration before loading other features.","locale":"en"},"7376":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-34","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"After the application opens, return to **Paths** and **Runtime**. Confirm the current runtime root and the states of Python, Micromamba, and Git.","locale":"en"},"7377":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-35","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"Migration does not merge runtime content into an existing directory. During migration, do not move\nthe source directory, create the destination in advance, or start a second Hanafubuki process.","locale":"en"},"7378":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-36","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"If migration fails, the application continues using the original location if it remains valid and displays a recovery record. Resolve disk-space, permission, or destination-conflict problems, click **Retry on next restart**, then exit and start normally. Do not directly delete the source directory or staged destination content.","locale":"en"},"7379":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-37","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"If the page reports that the managed runtime storage configuration needs attention, the application uses the default root for this session and names the configuration file in the warning. It preserves that file and pauses migration. Repair a damaged file and restart, or open it with a compatible version of Hanafubuki if a newer version wrote it.","locale":"en"},"7380":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"page","content":"Runtime","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","locale":"en"},"7381":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","content":"Inspect and configure the application's Python, Micromamba, and Git.","locale":"en"},"7382":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Reading the status panels","locale":"en"},"7383":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-application-python","content":"Choosing application Python","locale":"en"},"7384":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Choosing a Git source","locale":"en"},"7385":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Troubleshooting failures","locale":"en"},"7386":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","content":"The Runtime page displays the Python, Micromamba, and Git that Hanafubuki itself depends on. These are application-level runtimes and are independent of each WebUI instance's own Python and Core.","locale":"en"},"7387":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Each panel shows the current status, preparation step, errors, and detected information:","locale":"en"},"7388":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Panel","locale":"en"},"7389":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Important information","locale":"en"},"7390":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Application runtime","locale":"en"},"7391":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Python version, executable, Python directory, Launcher Code, and application API","locale":"en"},"7392":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Micromamba","locale":"en"},"7393":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Bundled version, detected version, executable, and SHA-256","locale":"en"},"7394":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Git","locale":"en"},"7395":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Detected version, executable, installation task, and Conda-root repair state","locale":"en"},"7396":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"When the status is **Preparing**, watch the current step instead of repeatedly clicking Retry. When it is **Failed**, expand the error first and record the failed phase and details. Use Retry only when the panel offers it.","locale":"en"},"7397":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-application-python","content":"**Application Python version** supports the Python versions listed in the current interface. A change saves immediately but switches the application runtime only on the next startup.","locale":"en"},"7398":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-application-python","content":"Return to the Runtime page and confirm that the version, executable, and application API are all\nready.","locale":"en"},"7399":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-application-python","content":"Changing application Python does not reinstall an instance's Python or change the Python version selected for that instance. Troubleshoot instance-environment problems from the corresponding instance-management page.","locale":"en"},"7400":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Source","locale":"en"},"7401":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"7402":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Prefer system Git","locale":"en"},"7403":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"On the next startup, inspect Git on the system `PATH`; automatically fall back to Micromamba Git if it is unavailable","locale":"en"},"7404":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Use Micromamba Git","locale":"en"},"7405":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Skip system Git and always use the application-managed Git","locale":"en"},"7406":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"The Git source also takes effect on the next application startup. Keep the default when the system already has a usable Git installation. Choose Micromamba when you need a fixed, isolated Git environment.","locale":"en"},"7407":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Python download or verification failure: inspect the network, proxy, mirrors, disk space, and managed-runtime directory permissions.","locale":"en"},"7408":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Micromamba failure: confirm that a second application process is not using the runtime and that the destination disk is writable.","locale":"en"},"7409":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Git waiting for Micromamba: let Micromamba finish preparing first; this is not an independent Git hang.","locale":"en"},"7410":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"**Retry** under a status read error reads the status again. If live updates are unavailable, leave the Runtime page and reopen it to subscribe again and read the current result.","locale":"en"},"7411":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"To retry preparation, use **Retry** beside the runtime status or in its error details. It is available for the application runtime and Micromamba when idle or failed, and for Git after a failure. For repeated failures, collect a report from Diagnostics.","locale":"en"},"7412":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Do not overwrite managed Python, Micromamba, Conda, or Launcher Code from outside the application.\nHanafubuki prepares these components according to its own versions and verification rules, and may\nidentify manual changes as corruption during the next check.","locale":"en"},"7413":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"page","content":"WebView","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview","locale":"en"},"7414":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview","content":"Control whether WebUI pages are kept, whether instances share browsing data, how new windows open, and inspect or clear WebView data.","locale":"en"},"7415":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Fields","locale":"en"},"7416":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#keep-the-webui-page-when-leaving-its-workspace","content":"Keep the WebUI page when leaving its workspace","locale":"en"},"7417":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#share-cache-and-cookies-between-instances","content":"Share cache and cookies between instances","locale":"en"},"7418":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"When the WebUI opens a new window","locale":"en"},"7419":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#open-the-webui-in-an-external-browser","content":"Open the WebUI in an external browser","locale":"en"},"7420":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#downloads","content":"Downloads","locale":"en"},"7421":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"WebView data","locale":"en"},"7422":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#troubleshooting-page-display","content":"Troubleshooting page display","locale":"en"},"7423":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview","content":"A running WebUI is shown in the application's built-in browser (WebView). This section decides how that browser behaves and shows the data it keeps on disk. These settings affect only how pages are shown; they never start, stop, or modify the WebUI itself.","locale":"en"},"7424":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview","content":"WebView uses the browser engine the system provides: Microsoft Edge WebView2 on Windows, WebKitGTK on Linux, and WebKit on macOS.","locale":"en"},"7425":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"7426":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"7427":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"7428":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Keep the WebUI page when leaving its workspace","locale":"en"},"7429":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"On","locale":"en"},"7430":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Whether a page is kept as it was after you switch workspace or instance","locale":"en"},"7431":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Share cache and cookies between instances","locale":"en"},"7432":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"On","locale":"en"},"7433":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Whether every instance uses the same browsing data","locale":"en"},"7434":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"When the WebUI opens a new window","locale":"en"},"7435":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Built-in popup, and offer the external browser","locale":"en"},"7436":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"What happens when a page asks for a new window","locale":"en"},"7437":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"GPU acceleration (Linux)","locale":"en"},"7438":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"On","locale":"en"},"7439":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Uses the GPU to draw the app and its embedded WebUIs","locale":"en"},"7440":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#fields","content":"Changes save automatically. On Linux, if the window freezes or appears blank, turn off **GPU acceleration** and restart Hanafubuki to have WebKitGTK draw with the CPU. This setting controls rendering. Each instance retains its own settings for model inference.","locale":"en"},"7441":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#keep-the-webui-page-when-leaving-its-workspace","content":"When on, returning to the workspace finds the page exactly as you left it, including unsubmitted input and scroll position, without reloading. When off, leaving the workspace closes the page and returning reloads it. The WebUI itself keeps running either way.","locale":"en"},"7442":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#keep-the-webui-page-when-leaving-its-workspace","content":"Kept pages are listed and switched in WebUI Tabs in the title bar. Switching between the pages of one instance is not leaving its workspace, so those pages are always kept regardless of this setting.","locale":"en"},"7443":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#share-cache-and-cookies-between-instances","content":"When on, all instances use a shared store. Visiting the same site from another instance can reuse its saved sign-in. When off, each instance has its own cache, cookies, and site data.","locale":"en"},"7444":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#share-cache-and-cookies-between-instances","content":"After a change, a WebUI that is already open keeps the store it was opened with and switches only when it is opened again.","locale":"en"},"7445":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"When a page asks for a new window through a link or script, such as a `target=\"_blank\"` link or a popup sign-in, the choice decides what happens:","locale":"en"},"7446":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-32","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Choice","locale":"en"},"7447":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-33","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"7448":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-34","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Built-in popup, and offer the external browser","locale":"en"},"7449":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-35","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Opens a built-in popup and shows an **Opened in a new window** notice in the WebUI, offering the external browser instead","locale":"en"},"7450":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-36","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Built-in popup only","locale":"en"},"7451":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-37","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Opens only the built-in popup, without a notice","locale":"en"},"7452":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-38","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"External browser","locale":"en"},"7453":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-39","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Refuses the page's request and opens the destination in the system's default browser","locale":"en"},"7454":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-40","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"The built-in popup shares the WebUI's sign-in, which popup-based login flows depend on, but it has no toolbar and cannot download files on macOS. Under **External browser**, the page is told its window was blocked and popup-based sign-in fails. The setting applies to WebUI pages opened after the change.","locale":"en"},"7455":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-41","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Keep the default, **Built-in popup, and offer the external browser**. Sign-in works, and when you\nneed a download or a full browser, click **Open in external browser** in the notice.","locale":"en"},"7456":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-42","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#when-the-webui-opens-a-new-window","content":"Whichever you choose, the application refuses unsafe destinations and shows **Link blocked**: only HTTP and HTTPS addresses are allowed, and destinations carrying credentials, lacking a host name, or exceeding the length limit are refused.","locale":"en"},"7457":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-43","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#open-the-webui-in-an-external-browser","content":"The workspace's **Open in external browser** button hands the current WebUI address to the system's default browser; the page inside the application is left unchanged. When an instance has several pages, the one currently showing is opened. If no browser can be started, the application shows **Could not open your browser**.","locale":"en"},"7458":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-44","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#downloads","content":"Files downloaded in a WebUI are saved to **WebUI download directory** under Paths, which defaults to the `downloads` folder inside the application data directory. When a file with the same name exists, a number is appended to the new file's name; existing files are never overwritten.","locale":"en"},"7459":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-45","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#downloads","content":"Ordinary HTTP and HTTPS downloads appear in the **Downloads** tab of Task Center, where you can follow progress, pause, resume, and cancel them; they continue after the WebUI page closes. Files a page generates inside the browser (`blob:` or `data:` addresses) are saved directly by the browser engine and show only their result, without pause or cancel.","locale":"en"},"7460":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-46","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"The **WebView data** panel below the fields shows:","locale":"en"},"7461":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-47","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"The engine name and version.","locale":"en"},"7462":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-48","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"The storage directory, total disk usage, and the size of each shared or per-instance store. Both kinds can remain on disk after you change the sharing setting.","locale":"en"},"7463":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-49","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"**In use** marks stores that match the current sharing setting. If an open page holds a store, its row also explains why clearing is blocked. After closing the tab, use **Refresh** to check again.","locale":"en"},"7464":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-50","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"To clear one store, close the WebUI tabs using it, click the trash button on its row, and check the name in the confirmation. Pages using other stores can stay open. Clearing **Shared by every instance** affects every instance using that store. To clear the whole list, close all WebUI tabs and choose **Clear WebView data** beside the total.","locale":"en"},"7465":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-51","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#webview-data","content":"Clearing permanently removes cached files, cookies, and site preferences in the selected stores. You may need to sign in again. Instance files, models, and outputs stay on disk.","locale":"en"},"7466":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-52","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#troubleshooting-page-display","content":"Click **Open in external browser**. If the external browser cannot open it either, the problem\nlies with the WebUI service rather than WebView.","locale":"en"},"7467":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-53","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#troubleshooting-page-display","content":"If the external browser works but the page inside the application does not, close the WebUI page\nand open it again to rule out page state.","locale":"en"},"7468":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-54","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#troubleshooting-page-display","content":"If only one store is affected, close the tabs using it, clear its row, and open the page again.","locale":"en"},"7469":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-55","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#troubleshooting-page-display","content":"<Card title=\"WebUI Tabs\" href=\"/docs/webui-tabs\" description=\"Switch between, open, and close WebUI pages.\" />","locale":"en"},"7470":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-webview-56","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-webview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-webview#troubleshooting-page-display","content":"<Card title=\"Instance Startup and Access\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting-instance-start\" description=\"Separate problems in the WebUI service, address capture, and the embedded page.\" />","locale":"en"},"7471":{"id":"/en/docs/settings","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"page","content":"Settings","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings","locale":"en"},"7472":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings","content":"Understand how settings are saved and configure Hanafubuki by section.","locale":"en"},"7473":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"How settings are saved","locale":"en"},"7474":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings#modules","content":"Modules","locale":"en"},"7475":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"Finding settings by section","locale":"en"},"7476":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings","content":"The settings window manages options that apply across the application. The sidebar shows the sections provided by the current modules. To change an individual instance's paths, launch arguments, or maintenance options, open its management page.","locale":"en"},"7477":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Different field types use different save behavior:","locale":"en"},"7478":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Field type","locale":"en"},"7479":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Save behavior","locale":"en"},"7480":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Switch, dropdown","locale":"en"},"7481":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Saves automatically after selection","locale":"en"},"7482":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Text, number","locale":"en"},"7483":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Saves automatically when you press `Enter` or leave the input","locale":"en"},"7484":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Path","locale":"en"},"7485":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Click **Save** at the bottom of the page after editing","locale":"en"},"7486":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Save progress and results appear in the lower-right corner of the settings window. If saving is rejected, the input remains on the page. Complete or correct the field according to the error; click **Discard** if you do not want to continue editing.","locale":"en"},"7487":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"**Restore defaults** and **Discard** have different meanings:","locale":"en"},"7488":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"**Restore defaults**: Changes the current section to application defaults; ordinary fields save immediately.","locale":"en"},"7489":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"**Discard**: Reverts edits that have not been saved successfully and returns to the persisted values.","locale":"en"},"7490":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"**Restore defaults in a path section**: Places the default path in the input, but still requires **Save**, preventing an unconfirmed directory from being created.","locale":"en"},"7491":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Restore defaults does not delete downloaded files, move instances back, undo runtime migration, or\nrestore logs that have already been removed.","locale":"en"},"7492":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#modules","content":"**Settings → Modules** has three tabs, **Platform**, **Features**, and **Extensions**. Each card shows its state and what it contributes, such as instance types, Task Center entries, or diagnostic reports. Platform modules are required. The switches for installed extensions are on the Extensions page.","locale":"en"},"7493":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#modules","content":"When turning off a feature module, read the confirmation if one appears. It lists which modules will stop, which will keep running with some operations unavailable, and which instance maintenance tasks must wait until you turn the module back on. Configurable modules have a **Settings** expander. For example, the management MCP server lets you change its port and choose whether registered external clients can connect. Management MCP settings","locale":"en"},"7494":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#modules","content":"If a module fails, its card shows the error and whether an automatic restart is pending. Choose **Restart** to retry immediately.","locale":"en"},"7495":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Language\" href=\"/docs/settings-language\" description=\"Follow the system language, or choose Chinese or English.\" />","locale":"en"},"7496":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Appearance\" href=\"/docs/settings-appearance\" description=\"Configure the theme, accent color, and wallpaper.\" />","locale":"en"},"7497":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Paths\" href=\"/docs/settings-paths\" description=\"Manage the cache, default installation directory, and managed runtime storage.\" />","locale":"en"},"7498":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Network and Proxy\" href=\"/docs/settings-network\" description=\"Use the system proxy, a manual proxy, or no proxy.\" />","locale":"en"},"7499":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Mirrors\" href=\"/docs/settings-mirrors\" description=\"Configure package, code, and model download sources.\" />","locale":"en"},"7500":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Runtime\" href=\"/docs/settings-runtime\" description=\"Inspect the application's Python, Micromamba, and Git.\" />","locale":"en"},"7501":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Environment Tools\" href=\"/docs/settings-environment-tools\" description=\"Configure uv, environment checks, and CUDA memory optimization.\" />","locale":"en"},"7502":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"API Servers\" href=\"/docs/settings-api-servers\" description=\"Inspect background service status, health checks, and automatic restarts.\" />","locale":"en"},"7503":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"MCP Server\" href=\"/docs/settings-mcp-server\" description=\"Let other AI tools manage your instances, with the access you give each one.\" />","locale":"en"},"7504":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-32","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Logs\" href=\"/docs/settings-logs\" description=\"Control log levels, file rotation, and retention.\" />","locale":"en"},"7505":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-33","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"WebView\" href=\"/docs/settings-webview\" description=\"Control page retention, shared browsing data, new windows, and downloads.\" />","locale":"en"},"7506":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-34","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Agent\" href=\"/docs/settings-agent\" description=\"Configure models, permissions, tools, MCP, Skills, and memory.\" />","locale":"en"},"7507":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-35","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Diagnostics\" href=\"/docs/settings-diagnostics\" description=\"Generate, inspect, and export application diagnostic bundles.\" />","locale":"en"},"7508":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-36","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Automation\" href=\"/docs/settings-automation\" description=\"Switch automatic application update checks and daily instance snapshots and checks on or off.\" />","locale":"en"},"7509":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-37","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"Extensions\" href=\"/docs/settings-extensions\" description=\"Install, turn on, update, and uninstall application extensions.\" />","locale":"en"},"7510":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-38","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"<Card title=\"About and Updates\" href=\"/docs/settings-about-updates\" description=\"View the version and check for application updates.\" />","locale":"en"},"7511":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-39","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"When unsure whether a setting needs to change, keep the default. During troubleshooting, change only one relevant setting at a time and decide whether to retain it after retrying.","locale":"en"},"7512":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","type":"page","content":"Task Center","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Workspace"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/task-center","locale":"en"},"7513":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center-0","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/task-center","content":"Inspect the status, output, and errors of application and instance tasks, cancel tasks, and manage WebUI downloads.","locale":"en"},"7514":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center-1","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/task-center#open-task-center","content":"Open Task Center","locale":"en"},"7515":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center-2","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/task-center#tasks","content":"Tasks","locale":"en"},"7516":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center-3","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/task-center#the-task-list","content":"The task list","locale":"en"},"7517":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center-4","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/task-center#task-detail","content":"Task detail","locale":"en"},"7518":{"id":"/en/docs/task-center-5","page_id":"/en/docs/task-center","type":"heading","tags":[]