":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#before-importing","content":"The Python directory should be the root of a standalone Python installation, not a regular virtual environment that contains only activation scripts. Hanafubuki must find `python.exe` on Windows, or `bin/python3` or `bin/python` on Linux and macOS, and the executable must pass a version check.","locale":"en"},"8051":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#before-importing","content":"If you have only WebUI Core and no suitable Python, do not force an import. Use Scan the\nSystem. A recognized Core becomes an instance awaiting installation, and\nHanafubuki then prepares managed Python for it.","locale":"en"},"8052":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#select-the-import-source","content":"On Home, select **Add instance**, then switch the source at the top to **Import existing instance**.","locale":"en"},"8053":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#select-the-correct-webui-type","content":"Select the type used by the existing project. This determines launch arguments and management features; Hanafubuki does not convert one WebUI into another.","locale":"en"},"8054":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#set-the-name-and-root-directory","content":"You may leave the instance name blank to generate one automatically. **Existing instance root** must be an existing directory.","locale":"en"},"8055":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-30","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#confirm-the-python-directory-if-the-type-requires-it","content":"For a standard layout, leave it blank to use `<root>/python`. If Python is elsewhere, select its actual root. The application checks that it is usable before saving the record.","locale":"en"},"8056":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-31","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#confirm-the-core-directory","content":"For a standard layout, leave it blank to use `<root>/core`. If the existing root is itself WebUI Core, explicitly select the root as the Core directory.","locale":"en"},"8057":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-32","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#import-and-verify","content":"Select **Import instance**. The instance workspace opens. You can check the registered components under **Instance Management → Component Paths**.","locale":"en"},"8058":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Creates a Hanafubuki instance record and default launch arguments.","locale":"en"},"8059":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-34","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Leaves the existing root, Python, and Core in their original locations without copying or moving them.","locale":"en"},"8060":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-35","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Does not install or update Python packages, Core, extensions, or models as part of the import itself.","locale":"en"},"8061":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-36","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"A