n/docs/webui-install-options-78","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#python","content":"Changing the Python version does not reuse system Python. The application prepares a standalone runtime in the instance's Python directory. When importing an existing instance, the selected Python directory must likewise contain a working standalone Python.","locale":"en"},"8154":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-79","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"Stable Diffusion WebUI, ComfyUI, Fooocus, SD Trainer, Qwen TTS, RVC Next, and Mizuoto TTS use **PyTorch build**.","locale":"en"},"8155":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-80","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"InvokeAI uses the higher-level **Device family** option.","locale":"en"},"8156":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-81","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"**Automatic** leaves the build unpinned so that the current installer can choose for the environment.","locale":"en"},"8157":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-82","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"Pin an option manually only when you know the GPU driver, CUDA, ROCm, or CPU requirements.","locale":"en"},"8158":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-83","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"Selecting an incompatible build manually may let installation succeed while leaving the GPU unavailable at startup.","locale":"en"},"8159":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-84","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#branches","content":"Stable Diffusion WebUI, Fooocus, and SD Trainer can select a branch preset returned by the installation catalog. Stable Diffusion WebUI resolves **Default branch** to `sd_webui_forge_neo`; the Fooocus and SD Trainer defaults add no override. A selected branch becomes the baseline for later instance reinstallation and version management.","locale":"en"},"8160":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-85","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#branches","content":"For the repository, branch, and submodules behind each preset, see Supported variants.","locale":"en"},"8161":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-86","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Each predownload option has three states:","locale":"en"},"8162":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-87","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Selection","locale":"en"},"8163":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-88","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"8164":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-89","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Use installer default","locale":"en"},"8165":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-90","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Do not force enablement or disablement; let the cur