n","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#review-advanced-options","content":"Review advanced options","locale":"en"},"8395":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-9","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#create-and-install","content":"Create and install","locale":"en"},"8396":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-10","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#wait-for-automatic-startup","content":"Wait for automatic startup","locale":"en"},"8397":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-11","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"Default directory layout","locale":"en"},"8398":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-12","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","content":"A new installation creates an instance record and installs the components required by the selected type. Built-in WebUIs use standalone Python and a Core directory. Retain all default options the first time you use it.","locale":"en"},"8399":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-13","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#open-the-add-instance-page","content":"Select **Add instance** on Home and confirm that the instance source at the top is **New installation**. Select **Back to Home** or **Cancel** to exit without creating any files.","locale":"en"},"8400":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-14","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#select-a-webui-type","content":"Select the type to install on the left. The list includes the built-in WebUIs and types from enabled extensions that support new installations. Your choice determines which fields appear next and which management features are available after installation.","locale":"en"},"8401":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-15","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#continue-to-configuration","content":"Select **Next**. The application loads the branch and PyTorch options if the selected type uses them. If loading fails, use **Reload options** without selecting the WebUI again.","locale":"en"},"8402":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-16","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#start-from-a-preset-optional","content":"**Preset** at the top lists the presets of the selected type: those an installed extension contributes and those you saved. Choosing one fills the form below with its values, which you can still change; **None** puts back the type's defaults. A preset can also set launch arguments, shown under the list, which the new instance starts with.","locale":"en"},"8403":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-17","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#start-from-a-preset-optional","content":"**Save as preset** keeps the current install options and leaves secret fields for you to fill in again. You can delete presets you saved yourself. A preset that no longer fits its type shows why it is unavailable. Removing a preset leaves existing instances as configured. Instances of an extension-provided type still need that extension enabled.","locale":"en"},"8404":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-18","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#start-from-a-preset-optional","content":"If the form reports unusable presets, expand the details for their names and reasons. Select **Remove yours** and confirm to clear your unusable saved presets together. Extension-provided presets are managed by the extension that supplies them.","locale":"en"},"8405":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-19","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#set-the-instance-name","content":"**Instance name** is shown on Home and in Instance Management. You may leave it blank, in which case the application generates a name from the WebUI product name with a random suffix.","locale":"en"},"8406":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-20","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#confirm-the-installation-root","content":"Leaving **Installation root** blank is recommended. The application uses the global default directory shown in Settings and creates a dedicated directory named with the instance ID beneath it.","locale":"en"},"8407":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-21","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#confirm-the-installation-root","content":"If you select a directory manually, that directory itself becomes the final instance root; another nested directory is not created automatically. Use a new, dedicated directory. Do not select a drive root, your home directory, or an existing directory containing important files.","locale":"en"},"8408":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-22","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#select-a-branch","content":"**Branch** appears only for WebUIs that support branch presets. Most users should select **Default branch**. Switch only when you specifically need a prerelease or variant. See Supported variants for each variant's repository and branch.","locale":"en"},"8409":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-23","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#review-advanced-options","content":"Expand **Advanced options** to change the Python/Core subdirectories, Python version, PyTorch build, and predownload settings. The defaults already form a working installation plan; do not change an option you do not understand.","locale":"en"},"8410":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#review-advanced-options","content":"The installer requires Python inside the instance root. Core also defaults to a directory inside the root. If you select an existing Core elsewhere, the installer may update its files. The new instance owns that Core, so a later forced rebuild or full deletion can delete its directory. Use Scan the System if you are unsure where your Core is located.","locale":"en"},"8411":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#create-and-install","content":"Select **Create and install**. The application first saves the instance record, then opens that instance's installation workspace and prepares Python and WebUI Core in sequence. Do not manually move or delete directories during installation.","locale":"en"},"8412":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#wait-for-automatic-startup","content":"After installation, the workspace continues preparing management services and starts WebUI automatically. You can use it once a startup address is captured. If startup requires a PyTorch decision or dependency-conflict resolution, the workspace displays the corresponding decision.","locale":"en"},"8413":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"Each WebUI determines its own model, extension, and output directories, so they do not necessarily share one location. Before changing advanced settings, read Installation Options in Detail.","locale":"en"},"8414":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"In rare cases, the instance record is created but the installation task cannot start. The instance\nis not lost: reopen it and select **Start installation** in the workspace to continue.","locale":"en"},"8415":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"If installation fails or progress does not change for a long time, see Installation Progress and Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"8416":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"page","content":"Scan for Existing WebUIs","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","WebUI Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","locale":"en"},"8417":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-0","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","content":"Scan the computer or a selected folder to discover and attach existing WebUIs automatically.","locale":"en"},"8418":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-1","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#two-scan-scopes","content":"Two scan scopes","locale":"en"},"8419":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-2","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#scan-steps","content":"Scan steps","locale":"en"},"8420":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-3","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#select-scan-system","content":"Select Scan system","locale":"en"},"8421":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-4","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-and-confirm-the-scan-scope","content":"Review and confirm the scan scope","locale":"en"},"8422":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-5","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#return-to-home-and-wait","content":"Return to Home and wait","locale":"en"},"8423":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-6","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-the-completion-summary","content":"Review the completion summary","locale":"en"},"8424":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-7","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#handle-instances-awaiting-installation","content":"Handle instances awaiting installation","locale":"en"},"8425":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-8","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"What the summary results mean","locale":"en"},"8426":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-9","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#why-an-instance-was-not-found","content":"Why an instance was not found","locale":"en"},"8427":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-10","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","content":"Scanning is appropriate when you do not know an instance's path, or when only WebUI Core exists without a usable standalone Python. Scanning identifies the WebUI type from marker files in its directory, so you do not need to select a type first.","locale":"en"},"8428":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-11","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","content":"To find an extension-provided type, enable its extension before starting the scan. When the scanner recognizes the type’s directory markers and validates the required components, the app adds a ready instance. This also works for types that can only be attached by scanning. Deleting the instance preserves any component the scan rule explicitly marks as external.","locale":"en"},"8429":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-12","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#two-scan-scopes","content":"Select **Scan system** on the **Add instance** page. Windows scans fixed disks on the computer;\nLinux and macOS scan the current filesystem beginning at the system root. A full scan may read\nmany directories and take several minutes.","locale":"en"},"8430":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-13","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#two-scan-scopes","content":"Drag a folder from the file manager onto Hanafubuki Home to scan only that directory. This is\nfaster when WebUI resides on an external disk, in a mounted directory, or near a known location,\nand it more easily avoids full-system scan-scope limitations.","locale":"en"},"8431":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-14","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#select-scan-system","content":"Select **Add instance** on Home, then switch to **Scan system**. This mode has no WebUI type list or second-step configuration form.","locale":"en"},"8432":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-15","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-and-confirm-the-scan-scope","content":"Selecting **Scan this computer** opens a confirmation window describing the estimated duration, automatic-add behavior, and background execution. A full-system scan starts only after confirmation.","locale":"en"},"8433":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-16","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#return-to-home-and-wait","content":"The page returns to Home while scanning continues in the background. The bottom status report first shows directories read and candidates found, then shows the number processed during the attachment stage.","locale":"en"},"8434":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-17","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-the-completion-summary","content":"The completion report lists counts for added, awaiting installation, already existing, and skipped items. Scanning does not ask for confirmation on each candidate; qualifying projects appear on Home automatically.","locale":"en"},"8435":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-18","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#handle-instances-awaiting-installation","content":"If only Core is found without usable Python, the instance displays **Not installed**. Open it and select **Start installation**. The application prepares Python in a new managed instance root while continuing to use the discovered external Core.","locale":"en"},"8436":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-19","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#handle-instances-awaiting-installation","content":"Scanning and attachment only read existing files and write instance records. Installing an\ninstance that is **Awaiting installation** runs the complete installer against the discovered Core\nand may download, update, or adjust its files. Back up custom code first.","locale":"en"},"8437":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-20","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"8438":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-21","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"8439":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-22","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Next step","locale":"en"},"8440":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-23","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Added","locale":"en"},"8441":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-24","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"The required components for the type were found and attached, and the instance is ready","locale":"en"},"8442":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-25","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Open the instance and verify startup","locale":"en"},"8443":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Awaiting installation","locale":"en"},"8444":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"A built-in WebUI Core was recognized without a unique, usable standalone Python","locale":"en"},"8445":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Open the instance and start installation","locale":"en"},"8446":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Already exists","locale":"en"},"8447":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-30","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"The same Core is already managed by an instance","locale":"en"},"8448":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-31","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Use the existing instance; do not add it again","locale":"en"},"8449":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-32","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Skipped","locale":"en"},"8450":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"The candidate did not meet a condition during attachment or validation","locale":"en"},"8451":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-34","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Open Task Center for the exact reason","locale":"en"},"8452":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-35","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Detailed Task Center results may also include:","locale":"en"},"8453":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-36","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Path conflict**: The candidate root, Python, or Core overlaps an existing instance.","locale":"en"},"8454":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-37","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Invalid Python**: A possible Python was found, but it could not execute or its version could not be parsed.","locale":"en"},"8455":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-38","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Access warning**: A subdirectory could not be read; scanning continues with other directories.","locale":"en"},"8456":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-39","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Root failure**: The selected scan root itself could not be read. The entire scan fails if every root fails.","locale":"en"},"8457":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-40","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Processing failure**: Path safety, instance-record, or lifecycle-commit steps did not complete.","locale":"en"},"8458":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-41","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#why-an-instance-was-not-found","content":"Scanning recognizes only currently supported directory markers and deliberately skips symbolic links and Windows reparse points. On Unix systems, a full-system scan does not cross into another filesystem, so scan an external disk or certain mount directories by dragging in the folder. Highly customized layouts may also prevent Python from being associated automatically; in that case, import the instance manually.","locale":"en"},"8459":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-42","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#why-an-instance-was-not-found","content":"Open Task Center to inspect scan paths, warnings, and exact results. If the cause remains unclear, see Installation Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"8460":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"page","content":"Restore from a Snapshot","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","WebUI Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","locale":"en"},"8461":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-0","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","content":"Create and rebuild a new WebUI instance from an environment snapshot JSON file.","locale":"en"},"8462":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-1","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#obtain-the-snapshot-file","content":"Obtain the snapshot file","locale":"en"},"8463":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-2","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Compatibility checks before restoration","locale":"en"},"8464":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-3","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#create-the-restored-instance","content":"Create the restored instance","locale":"en"},"8465":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-4","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-snapshot-restoration","content":"Select snapshot restoration","locale":"en"},"8466":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-5","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-webui-type","content":"Select the WebUI type","locale":"en"},"8467":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-6","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#set-the-name-and-root","content":"Set the name and root","locale":"en"},"8468":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-7","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#confirm-python-and-core","content":"Confirm Python and Core","locale":"en"},"8469":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-8","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-snapshot-json","content":"Select the snapshot JSON","locale":"en"},"8470":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-9","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#restore-and-install","content":"Restore and install","locale":"en"},"8471":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-10","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#verify-and-restore-user-data","content":"Verify and restore user data","locale":"en"},"8472":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-11","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"What a snapshot does and does not include","locale":"en"},"8473":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-12","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","content":"An environment snapshot records recoverable information such as the WebUI type, Python, packages, Core commit, and extensions. It is suitable for recreating an environment or migrating its configuration, but it is not a complete backup of models, outputs, and all user files.","locale":"en"},"8474":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-13","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#obtain-the-snapshot-file","content":"In the original instance, open **Instance Management → Snapshots** and select **Create snapshot**. The resulting JSON is located at:","locale":"en"},"8475":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-14","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#obtain-the-snapshot-file","content":"After creation, expand the details to confirm the WebUI type, Python version, packages, extensions, and Core commit. To migrate to another device, copy this JSON yourself along with models, outputs, configuration, and custom files.","locale":"en"},"8476":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-15","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Restoring a new instance validates the snapshot before creating its record:","locale":"en"},"8477":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-16","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"8478":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-17","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Requirement","locale":"en"},"8479":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-18","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"File","locale":"en"},"8480":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-19","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"A valid JSON file no larger than 64 MiB","locale":"en"},"8481":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-20","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Snapshot format","locale":"en"},"8482":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-21","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"A currently supported environment snapshot format version","locale":"en"},"8483":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-22","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"WebUI type","locale":"en"},"8484":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-23","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Must match the type selected on the creation page","locale":"en"},"8485":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-24","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Python","locale":"en"},"8486":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-25","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"CPython with a major and minor version supported by the application","locale":"en"},"8487":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Platform","locale":"en"},"8488":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"The Windows, macOS, or Linux platform must be compatible with the current system","locale":"en"},"8489":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"A snapshot does not automatically convert a Python environment across platforms or turn it into another WebUI type.","locale":"en"},"8490":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-snapshot-restoration","content":"Select **Add instance** on Home, then switch the source to **Restore from snapshot**.","locale":"en"},"8491":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-30","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-webui-type","content":"Select the built-in WebUI that produced the snapshot. This mode lists only types that support creating an instance from a snapshot. If the type of an existing installation can only be attached by scanning, use Scan the system. On submission, the app also checks the type recorded in the JSON.","locale":"en"},"8492":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-31","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#set-the-name-and-root","content":"You may leave the name blank. Leave the installation root blank or select a new, dedicated directory. A manually selected directory is the final instance root.","locale":"en"},"8493":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-32","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#confirm-python-and-core","content":"A standard restoration retains the default `<instance root>/python` and `<instance root>/core`. Do not target an existing Core that contains important, unbacked-up changes.","locale":"en"},"8494":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-snapshot-json","content":"Under **Snapshot JSON file**, select the file from the original instance's `snapshots` directory. During instance creation, the original file is read and stored as managed recovery data for the current instance.","locale":"en"},"8495":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-34","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#restore-and-install","content":"Select **Restore and install**. The application prepares the Python version recorded in the snapshot, then restores WebUI Core, packages, and extensions.","locale":"en"},"8496":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-35","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#verify-and-restore-user-data","content":"After completion, check versions, extensions, and component paths, then confirm that WebUI starts. Finally, separately copy or reconfigure models, outputs, workflows, and custom files that the snapshot did not include.","locale":"en"},"8497":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-36","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#verify-and-restore-user-data","content":"Restoration removes packages and extensions absent from the snapshot and force-resets the target\nWebUI and extension Git repositories. Uncommitted code changes in the target directory may be\nlost, so prefer an empty directory.","locale":"en"},"8498":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-37","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Usually recorded","locale":"en"},"8499":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-38","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Not stored as a complete file copy","locale":"en"},"8500":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-39","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Python version and packages","locale":"en"},"8501":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-40","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"The Python installation directory itself","locale":"en"},"8502":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-41","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"WebUI type and Core commit","locale":"en"},"8503":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-42","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Models and large resource files","locale":"en"},"8504":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-43","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Recognized extensions and their versions","locale":"en"},"8505":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-44","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Generated results and user output","locale":"en"},"8506":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-45","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Some system and environment information","locale":"en"},"8507":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-46","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"Every configuration, script, workflow, and external directory","locale":"en"},"8508":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-47","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"To restore the current instance to an earlier state within the same instance, use **Instance Management → Snapshots → Restore**, which previews changes first. This page describes creating a new instance from JSON.","locale":"en"},"8509":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-48","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"For type, platform, or installation errors, continue with Installation Progress and Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"8510":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","type":"page","content":"WebUI Tabs","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Workspace"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","locale":"en"},"8511":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-0","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","content":"Switch between, open, and close WebUIs from the tab manager in the title bar, and move between the pages of one instance.","locale":"en"},"8512":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-1","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#open-the-tab-manager","content":"Open the tab manager","locale":"en"},"8513":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-2","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"The tab list","locale":"en"},"8514":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-3","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#several-pages-in-one-instance","content":"Several pages in one instance","locale":"en"},"8515":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-4","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#swit