s","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Select the close button on the row, or press `Delete`","locale":"en"},"8544":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Closes the page; the WebUI keeps running in the background","locale":"en"},"8545":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-34","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Stop WebUI","locale":"en"},"8546":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-35","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Right-click the tab and choose “Stop WebUI”","locale":"en"},"8547":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-36","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Ends the WebUI process, the same as stopping it from the instance","locale":"en"},"8548":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-37","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"New tab","locale":"en"},"8549":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-38","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Select “New tab” at the bottom of the panel","locale":"en"},"8550":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-39","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Pick an instance that has no tab yet; it is launched first if needed","locale":"en"},"8551":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-40","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Keyboard: `↑` `↓` move between rows, `Home` `End` jump to the first and last, `Enter` or Space switches, `Delete` or Backspace closes.","locale":"en"},"8552":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-41","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#the-tab-list","content":"Closing a tab only closes the page inside the application. The WebUI process keeps running and\nkeeps its VRAM and port; reopening the tab loads the same WebUI. Use “Stop WebUI” to end the\nprocess.","locale":"en"},"8553":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-42","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#several-pages-in-one-instance","content":"Some WebUIs serve more than one page on separate ports. SD Trainer Next, for example, has a separate training monitor alongside its main page. Such an instance is still one tab, and its pages are listed beneath it:","locale":"en"},"8554":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-43","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#several-pages-in-one-instance","content":"The tab row shows “N pages”, with one row per page below it showing a name, address, and state.","locale":"en"},"8555":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-44","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#several-pages-in-one-instance","content":"The first page is the one the WebUI opened first and is labelled “Main”; the others are labelled “Page 2”, “Page 3” in the order they appeared.","locale":"en"},"8556":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-45","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#several-pages-in-one-instance","content":"Launching the instance or entering its workspace shows the main page. A page that appears later never takes over the one on screen.","locale":"en"},"8557":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-46","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#switch-to-another-page","content":"Open the tab manager and select the page row under the instance. A page that has not been opened yet is loaded at this point.","locale":"en"},"8558":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-47","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#go-back-and-forth","content":"Open the manager again and select the other page. Pages already opened stay in the background, so switching does not reload them and unsubmitted input and scroll position are kept.","locale":"en"},"8559":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-48","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#close-a-page-you-no-longer-need","content":"Select the close button on a background page's row to close it on its own and free memory. Selecting the row later loads it again. The page currently showing cannot be closed on its own; it closes with its tab.","locale":"en"},"8560":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-49","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#close-a-page-you-no-longer-need","content":"When you leave a workspace and return, you see the page you were looking at before you left. “Reload WebUI” and “Open in external browser” in the title bar act on the page currently showing.","locale":"en"},"8561":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-50","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#close-a-page-you-no-longer-need","content":"Built-in WebUIs report their addresses at startup. SD Trainer Next opens its monitor automatically\non Windows. On other systems, use the link inside the WebUI. An extension type can also declare a\nrunning service as a workspace page, which can open as soon as the service is ready. An instance\ntype that provides no WebUI page can still run without a tab to switch to.","locale":"en"},"8562":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-51","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Situation","locale":"en"},"8563":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-52","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"8564":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-53","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Switching to another instance or workspace","locale":"en"},"8565":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-54","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Kept by default; closed when the keep pages setting is turned off","locale":"en"},"8566":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-55","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Switching between pages of the same instance","locale":"en"},"8567":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-56","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Always kept, regardless of that setting","locale":"en"},"8568":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-57","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"Launching that instance's WebUI again","locale":"en"},"8569":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-58","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"All of the old pages close and the new launch opens fresh","locale":"en"},"8570":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-59","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"The WebUI stops or exits","locale":"en"},"8571":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-60","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"All of that instance's pages close and the tab disappears","locale":"en"},"8572":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs-61","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-tabs#when-pages-are-kept-or-closed","content":"With “Keep the WebUI page when leaving its workspace” turned off there is only ever one tab at a time. The panel says so and links to the setting.","