Every method and its params are in the Interface Reference and the backend protocol reference."],[5353,"A backend never writes anything but the protocol to stdout. In Rust, log with `eprintln!`; the\nPython SDK moves `sys.stdout` to stderr, so a `print` goes to the log instead of breaking a frame."],[5532,"A backend on the Rust SDK can also be tested without a process, with `run_on(handler, reader, writer)` over in-memory streams. A Python backend can be run as a subprocess with the unpacked Python SDK on its `PYTHONPATH` and spoken to with protocol frames."],[4820,"A backend runs with the user's rights. The manifest's permissions only gate which host API methods\nit may call; a native program can still use the network and the filesystem directly. Do not rely\non permissions to confine your own code, and do not let users believe they do."],[7851,"A backend task or child process is still working"],[4894,"A backend that does not announce `migrate` is updated without one: announcing it is how a backend says its data needs migrating. The replaced version is held in memory only until the new version's first start, so an application restart before then loses the `migrate` call."],[5691,"A backend that lists the hook `ui` in `initialize`'s `hooks` has one UI state: a JSON value its panels and frames show, which it pushes whenever it changes, so nothing polls it. A backend that does not list `ui` is unaffected."],[5388,"A backend that provides an instance type: it checks the values, answers the install plan and the launch command, and logs a line from its `activate` hook."],[5391,"A backend with a UI state returns its `Ui` from `Handler::ui`, and pushes each new state with `Host::emit_state`:"],[4973,"A backend with management read access can call `get_app_runtime_status` through `tools.call` with `{\"runtime\":\"mirrors\"}` to read the model download source (`modelSource`) and the Micromamba mirror preference (`useMicromamba`)."],[5685,"A block of a kind this version of the application does not know says in its place that it can't be shown, and the rest of the panel works; raise `engines` when a panel needs a newer kind."],[4542,"A blocking question temporarily replaces the input. Choose an option, write your own answer, or skip it to continue the planning turn. A card labeled **Optional questions** can be answered later while the Agent continues working."],[7995,"A browser or the embedded page has opened the WebUI interface."],[8444,"A built-in WebUI Core was recognized without a unique, usable standalone Python"],[5871,"A button for an operation of a backend-provided type's own takes its label from `ext.<extension id>.operations.<operation>`, or shows the operation's name without one."],[4970,"A caller whose manifest does not depend on the target, or a method the target does not export, gets `PERMISSION_DENIED`."],[7130,"A card with an update shows **Update available**, and its Update button reads **Update to** that version; the marketplace entry shows the same button. Either one runs the one-click update above."],[6954,"A check you start from the instance card while that instance is being snapshotted waits for the snapshot. The card shows **Waiting for snapshot…** until the check begins."],[7253,"A client added with an earlier version of the application, before tokens were kept, has only a fingerprint of its token stored: its row says its token can't be shown, and **Show token** explains why. It keeps working with the token it has. To get a token you can show again, revoke the client and add it again."],[7250,"A client can read your instances and their tasks. Within the access you give it, it can also\nstart, change, install into or delete them. Its token works for any program that has it, so keep\nit private, and add only tools you trust."],[7287,"A client that shows MCP resources lets you attach them to a conversation; otherwise ask the agent to read the `SKILL.md` resource of the `hanafubuki` server before it starts. If your agent has a Skill system of its own (Claude Code, Codex and others read the same `SKILL.md` format), you can download the Skill's folder and unpack it into it. The guide calls the server `hanafubuki`, the name the configurations above give it."],[4985,"A complete example"],[4547,"A complete, reviewable implementation plan delivered at the end of Plan mode"],[5058,"A component can declare `rebuildable`. This example offers a Node.js rebuild switch and hides the Core switch. By default, only `core` and `python` offer switches. Each switch starts off and applies to one install. External directories cannot be rebuilt."],[5053,"A component may set `defaultPath = \"assets/weights\"` to place it below the install root. Explicit component locations take precedence. Set `[terminal].cwd` to a component path such as `\"{component.core}/tools\"` for an instance terminal that opens in the CLI directory. The default is the core directory."],[6197,"A compressed copy of the same `.app`"],[5100,"A condition is `{ key = \"<field>\", equals = <value> }`, or several combined with `{ any = [...] }` or `{ all = [...] }`, and reads only declared fields."],[7572,"A configuration recovery is also listed when the Agent repairs one of its own files (`config.toml`, `providers.toml` or `mcp.toml`): the log names the file and each value it replaced. When the original could not be kept aside, the Agent uses the repaired values from memory and leaves the file untouched; the row then records an error, and the file accepts no changes until the Agent restarts."],[5931,"A copied installation puts each version in `extensions/<id>/<version>/` under the application's data directory. A development link reads the selected source directory in place. Both store persistent data in `extensions/<id>/data/` and settings in `extensions/<id>/settings.json`. These survive updates and reloads."],[8482,"A currently supported environment snapshot format version"],[5249,"A custom operation can accept input and ask for co