ching `.toml` or `.json` files; it must match at least one (see Presets)"],[6005,"A glob of instance type descriptors (such as `types/*.toml`), matching `.toml` or `.json` files; it must match at least one"],[7802,"A high-quality issue report should let someone who cannot see your screen reconstruct what happened. A single sentence such as “It won't start” or a screenshot of only the final dialog is rarely enough to determine whether the issue comes from the application, an instance, or WebUI."],[4872,"A hook is called only when `initialize`'s answer lists it in `hooks`; an unknown name there is ignored."],[6957,"A job already running on an instance finishes, and the instances it had not reached are skipped. A\nsnapshot is not stopped partway, so no incomplete snapshot is left behind."],[5004,"A JSON descriptor uses the same keys, such as `\"displayName\"` and `\"install\": { \"parameters\": [...], \"steps\": [...] }`."],[5195,"A launch field with `kind = \"select\"` may set `optionsSource = \"models\"` when its extension has a backend. Opening Launch for this instance requests its choices from `provider.launchOptions`. For example, return `{ \"options\": { \"models\": [\"a.gguf\", \"b.gguf\"] } }`. The management tool `get_instance_launch_options` lists the nonsecret choices for this instance by field key. Static options remain available. The host checks a newly selected dynamic value on save. A saved value can be kept when the backend is offline or the model has disappeared."],[5555,"A linked extension is never updated, and an id installed as a copy cannot also be linked, nor the reverse: uninstall the one to install the other. Uninstalling a link removes only what the application recorded; your folder stays as it is."],[7079,"A list of host names (`*.example.com` matches subdomains)"],[5680,"A list of models, each with its state and the buttons it offers:"],[6013,"A list of panels and frames, each as below"],[5421,"A list of steps"],[5259,"A list of steps, written as `install.steps` are, placeholders and all"],[5682,"A list row offers the actions its `actions` names, or all of the block's without it; a row without an `id` offers none. Pressing one calls `ui.panel.action` with `row`, the row's `id`, after asking its `confirm`."],[4735,"A long-running command can be moved to the background and assigned a terminal session identifier. It belongs to the Agent session that created it and does not end automatically when you collapse its tool card, switch sessions, or close the Agent window."],[6645,"A malformed snapshot displays a parsing error and cannot be restored directly. Deleting a snapshot permanently deletes only the corresponding snapshot file; it does not change the current environment."],[5878,"A manifest"],[5237,"A marker counts only when it is a regular file or directory reached without following a link. Paths are relative, `/`-separated, of ordinary names: `..`, a leading `/`, a backslash, or a drive is refused at registration."],[5240,"A match is imported as a ready instance of your type. A directory already managed is reported, never imported twice. Values the type refuses then (for a type a backend provides, `provider.validateSpec`), or a component missing on disk, make it a warning instead of an instance."],[5341,"A minimal example"],[5345,"A minimal example"],[7323,"A mirror may omit the latest commit, return a different file, or synchronize late. If an\ninstallation result is abnormal, retry from the official source and review task output. Do not\ndisable verification to accept a mismatched file."],[6661,"A mismatched type, missing Core, uncommitted repository changes, or another unresolved problem blocks restoration. Follow the instructions or enable the required options, then wait for the preview to be analyzed again automatically."],[7832,"A model or workflow has missing components or incompatible versions: contact the publisher and include the required dependency information."],[8398,"A new installation creates an instance record and installs the components required by the selected type. Built-in WebUIs use standalone Python and a Core directory. Retain all default options the first time you use it."],[5056,"A newly created instance owns its components. When the user selects an external directory in **Paths**, the host checks that the directory and the optional platform-specific executable exist. Discovery can also mark components external during import. The managed `python` component always belongs to the instance."],[7065,"A newly installed extension starts turned off; turn it on yourself. An extension that is already installed cannot be installed again: use **Update**. **Install** in the marketplace goes straight to the confirmation."],[5430,"A notice, or `None`"],[5436,"A notice, or `None`"],[5384,"A notification (an event, a process's output); runs on the loop's thread, so it returns quickly and never calls the application"],[5453,"A notification; runs on the loop's thread"],[5089,"A number's bounds and step; `min` not above `max`, `step` positive; a `slider` needs both `min` and `max`"],[5622,"A number's bounds and step; a `slider` needs both `min` and `max`"],[5927,"A package can omit `[backend]` when its contributions are files the host reads. For example, a data-only preset can supply defaults for an existing instance type. Instance types can still declare commands that run during installation or launch, and the Agent can start a declared stdio MCP server."],[5929,"A package is a directory with `hanafubuki-extension.toml` at its root. In an archive, the files may sit at the archive's root or inside one wrapping directory. Where everything else goes is up to the manifest; a common layout:"],[5690,"A panel action neither stops the instance nor holds its maintenance, so it must not change the instance's files. When it needs to, declare an operation of the type's own instead (see Types a backend provides)."],[5715,"A panel block names where its data comes from:"],[5646,"A panel has an `id`, a `title`, and `blocks`. Panel and frame IDs must be unique across the extension, even when contributed to different slots. Each block has a `kind`, an `id` unique within its panel (letters A–Z or a–z, digits, `_`, or `-`), and an optional `title`. Action IDs are shared across all `actions` and `list` blocks in that panel."],[5507,"A panel in Settings: a **Greet** action and a table of the greetings sent, shown from the UI state (`\"source\": \"state\"`)"],[5709,"A panel with state-backed blocks reads `ui.state` when it opens, when the backend restarts, and after each push, so keep this method cheap. A frame page reads its initial snapshot by calling `state()` itself and listens for pushes with `onState(listener)`. Calling `ready()` starts the handshake and reports the page height. Both `ui.state` and `ui.call` have a 10 s bound."],[6026,"A panel's JSON file"],[6011,"A pattern naming each language's file with exactly one `{locale}` in its file name, such as `locales/{locale}.json`"],[5274,"A preset is a set of defaults over one instance type, which the new installation page lists under that type: choosing it fills the form, and the user can still change every value. Every `.toml` or `.json` file the manifest's `contributes.presets` glob matches is one preset, whose id is `<extension id>:<id>`, such as `com.example.greeter:morning`. Its base type can be one of your extension's types, another extension's, or a built-in one."],[5499,"A preset over the `greeter` type: the new installation page lists it under Greeter and fills the greeting with it"],[5066,"A program on the system; `name` is a program name without a path separator"],[7036,"A program that runs in the background while the extension is on and supplies data and actions for the above"],[5918,"A program that runs while the extension is on and talks to the application over its stdin and stdout"],[4552,"A proposed plan should leave no key implementation decisions unresolved for the executor. A task plan only describes the progress of current work. Even if a step is marked **In progress**, that does not mean its command succeeded or a risky operation was approved."],[4960,"A provider callback’s `instance` contains `id` and a `components` map. For example, `instance.components.core.path` is the current native path for `core`, and `external: true` marks a user-owned directory. Read that path to inspect a component and use `{component.core}` in a returned plan. `provider.validateSpec` receives this object when an existing instance is reinstalled with new values. Creation has no instance yet."],[4765,"A provider describes only the server connection. The model is selected separately in the model policy. After saving the provider, select the default provider and model."],[7712,"A proxy determines *how to connect*; a mirror determines *which source to connect to*. First compare proxy and direct connections, then adjust the relevant mirror. Changing several settings at once makes the result impossible to interpret."],[5469,"A Python handler overrides `diagnostics_collect`; the SDK announces the `diagnostics` hook automatically:"],[7901,"A Python traceback begins with `Traceback (most recent call last):` and lists the call path. The final unindented exception type and description are often the best search terms, for example:"],[4759,"A recommended task format"],[4769,"A regular new conversation uses the default workspace. Create the conversation inside a project to use its selected folders. Type `/pwd` to check the current working directory. Projects and workspaces"],[7854,"A request was sent, but a terminal state is not confirmed"],[5941,"A reverse-DNS id: two or more labels of `a-z`, `0-9`, and `-`, joined by `.`, at most 128 bytes. It names the extension's store directory, the namespace of its instance types, and the prefix of its text keys"],[6355,"A running WebUI does not restart automatically when its configuration changes. Stop the instance first s