 log. The same `ImportError` can originate in Core, an extension, or a user script. Use the actual file path in the traceback to tell them apart."],[7540,"Error notices from interface actions; they have no output and cannot be cancelled"],[7539,"Errors"],[4593,"Even when their targets look reasonable, manually confirm the scope and recovery method for:"],[5297,"Event topics"],[7246,"Every built-in tool is listed with what it may do in the tool reference, which the server also serves to clients (below). Long operations, such as an installation, return a task to follow: the client reads its progress and log the way you do in the Task Center. Instance types are named by their id, such as `builtin:comfyui`, so a client can create an instance of any type you have, an extension's included."],[7282,"Every change a client asked for appears in the **Task Center** with the kind **MCP client**, named after the client and what it did: completed, failed with its error, or cancelled with the reason (denied by you, not confirmed in time, or not allowed by its access). The Task Center keeps the latest 100 of these while the application runs; they are not kept after it quits. Reads are not listed one by one; each client's row on the settings card shows when it was last used."],[8507,"Every configuration, script, workflow, and external directory"],[6041,"Every descriptor the `instanceTypes` glob matches is a valid instance type (see Instance types); a `provider = \"backend\"` type requires a `[backend]`. Every preset the `presets` glob matches reads (see Presets)."],[6566,"Every instance has a root and a Core directory. Built-in WebUIs also have their own Python. Extension-provided types list the components they declare. Components can live outside the instance root. Full deletion checks which directories the instance owns."],[5284,"Every interface an extension can use - the frame protocol, the UI kit's classes, panel blocks and form fields, components, the host API, the application's calls on a backend, and the manifest and instance-type descriptor keys, and the management tools. Generated from the application's interface exports."],[6174,"Every link on the download page points to the project's release repositories on ModelScope and\nHugging Face. The page automatically selects the source that responds first. Do not download\ninstallers from third-party mirrors or reposts."],[5382,"Every other request: hooks, provider callbacks, panel and frame calls, service calls; `METHOD_NOT_FOUND` by default"],[5529,"every path in `[backend].command` has its program, with the executable bit kept on Linux and macOS;"],[5930,"Every path in the manifest is relative to the package root, separated by `/`, and contains no `..`, no backslash, and no root. Symbolic links in a package are never followed."],[4877,"Every start, after `initialize` (and `migrate`)"],[4711,"Every time the Agent starts, the application installs it again unless the installed copy is exactly the bundled one, so your edits to it are replaced. To change it, duplicate it under another name."],[7187,"Everyday use; preserves key phases and errors"],[7259,"Everything, but every change waits until you allow it in the main window"],[7584,"Evicted"],[4588,"Exact target: program, arguments, working directory, file path, or service identifier."],[5966,"Exactly one of `command` and `python`."],[4433,"Exclude external context"],[5304,"Executable motion examples"],[8189,"Executing the steps declared by the extension type. Open the log for their output."],[8041,"Existing instance root"],[8258,"Existing root, Core, and standalone Python are known"],[7349,"Exit normally and restart"],[7736,"Exits immediately after startup"],[6623,"Expand “Last reinstall” to check the selected build, executor status, and exit code. The app restarts the instance API and shows any restart error or post-restart compatibility result here. Refresh the page to confirm the installed build, then launch the WebUI to verify it in use."],[8409,"Expand **Advanced options** to change the Python/Core subdirectories, Python version, PyTorch build, and predownload settings. The defaults already form a working installation plan; do not change an option you do not understand."],[7858,"Expand the error and cleanup status"],[7696,"Expand the log in the installation workspace and record the current stage and the last normal\noutput."],[7766,"Expand the startup log and find the first complete exception before the process exited."],[8167,"Explicitly require the installer to perform the predownload"],[8169,"Explicitly require the installer to skip the predownload"],[4393,"Expose only selected tools from the server"],[4388,"Exposure"],[7568,"Extension"],[5873,"Extension Development Overview"],[6267,"Extension Management"],[7937,"Extension or node author"],[5305,"Extension presets"],[7015,"Extension settings, panels, and views"],[7912,"Extension, dependency, and version corresponding to the error path"],[7002,"Extensions"],[7017,"Extensions are packages installed into Hanafubuki itself. They can add instance types, settings sections, interface panels, and translated text to the application, and some also run a program of their own beside it, called a **backend**. Install and manage them in the **Extensions** section of the Settings window. Its **Installed** tab lists the extensions installed here. The row at the top of the tab, the search box with **Check for Updates** and **Install extension** beside it, stays in place while the list scrolls; the search finds extensions by name, ID, publisher, or description."],[6450,"Extensions can add management sections for their own instance types. The list omits features the type does not declare. If switching sections or instances opens **Save changes before leaving?**, choose **Save and leave** to apply edits, **Leave without saving** to discard them, or **Cancel** to stay in the form."],[6458,"Extensions, models, and snapshots"],[5214,"Extensions: the adopted type's extensions (`core/extensions`, or `core/custom_nodes` for ComfyUI)"],[7249,"External access is **off** by default. On **Settings › API Servers**, the **Management MCP server** card has the switch **Let added clients connect** (the same settings are under the module's **Settings** on the Modules page). While it is off, a client's token is refused as if it did not exist. Turning it on or off applies at once, without restarting the server, and turning it off also closes the connections clients have open."],[7452,"External browser"],[6191,"Extract and run; does not participate in in-app updates"],[6161,"Extract it and run the Launcher directly"],[6843,"Failed"],[7103,"Failed"],[7580,"Failed"],[7856,"Failed"],[8196,"Failed / Canceled"],[6388,"Failures and recovery"],[4795,"Faults"],[6054,"Field"],[6075,"Field"],[8083,"Field"],[7163,"Field reference"],[7478,"Field type"],[5787,"Fields"],[7415,"Fields"],[5636,"Fields of one group are submitted together"],[6801,"Fields show their effective source, application timing, and configuration issues. Reset removes the user's override."],[8479,"File"],[6571,"File boundary of the complete instance"],[6481,"File browser"],[6492,"File browser"],[7708,"File checksum or size mismatch"],[6429,"File deletion cannot be undone through Hanafubuki. If you pointed Core to an existing project on\nanother drive and want to keep all of its files, choose **Delete record only**."],[6973,"File logs and the in-memory log for the current run."],[4727,"File patches and summaries of added, modified, or deleted files."],[4570,"File reads, with writes and network access restricted"],[7081,"Files"],[7614,"Files a page generates inside the browser (`blob:` or `data:` addresses) are saved directly by the browser engine. They show only their result and cannot be paused, resumed, or cancelled. If the download directory already has a file with the same name, a number is added to the new file's name; nothing is overwritten."],[7458,"Files downloaded in a WebUI are saved to **WebUI download directory** under Paths, which defaults to the `downloads` folder inside the application data directory. When a file with the same name exists, a number is appended to the new file's name; existing files are never overwritten."],[5840,"Fill"],[6924,"Fills the window and may crop image edges"],[6928,"Fills the window exactly and may distort the image; **Image position** has no effect"],[6449,"Filter the instance list by name, type ID, or part of its installation path. The buttons below the list add an instance or scan for existing WebUIs. Up and Down in the instance list switch the detail view. In the section navigation, use the arrow keys to focus an icon and press `Enter` to open it. When a narrow window shows only icons, hover or move keyboard focus into the list to reveal the labels. When space permits, use the arrow at the bottom to keep the navigation expanded or collapsed."],[4458,"Find a keyword and return ids with line numbers"],[6117,"Find an instance on Home"],[7518,"Find the earliest failed task"],[7949,"Find the first failed task"],[6325,"Find the target feature in the form. Keep the default when you are unsure what a field means."],[7475,"Finding settings by section"],[7375,"Finish running instances, terminals, and maintenance tasks first, then exit the application normally. On restart, the startup page completes migration before loading other features."],[7961,"First expand the bottom-right status item on the current page, then open Task Center in the title bar. Select the earliest related failure instead of looking only at subsequent cascading failures."],[6155,"First launch"],[7199,"First reproduce the problem at the default **Info** level and inspect the direct error in the\ntask center."],[4753,"First use"],[7317,"First verify the connection method under **Network and Proxy** so you do not mistake a proxy\nproblem for a mirror problem."],[7947,"Five-minute troubleshooting flow"],[7193,"Focusing only on anomalies and potential problems"],[7057,"Folder"],[7811,"Follow the call path and determine whether each file belongs to Core, an extension, a custom\nnode, or a Python package."],[7145,"Follow the system language or choose a Chinese or English interface."],[3777,"Fooocus"],[3939,"Fooocus"],[4006,"Fooocus"],[8121,"Fooocus"],[8283,"Fooocus"],[8350,"Fooocus"],[8241,"Fooocus variants"],[3897,"Fooocus 变体"],[4014,"Fooocus-MRE"],[8358,"Fooocus-MRE"],[6896,"For a **Failed** server, rule out runtime-environment or port problems first, then click\n**Start**."],[6977,"For a module failure, compare the current state in `app/modules.json` with the fault history in `app/module-faults.json`. The Agent and its plugins report their status in `app/agent-status.json` and `app/agent-plugins.json`. An extension that provides diagnostics can include reports under `app/extensions/<extension-id>/`. If an item could not be collected, `manifest.json` records the reason. You can still inspect the files collected successfully."],[7776,"For a port conflict or connection failure:"],[6799,"For a read-only role, select **Copy to a user role** in the role entry before editing the copy. Under **Models → Role source files**, you can inspect the source path, edit a writable user role file, or create your own."],[8056,"For a standard layout, leave it blank to use `<root>/core`. If the existing root is itself WebUI Core, explicitly select the root as the Core directory."],[8055,"For a standard layout, leave it blank to use `<root>/python`. If Python is elsewhere, select its actual root. The application checks that it is usable before saving the record."],[4748,"For a test command, inspect the exit status and failed cases instead of relying on partial output."],[5189,"For a UI hosted below the root, set `webview = true` and\n`webviewPath = \"/dashboard/\"`. The readiness probe may use a separate path. Set `externalBrowserPath = \"/studio\"` to choose a different same-origin page for the title bar browser button.\nA role with `after = [\"api\"]` can pass `{endpoint.api}` in its command or\nenvironment. It resolves at start to the running API role's base URL, including\nthe allocated port."],[7717,"For access-denied errors, check whether the file is in use by WebUI, a terminal, an editor, security software, or another application process."],[7121,"For an extension whose author publishes its versions, **Update** on its card is one click: the application checks that extension now and, when it finds a newer version, downloads it, checks it against the digest its author published, and opens the confirmation. When there is none, the card says it is up to date, or why the check failed. While it works, the card's buttons wait."],[6177,"For another platform or format, select “Choose Manually” to open the full list, which includes\nfile names and sizes."],[5320,"For bounded UTF-8 requests, mirror-aware downloads and per-process proxy selection, see the SDK networking example. The entries below include their optional fields and defaults directly from the Rust contract; HTTP status codes are part of the response, while transport and permission failures are RPC errors."],[6991,"For built-in WebUIs, the PyTorch compatibility check runs before this step. Even with environment checks off, an incompatible result asks whether to continue. If compatibility cannot be determined, startup continues with a warning."],[8073,"For complete errors and startup output, use Task Center or Installation Troubleshooting."],[4599,"For deletions, confirm a backup or snapshot first. For external systems, verify the account, environment, and target object. For commands, verify the working directory and complete arguments."],[5282,"For descriptor defaults, conditional requirements and validation stages, see the instance-type descriptor reference."],[4979,"For documents about one instance, announce `diagnostics.collectInstance`. The host sends `{id}` for an instance of your extension’s type and writes the returned documents beneath that instance’s `extensions/<id>/` directory. Rust implements `InstanceDiagnostics` and returns it from `Handler::instance_diagnostics`. Python overrides `diagnostics_collect_instance(host, instance_id)`."],[6070,"For each release:"],[7247,"For example, a client can read the current managed runtime directories and call `preview_runtime_storage_migration` to check a destination and show where each component would move. You can start the move from Settings after reviewing the preview. For application updates, `get_app_update_status` reads the existing result. A fresh `check_app_update` may download and prepare an update. You install it and restart from the application. Built-in management tools and arguments"],[4809,"For extensions declaring `requirements`, at startup, enable, update, rollback and Retry, the host checks the declared file against package metadata in the extension’s own directory for the current Python release (for example, `data/python-packages/cp315/`). A new directory, missing distribution or incompatible version triggers a pip install. The Task Center shows the install and lets you cancel it. Check or installation errors prevent the backend from starting and give the reason."],[6114,"For field defaults, conditional requirements and validation stages, use the generated configuration reference. A JSON Schema `null` describes the JSON representation or omission behavior; TOML has no `null` literal. Do not copy it as `field = null`. A schema default and a domain effective default are shown separately; the website does not infer runtime values from nullable fields."],[5600,"For its calls"],[7060,"For local development. Choose the directory containing the manifest and check its path in the confirmation. The application reads it in place. Click **Reload** on the card after editing it. See Linking a folder while you work."],[7139,"For panels with forms or lists, fill in the fields or choose the action on the relevant row. Some actions ask for confirmation, and the panel refreshes its data after an action runs. An extension view in Instance Management can also request a reinstall of the current instance with different parameters. The confirmation names the instance and shows the changes. Once confirmed, the new values also apply to future installations."],[8160,"For the repository, branch, and submodules behind each preset, see Supported variants."],[8509,"For type, platform, or installation errors, continue with Installation Progress and Troubleshooting."],[8269,"For your first use, select **New installation** and retain the defaults. Select **Import existing\ninstance** when you already have a working standalone Python and WebUI. Use **Scan system** when\nyou have only a source directory or are unsure about its layout."],[6655,"Force Git reset"],[7870,"Force-ending a process from the system task manager may temporarily prevent Hanafubuki from confirming resource state. If force is unavoidable, save the logs first, then return to the original task and retry cleanup. Do not immediately delete the task record or instance directory."],[4473,"Fork"],[4345,"Fork before that message and restore it to the input for editing"],[4250,"Fork from the end of the currently committed session"],[4343,"Fork from the end of the currently committed session"],[4317,"Forking a session"],[4339,"Forking is useful when you want to preserve the current approach while trying another solution from a point in history."],[5059,"Form"],[5292,"Form fields"],[6181,"Format"],[6207,"Formats that do not participate in in-app updates can still check for updates. The app will offer a manual installer for the current platform instead."],[5810,"Forms"],[6033,"Frame and panel ids are unique within an extension."],[5289,"Frame client"],[5351,"Frame host operations and declarative Agent content"],[5287,"Frame messages"],[1227,"frame SDK 提供 `openSettings(section: string): Promise<void>` 与 `openExternal(url: string): Promise<void>`，分别封装 `open-settings` 和 `open-external` 宿主请求。未知 section、无效 URL 或宿主错误都会以 `FrameError` 结束 Promise，见 frame 示例。"],[1058,"Frame 安全工具"],[1107,"Frame 宿主操作与声明式 Agent 内容"],[5303,"Frame-safe utilities"],[5573,"Frames"],[5597,"Frames"],[5911,"Frames"],[5286,"Frontend"],[4578,"Full access"],[7264,"Full access"],[5735,"Function"],[6443,"General"],[6453,"General"],[7683,"Generate an application diagnostic bundle and include the startup failure stage, a screenshot of the runtime page, application logs, and recent changes. If the application cannot open the settings page at all, preserve the existing application data and avoid cleanup beyond reinstalling over the application until the maintainers confirm which files they need."],[7917,"Generate button does nothing while the process remains active"],[4431,"Generate memories"],[6959,"Generate, inspect, and export application-level diagnostic bundles."],[8505,"Generated results and user output"],[6960,"Generating application diagnostics"],[3077,"Git"],[7394,"Git"],[2455,"Git\n操作只管理代码仓库，不能保护模型、输出、配置或未提交代码。执行切换前应同时准备环境快照和独立文件备份。"],[6738,"Git operations manage only the code repository. They do not protect models, outputs,\nconfiguration, or uncommitted code. Prepare both an environment snapshot and a separate file\nbackup before switching."],[8218,"Git or Core download fails"],[7409,"Git waiting for Micromamba: let Micromamba finish preparing first; this is not an independent Git hang."],[2436,"Git 型 WebUI"],[3874,"Git 或 Core 下载失败"],[3088,"Git 来源同样在下次应用启动时生效。系统已经安装可用 Git 时通常保留默认选择；需要固定、隔离的 Git 环境时再选择 Micromamba。"],[3091,"Git 等待 Micromamba：先让 Micromamba 完成准备，这不是独立的 Git 卡死。"],[6719,"Git-based WebUIs"],[7310,"GitHub mirror"],[1823,"GitHub 仓库可以把所有文件作为 Release 的附件发布。GitHub 会在固定地址提供最新 Release 中名为 `latest.json` 的附件，因此清单只需写一次："],[3004,"GitHub 镜像"],[6921,"Glass blur"],[4419,"Global settings"],[6792,"Global settings control tool approvals and the command sandbox separately. In chat, open the permission menu beside the message box or type `/permissions` to see both and select a preset for the current session. **Read only** prevents commands from writing files. **Full access** disables the command sandbox and grants routine approvals. If the Windows sandbox needs setup, use the action in the menu or open its settings with `/setup-default-sandbox`."],[8516,"Go back and forth"],[4612,"Go to **Settings → Agent → Models → Providers**, or type `/providers` in chat, then add a provider."],[6586,"Goal"],[7437,"GPU acceleration (Linux)"],[7906,"GPU driver, instance PyTorch, and current platform combination"],[3119,"GPU 加速（Linux）"],[8275,"Gradio-based image-generation interface"],[5487,"Greeter is a complete sample extension, and you can download it. It is small, but it goes through the main paths an extension takes: a native backend on the Rust SDK, an instance type its backend provides, an install parameter, a preset that fills it, a server role the embedded browser opens, extension settings, a frame, a panel that follows the state its backend pushes, and text in two languages. The application's own tests build, install, and run it, and it is already a repository of its own, so it can start a new extension as it is."],[5518,"Greeter uses the same binary for its extension backend and its instance server. At instance start, the backend reads the user's saved signature, finds its own program with `std::env::current_exe()`, and returns a command that runs it with `serve`. For a server with a fixed command, a declarative type can also use `{extension.root}` to run a program or script from its package. See Placeholders."],[1243,"Greeter 是一个完整的示例扩展，可以下载。它很小，但覆盖了扩展的主要路径：基于 Rust SDK 的原生后端、由后端提供的实例类型、安装参数、填写该参数的预设、在内置浏览器中打开的服务器角色、扩展设置、视图、跟随后端推送状态的面板，以及中英文文字。应用自己的测试会构建、安装并运行它；它本身就是一个独立仓库，可以直接作为新扩展的起点。"],[1274,"Greeter 用同一个程序运行扩展后端和实例服务器。启动实例时，后端读取用户保存的署名，用 `std::env::current_exe()` 找到当前程序，再返回带有 `serve` 参数的启动命令。对于命令固定的服务器，声明式类型也可以用 `{extension.root}` 引用软件包中的程序或脚本。见占位符。"],[5783,"Group"],[5806,"Group"],[5834,"Group"],[7220,"Group"],[7537,"Group"],[1892,"Hanafubuki"],[6138,"Hanafubuki"],[8520,"Hanafubuki can keep several instances' WebUIs open at once. Each instance workspace with an open WebUI is one tab, and the “WebUI tabs” button in the title bar is where you manage them. The number on the button is how many tabs are open."],[7932,"Hanafubuki cannot install, start, or manage an instance"],[7829,"Hanafubuki cannot prepare the runtime, manage tasks, persist settings, or render a window: report it to Hanafubuki maintainers."],[6140,"Hanafubuki is a Tauri-based desktop manager for installing, importing, running, and maintaining local generative AI WebUIs. It brings Python, Git, launch arguments, models, extensions, snapshots, and diagnostics together in one place, and includes an Agent that can connect to local tools."],[6156,"Hanafubuki is available in two forms: an **installer** installs the app into your system, while the **portable package** is a Launcher that runs after extraction. Both are available from the download page, which automatically detects your current system."],[6147,"Hanafubuki is still under development and testing. Create snapshots or your own backups of\nimportant instances and configuration regularly."],[7933,"Hanafubuki maintainers"],[7846,"Hanafubuki retains ownership of tasks and processes until it confirms that the process has ended and its resources have been released. Therefore, **Cancellation requested**, a command producing no new output, and a closed window do not mean that task cleanup has completed."],[7339,"Hanafubuki synchronizes the effective proxy with running application and instance API servers. New child processes also use the new settings. An existing WebUI, command, or ordinary terminal keeps its startup environment. Restart that process if it needs the new proxy."],[7805,"Hanafubuki version, operating system, and hardware platform."],[7968,"Hanafubuki will not open normally, or application Python, Micromamba, or Git is not ready"],[1901,"Hanafubuki 仍在开发和测试中。重要实例和配置建议定期创建快照或自行备份。"],[3510,"Hanafubuki 会保留任务和进程的所有权，直到确认进程已经结束并释放资源。因此“已请求取消”“命令没有新输出”和“窗口已经关闭”都不等于任务已经清理完成。"],[4176,"Hanafubuki 可以同时打开多个实例的 WebUI。每个已打开 WebUI 的实例工作区是一个标签页，标题栏的“WebUI 标签页”按钮是管理它们的入口，按钮上的数字是当前打开的标签页数量。"],[1910,"Hanafubuki 提供两种获取方式：**安装包**把应用装进系统，**便携版**是一个解压即用的 Launcher。两者都在下载页提供，并且都会自动识别当前系统。"],[3493,"Hanafubuki 无法准备运行环境、管理任务、持久化设置或呈现窗口：提交给 Hanafubuki 维护者。"],[3588,"Hanafubuki 无法安装、启动或管理实例"],[3624,"Hanafubuki 无法正常打开，或应用 Python、Micromamba、Git 未就绪"],[1894,"Hanafubuki 是一个基于 Tauri 的桌面管理器，用来安装、导入、运行和维护本地生成式 AI WebUI。它统一管理 Python、Git、运行参数、模型、扩展、快照和诊断信息，并提供可连接本地工具的 Agent。"],[3472,"Hanafubuki 版本、操作系统和硬件平台。"],[3320,"Hanafubuki 的应用运行环境用于执行管理能力，与每个 WebUI 实例自己的 Python 和 Core 相互独立。先判断失败的是应用级运行时，还是某个实例内部依赖。"],[3589,"Hanafubuki 维护者"],[7640,"Hanafubuki's application runtime environment powers its management features and is independent of each WebUI instance's own Python and Core. First determine whether the failure is in the application-level runtime or in the dependencies of a specific instance."],[6563,"Handle a stale configuration warning"],[7840,"Handle cancellation, pending cleanup, maintenance locks, lingering terminals, and duplicate tasks."],[6606,"Handle failures"],[8424,"Handle instances awaiting installation"],[6524,"Handle launch decisions"],[4561,"Handling manual approval"],[3962,"Haoming02/sd-webui-forge-classic"],[3966,"Haoming02/sd-webui-forge-classic"],[8306,"Haoming02/sd-webui-forge-classic"],[8310,"Haoming02/sd-webui-forge-classic"],[6817,"Health checks and automatic restarts"],[6838,"Health checks have started failing, but the server is not yet confirmed stuck"],[7800,"Help request template"],[5081,"Help text"],[5618,"Help text"],[5795,"Helpers"],[4563,"High-risk operations"],[4780,"Higher permission only reduces approval steps; it does not make commands, file changes, or\nexternal actions inherently safe. Review the target, arguments, and risk notice before allowing an\noperation, then inspect the diff and test results afterward."],[7171,"Historical `.