ng Face 仓库与文件"],[3006,"Hugging Face 镜像"],[7894,"Identify model, extension, node, generation, and WebUI interface errors and find the appropriate issue tracker."],[7946,"Identify the layer where an error occurred, then follow the relevant resolution steps."],[5880,"Identity"],[6530,"Identity"],[6414,"If “Migration Requires Recovery” appears, the instance remains closed to protect file consistency.\nDo not manually move or delete the source, destination, or temporary directory. Select the\noriginal destination parent and choose “Migrate Instance” again to continue recovery."],[6132,"If a card says its type is unavailable, the instance record is still there. Check the extension providing its type under Extensions, or open the card's management menu to inspect the record. The **Hanafubuki documentation** card opens the guide in your system browser."],[6996,"If a CUDA allocator error occurs during startup, disable this option and relaunch the instance for comparison. Do not change PyTorch and several launch arguments at the same time."],[7652,"If a download or verification fails, check the network, proxy, mirrors, and system time."],[7494,"If a module fails, its card shows the error and whether an automatic restart is pending. Choose **Restart** to retry immediately."],[6797,"If a process plugin is waiting for a grant, open **Plugins → Package permissions**. Compare its requested network access, workspace access, and environment variable names with its grants. **Grant these permissions** asks you to confirm the displayed set. If hooks are waiting for trust, you can trust the package's hooks from its entry, or open `/hooks` to inspect each event, command, and timeout before enabling or trusting a hook individually."],[6627,"If a PyTorch decision dialog appears during launch, you can cancel and return here to fix the environment. Use “Ignore and Launch” only when you accept the risk for this run."],[4581,"If a sandboxed preset is unavailable, the menu explains why. On Windows, choose **Set up the Windows sandbox** when offered and confirm the system administrator prompt. You can also open sandbox maintenance with `/setup-default-sandbox`."],[4744,"If a service must remain running, first ask the Agent to read incremental output and verify that\nit is healthy."],[4707,"If a Skill allows implicit invocation, its name and description appear in the model's catalogue and the Agent must use it when the task clearly matches. An explicit-only Skill stays out of that catalogue but can still be chosen by name."],[7881,"If a terminal reports **Cleanup failed**, retry closing the same session instead of repeatedly creating new terminals."],[4654,"If a test message fails, check in this order:"],[7548,"If an action fails before a task starts, look under **Errors**. Select the notice to read the full message. Repeated identical errors from the same action share a row with a count. Dismissing the notice clears that message. Cancelled tasks can appear under **Needs attention**, but only tasks marked as errors count towards the red title-bar badge."],[7723,"If an extension dependency fails, first confirm that it belongs to an optional extension; do not immediately rebuild the entire Core."],[6299,"If an extension download fails, check Network & Proxy and Mirrors. To roll back the environment as a whole, use Snapshot Management."],[7113,"If an extension shows **Restarting**, wait for the automatic restart. If it shows **Failed** or **Stopped after repeated crashes**, fix the cause and click **Retry** on its card. For a linked folder, use **Reload** to reread the source directory. For extensions with a backend, **View log** shows the most recent output (up to the last 256 KiB). Choose **Refresh** to read it again."],[6775,"If automatic installation fails, the application attempts to provide a manual installer. Exit the application completely before installing it normally for the current platform; do not run the old application and installer at the same time."],[6624,"If automatic selection fails, check the graphics driver, operating-system support, and detected device reported by the page. Do not try several CUDA/ROCm builds at random."],[4782,"If chat still works but a banner reports that a plugin stopped, **Open plugins** takes you to Agent settings to investigate. If a request was interrupted by an assistant restart, check its last tool records before deciding whether to resend it."],[4745,"If cleanup fails, run `/stop` again as directed by the card; do not merely delete the session."],[7594,"If earlier output was trimmed from this window's replay cache, **Copy log** or **Export log to\nfile** can still retrieve the portion retained by the backend. If the backend has also dropped\nearlier output, the export contains only what remains. Export the log before quitting the\napplication."],[7324,"If every source fails to connect, inspect system time, DNS, proxy, and firewall first. If only one type of resource fails, inspect its corresponding mirror or change the model download source."],[4510,"If image reading, decoding, or request admission fails, the text and attachment draft remain available so you can fix the problem and send again."],[8415,"If installation fails or progress does not change for a long time, see Installation Progress and Troubleshooting."],[7338,"If it fails, switch to **Disabled** for a direct-connection comparison before deciding whether\nto inspect the proxy or mirror."],[7769,"If it still fails, collect an instance diagnostic bundle and retain the failed startup activity."],[6297,"If launch fails, disable the most recently changed extension first, then inspect its task output\nand compatibility notes."],[7724,"If manual intervention is truly necessary, use the instance terminal and create a snapshot first."],[7653,"If Micromamba is not ready, resolve that first. Git waiting for Micromamba does not mean Git\nitself is damaged."],[7378,"If migration fails, the application continues using the original location if it remains valid and displays a recovery record. Resolve disk-space, permission, or destination-conflict problems, click **Retry on next restart**, then exit and start normally. Do not directly delete the source directory or staged destination content."],[7875,"If migration, reinstallation, or deletion was interrupted, return to **Maintenance** and continue the same recovery operation."],[4488,"If no model is currently selected, click the model button or run `/model` first."],[6329,"If online application is unavailable, stop and relaunch the WebUI, then inspect hotpatch runtime\nstatus under “Instance Information.”"],[8435,"If only Core is found without usable Python, the instance displays **Not installed**. Open it and select **Start installation**. The application prepares Python in a new managed instance root while continuing to use the discovered external Core."],[7647,"If only one instance reports `ModuleNotFoundError`, CUDA, or extension errors when it starts, investigate the instance environment rather than application Python."],[7468,"If only one store is affected, close the tabs using it, clear its row, and open the page again."],[6625,"If package downloads or resolution fail, check Network & Proxy and Mirrors."],[6232,"If preparation fails, go to “Settings → Runtime Environment” to retry or change download sources. You can also read Runtime Environment Troubleshooting."],[4338,"If process cleanup or session relationships still have unmet requirements, the backend rejects the deletion and preserves the data. Resolve the cleanup obligation in the message and retry. Do not interpret a failed deletion as meaning that records were partially removed."],[7722,"If PyTorch installation fails, restore **Automatic** or the type's default option and verify the GPU driver."],[7639,"If recovery still fails"],[7929,"If SD Note does not cover the issue, search official repository issues using the exception type, final-line description, WebUI name, and extension name. Prefer guidance from Core or extension authors, and check which versions and operating systems a solution applies to."],[4781,"If the **assistant panel** stops working, select **Reload assistant panel** to reopen the conversation view. If the assistant process stops, its status page shows the reason and whether an automatic restart is scheduled. After repeated startup failures, **Start in safe mode** loads only core plugins. Select **Restart normally** when ready to use your previous plugin selection."],[6319,"If the **Runtime control** tab appears, open it to check the current WebUI's hotpatcher. For **Not running**, launch the WebUI and wait for the runtime to connect. For **Not answering**, the app retries in a few seconds, or you can select **Check again**. **Not supported** means the hotpatcher is too old. Update this WebUI's environment to use runtime control."],[7666,"If the application still responds, record which page is affected. If only the embedded WebUI is affected, select **Open in external browser** in the title bar while that page is showing and compare the result at the same address. On Linux, if the whole window goes blank or freezes and Settings is still accessible, turn off **Settings → WebView → GPU acceleration** and restart the application. WebView settings"],[4647,"If the configured context window is too high, the server may reject a request first. If it is too low, compaction begins earlier. Compaction changes only the context sent to the model on the next turn; it does not delete messages or tool records saved in the interface."],[4556,"If the current response, compaction, or blocking decision has not finished, resolve that state before switching."],[5553,"If the extension is active and instances of its types are running, **Reload** lists their names. Stop those instances, then click **Reload** again."],[7467,"If the external browser works but the page inside the application does not, close the WebUI page\nand open it again to rule out page state."],[4750,"If the final response claims completion while a tool is still running or awaiting cleanup, trust the backend state."],[8404,"If the form reports unusable presets, expand the details for their names and reasons. Select **Remove yours** and confirm to clear your unusable saved presets together. Extension-provided presets are managed by the extension that supplies them."],[7200,"If the information is insufficient, switch to **Debug**. Use **Trace** only if the cause is\nstill unclear."],[7726,"If the instance record was saved but the task did not start, reopen that instance and select **Start installation**. You do not need to delete the record or recreate an instance with the same name."],[6737,"If the list is empty or fails to refresh, check the network, PyPI mirror, and instance management API."],[7770,"If the log clearly points to an extension, disable, update, or roll back that extension first. If Core and the extension interface are incompatible, check both versions together. Do not uninstall every Python package first; doing so destroys the environment needed for further diagnosis."],[7648,"If the main application has not opened, select **Open log** on the Launcher's error screen. It opens the file for this run in `.hanafubuki-launcher/logs/` beside the Launcher. If the failure occurred before the log was created, this button is disabled. Record the stage and full error shown in the window instead."],[7281,"If the main window is not open, the request is refused at once. Nothing is ever allowed without you."],[4299,"If the model explicitly reports insufficient context before producing any output, the application may compact and retry. Once output has been produced, it does not automatically replay the entire turn, avoiding duplicate tool calls or external actions."],[7779,"If the old task belongs to Hanafubuki, finish stopping and cleaning up that task before restarting; do not kill the process directly and immediately restart it."