inal opens with a warning that managed environment variables could not be applied, check the cache paths and settings you need before running commands that depend on them. For an instance with Python, these commands inspect the environment:"],[7997,"If the WebUI address is reachable but a feature inside the page fails, investigate WebUI, extensions, and models before reinstalling Hanafubuki's application runtime."],[6553,"If the WebUI is running but has no address, inspect the launch output for the listening address, port conflicts, and browser connection status."],[7667,"If the window does not open, remains blank, or the application exits immediately:"],[7000,"If there is no improvement, restore the default and continue inspecting instance dependencies or\nthe GPU environment."],[7321,"If versions, commits, or checksums disagree, disable the relevant mirror and verify against the\nofficial source."],[6932,"If wallpaper fails to display, first confirm that the entry is not marked **Missing**, then try importing it again. Do not directly edit wallpaper files in the application data directory; the resource record may remain after the file becomes unusable."],[6714,"If you changed Core outside the app and the “Current” and “Reinstall” labels point to different variants, select “Sync reinstall setting” on the current variant. Back up uncommitted edits and stop the WebUI first. Confirming checks out the target branch again from the displayed repository and forces the working tree back to that branch. Uncommitted edits can be lost. The app saves the variant for future reinstalls once the task succeeds."],[6209,"If you choose the standalone archive, extract it to a writable directory before running the executable inside."],[4511,"If you enter new content and click the primary button while the Agent is responding, the application does not immediately begin a second turn. Instead, it places the content in the current panel's message queue."],[8051,"If you have only WebUI Core and no suitable Python, do not force an import. Use Scan the\nSystem. A recognized Core becomes an instance awaiting installation, and\nHanafubuki then prepares managed Python for it."],[6511,"If you only want InvokeAI to stop using a model but keep the file, choose “Unregister.” Choose Delete only when you intend to free the disk space completely."],[6425,"If you only want to hide the instance from the app while preserving every file, choose “Delete\nRecord Only.”"],[7371,"If you previously moved the runtime to a custom directory, **Move to default location** previews a migration back to the default root. Check the destination before scheduling the move."],[8407,"If you select a directory manually, that directory itself becomes the final instance root; another nested directory is not created automatically. Use a new, dedicated directory. Do not select a drive root, your home directory, or an existing directory containing important files."],[7319,"If you truly need a fixed source, disable automatic mirrors and change only the setting related\nto the failed resource."],[7332,"Ignore both system and manual proxies and connect directly. Use this for a direct network or to\ndetermine whether a failure is caused by an incorrect proxy."],[6370,"Ignore Once"],[4639,"Image input"],[6929,"Image position"],[8281,"Image-creation tool with a unified canvas"],[8024,"Import an Existing Instance"],[6485,"Import and verify"],[8033,"Import and verify"],[8257,"Import existing instance"],[6903,"Import images"],[8027,"Import steps"],[6494,"Import, download, copy, move, rename, and delete files"],[7389,"Important information"],[8036,"Importing registers existing directories and marks the instance ready. Built-in WebUIs need a working standalone Python. For an extension-provided type, prepare the components listed by that type. Types that can only be attached through scanning are omitted from the import list."],[4638,"In **Default model**, choose a known level, enter a custom value, or