voke key or arbitrary Tauri command access. Do not log settings values, since declared secret fields may be present."],[5644,"On a management or diagnostic schema panel, set `\"toolbar\": \"button\"` to open the panel from its instance's title bar. The same property on a standalone button in an `actions` block exposes that action directly with its label and confirmation. Use `\"toolbar\": \"externalBrowser\"` for a shortcut that takes the place of the external-browser button while the WebUI is showing. The WebUI tabs context menu can still open the current page."],[8202,"On failure, the log expands automatically and shows diagnostic, cleanup, and retry actions."],[5890,"On GitHub releases"],[8052,"On Home, select **Add instance**, then switch the source at the top to **Import existing instance**."],[6225,"On its first run, the Launcher scans its directory for built-in WebUI layouts. If it finds only the Core, it registers the instance so you can finish installing it in the app. For WebUIs added later, open **Add instance** and use Scan system."],[6952,"On one instance, an update check and a snapshot never run at the same time. Whichever is requested second waits until the first finishes:"],[7076,"On or off"],[7085,"On or off"],[6747,"On the first launch, wait for Python, Micromamba, and Git to finish preparing. If a runtime environment error appears at the top of the window or on Home, go to “Settings → Runtime Environment” first."],[5489,"On the new installation page, choose **Local notes** and the **Welcome note** preset. Change **Message** to a line you will recognize, then create and install the instance."],[7403,"On the next startup, inspect Git on the system `PATH`; automatically fall back to Micromamba Git if it is unavailable"],[5732,"On Windows the package's root is `/<extension id>/`, not `/`. An absolute path starting with `/` points to the wrong place there, so refer to scripts, styles, and images by relative URLs (`./status.js`, `../__hanafubuki/frame.js`)."],[6230,"On Windows, the Launcher requires long-path support and the Visual C++ Runtime. If either is\nmissing, it requests administrator permission once to update the registry or install the runtime.\nIt continues to run as a standard user afterward. Rejecting either request leaves the Launcher on\na retry screen."],[6947,"Once a day, every installed extension that publishes its versions is checked for a newer one; nothing is installed. See Extensions."],[6774,"Once a signed update is ready, the main window also offers **Restart and update now**. If you keep working and quit normally, Hanafubuki defers the installation until the next launch. It checks again then and installs the signed update currently available."],[7134,"Once an extension is on, what it contributes appears here:"],[7330,"Once the application API server is running, it checks the system proxy about every 30 seconds.\nThe page shows the effective address. If the system reports no proxy, connections go directly.\nIf detection fails, the application keeps the last successful result for the current settings."],[8205,"Once the child process is confirmed stopped, the interface releases ownership for this installation. If termination or inspection fails, the error retains the unresolved cleanup obligation."],[4327,"Once the main conversation has a message, use `/side` to open a side chat or `/btw your question` to ask there directly. The side chat uses the main conversation as context and shows its replies in a separate pane while the main task continues. Use `/close` to close the side chat. To inspect work delegated by the main agent, use `/subagents` to switch to that subagent's conversation."],[5833,"Once the page is ready, and on every change of the application's theme or language, the client sets `data-theme` (`light` or `dark`), `color-scheme`, `lang`, and these CSS variables on the page's root, plus every variable the application sets at run time (the whole accent ramp, such as `--accent-indica