etail"],[7981,"Task lifecycle"],[7677,"Task output, disk space, temporary directory, and security software"],[4549,"Task plan"],[7573,"Task statuses:"],[7515,"Tasks"],[7536,"Tasks are grouped by state:"],[7622,"Tasks from every page, full output, and downloads"],[7542,"Tasks still executing"],[7544,"Tasks that failed or recorded a warning"],[7546,"Tasks that have ended"],[5738,"Tells the application the page is ready; from then on it sends the theme, follows the page's height, and pings it. A frame that does not call it within 10 s shows **Unavailable**"],[6213,"Terminal does not display characters while you enter your macOS password. When the command finishes, open Hanafubuki again. For other security prompts, use **System Settings → Privacy & Security** to confirm that you want to open the app."],[7860,"Termination, absence, or metadata release could not be confirmed"],[5480,"Testing"],[5474,"Testing and Packaging"],[4989,"Text"],[5601,"Text"],[5822,"Text"],[5836,"Text"],[5914,"Text"],[6086,"Text"],[7033,"Text"],[5583,"Text and languages"],[5957,"Text by language falls back to English when the current language is missing, and to the first language given when there is no English."],[5069,"text by language, `{ en = \"…\", zh = \"…\" }`;"],[8290,"Text to speech"],[8296,"Text to speech with multiple engines"],[7482,"Text, number"],[6092,"Text, or an object of language to text"],[6083,"Text, or an object of language to text (`{ \"en\": \"…\", \"zh\": \"…\" }`), as in a manifest"],[5526,"That is the binary for one platform. When publishing a native backend, supply a matching binary for each OS and architecture you support. In `latest.json`, use the host's platform and architecture names, such as `windows` and `x86_64` for Windows x64, or `macos` and `aarch64` for Apple silicon, and keep each archive's actual filename in its download URL. See Publishing updates."],[6342,"The “Launch” page saves the environment variables for the next launch of the current instance. Types that offer launch arguments also let you edit the command line here. Changes take effect the next time you start the WebUI."],[6389,"The “Maintenance” page does not depend on the WebUI management API and remains available when management features fail. Migration, reinstallation, and deletion are instance-lifecycle operations: the app first stops and confirms related runtime resources, then modifies files or records."],[6607,"The “PyTorch” page inspects Torch components in the instance Python environment, detects the device type, and lists installation combinations supported by the current WebUI. Options vary by WebUI, operating system, and hardware."],[6726,"The “Versions” page varies by WebUI type. Git-based instances such as Stable Diffusion WebUI, ComfyUI, Fooocus, SD Trainer, Qwen TTS WebUI, RVC Next WebUI, and Mizuoto TTS WebUI show repository branches and commits. InvokeAI shows installed and available package versions."],[4326,"The **…** menu on a project lets you start a conversation there, pin the project, edit it, or archive it. Use **Archive project** to put the whole project aside. To restore it, expand the archived projects in the Projects section."],[6759,"The **About** page shows the current Hanafubuki version and links to the project repository, author, and related WebUI documentation. External links open in the system browser rather than replacing the application window."],[6822,"The **App** server appears first, followed by instance servers known to the supervisor. An instance's control server uses its name. If its type declares more server roles, you can see multiple rows for the same instance, labelled **instance name · role**."],[8362,"The **Fooocus** variant is based on lllyasviel's original Fooocus but uses a fork maintained by licyk."],[7038,"The **Marketplace** tab of the **Extensions** section lists extensions published in the extension registry, read through the application's network and proxy settings. If the GitHub registry cannot be fetched or decoded, the app tries the Gitee mirror. The page reports a load error only if both sources fail. The listing is kept for a while: opening the tab again within two minutes shows it without reading the registry again, and **Refresh** at the top of the page reads it now. The search box at the top of the tab, which stays in place while the list scrolls, finds entries by name, ID, author, or description. Each entry shows its ID, author, a link to its source, which opens in your browser, and its description, with how it stands here:"],[7663,"The **Run anyway** button appears only after you expand **More info**. Do this only for a file downloaded from this site whose name and platform you have verified. Delete files from third-party reposts or unknown sources and download them again."],[7460,"The **WebView data** panel below the fields shows:"],[6167,"The `.hanafubuki-launcher` directory beside the program"],[5497,"The `greeter` type: `provider = \"backend\"`, only the `core` component, no runtime, the `greeting` parameter, one `ui` server role"],[4381,"The `hanafubuki-webui-management` Skill, installed with the entry, explains how the Agent uses these tools (Skills)."],[5323,"The `initialize` result lists known hooks from the method registry itself, including `diagnostics`. Expand `diagnostics.collect` for document fields and its timeout, count and byte bounds; runtime tools are listed in the host API above. See the SDK examples."],[5603,"The `locales` files"],[6910,"The accent color is used for buttons, selections, and emphasis. Select a preset swatch or open **Custom colour** to adjust hue, saturation, and brightness. You can also enter a hex value such as `#4c8df6` and press `Enter`. **Reset appearance** at the bottom restores the default theme and background settings and keeps your wallpaper library."],[7172,"The active log, directories, and symbolic links are not deleted by the retention policy."],[7273,"The address normally uses port 43761; the **Port** field on the **Management MCP server** card changes it (0 lets the system choose one at every start), and the server restarts on the new port at once. If that port is taken, the server uses another one, which the API Servers page shows; update the configuration of Claude Code, Cursor or VS Code to match. Claude Desktop's needs no change: the application writes the current address to the endpoint file whenever the server starts, and the bridge reads it each time Claude Desktop starts the bridge. The bridge reads it only then: if the server moved to another port while Claude Desktop was running, restart the server in Claude Desktop (or Claude Desktop itself) so that the bridge reads the new address."],[4763,"The Agent can read project context, invoke application tools, run commands, and help modify files. What it can do depends on the current model, permission mode, MCP, Skills, and session state. Before starting, configure at least one enabled model provider."],[4611,"The Agent configures \"how to connect to the server\" separately from \"how to use the model.\" A provider stores the protocol, API address, and credentials; the model policy stores the default model, reasoning effort, image input, and context rules."],[4673,"The Agent discovers Skills in these locations:"],[4465,"The Agent may only write a note when you have asked it to remember, forget, or update something. It does not decide on its own that a conversation was worth keeping."],[4708,"The Agent reads Skills through `skills_list` and `skills_read`, and can turn one on or off with `enable_skill` and `disable_skill` after you approve it. Writing, installing, and removing a Skill package uses the ordinary filesystem and command tools — a Skill directory is just a directory — which is why those actions go through the same approvals as any other file write."],[4451,"The Agent retrieves memory again for every model sampling step, so newly generated or reset results take effect in subsequent steps."],[4495,"The Agent uses the current session's permissions to read or write at the referenced location."],[4723,"The Agent uses tools to read files, modify code, run commands, and invoke application functions. Every call creates a tool card in the message history. Together, the tool state and final response describe the task result."],[4749,"The Agent's final response should state what changed, what was verified, and what remains incomplete."],[4856,"The answer could not be built"],[4628,"The API token is masked by default. Use the eye button to reveal or hide it. Enter one custom\nheader per line. Use `NAME=VALUE` to add or replace a header, or leave an existing name on its own\nto keep the saved value. Hide credentials before sharing screenshots."],[6424,"The app deletes the listed directories before removing the record. This usually includes the\nentire root with its models and outputs, plus any components the instance owns elsewhere. If the\nroot is itself a Core marked external, the app keeps the root and deletes only the individual\ncomponents that the instance owns."],[6585,"The app only updates the component references in the instance record. It does not copy or move the\nold directory to the new location. To relocate the complete instance, use “Migrate Instance” in\nInstance Maintenance."],[6231,"The app prepares runtime components including Python, Micromamba, and Git. Keep the network connected and wait for preparation to finish."],[6410,"The app revalidates instance identity, configuration, path overlap, and external components, then shows the final directory and warnings in the confirmation dialog."],[5590,"The application"],[5594,"The application"],[5602,"The application"],[5781,"The application also serves its own look to every frame: `__hanafubuki/ui.css` beside the frame client, and the fonts it loads under `__hanafubuki/fonts/`. Link it by a relative URL, as above. It is generated from the application's stylesheets, so a page that links it gets the application's buttons, fields, cards, lists, tabs, messages, progress bars, scrollbars, and typeface, in both themes, following the user's accent. It sets the body's text and colour but nothing of the page's height, so the frame still follows the page's content."],[5798,"The application also serves its own Vue components to every frame, built from the same sources as the application itself, so they always match the version they run in:"],[7167,"The application always retains a capacity-limited log buffer for the current run, which a diagnostic bundle exports as `session.log`. Disabling **Save logs to files** stops only disk persistence; diagnostics for the current run remain available."],[6821,"The application and built-in instances use background API servers for operations such as installation, version switching, and plugin and model management. Open this page to inspect the services or run a health check when a task stops responding. Connection settings for the management MCP server appear below the list."],[6864,"The application and instance control servers follow these rules:"],[7112,"The application cannot read its install record or its installed package; the card shows why. Usually uninstall it and install it again"],[5272,"The application checks a plan as it checks a descriptor's steps: an undeclared placeholder, a path that does not start in a declared component, an unknown step kind, or a value that would leave its component refuses the whole plan before anything runs. The backend names components, never paths; the application runs the steps."],[5278,"The application checks a preset against its base type each time it lists it. A preset whose base type is not installed, that sets a field the form does not have, or a value the field does not take, is listed as unavailable with the reason; it never fails your extension. A file that does not read, or a malformed id, base or argument, fails the install as a type descriptor does."],[6052,"The application checks each installed extension that names an `[update] url` once a day (and whenever the user clicks **Check for Updates**). It reads the `latest.json` there, and offers an update when its newest entry for the user's system is above the installed version. It never installs one by itself: the user clicks **Update** (or **Update to …**) on the card, which checks again, and confirms, as for any update."],[6790,"The application continues to own its proxy, log level, appearance, module switches, and desktop workspaces. The standalone Agent's terminal interface and configuration layers are not part of the desktop host's catalog."],[4969,"The application forwards it to the target's backend as a `service.models.list` call with `{ \"caller\": \"<caller id>\", \"params\": … }`, and answers the caller with what the target answered."],[6765,"The application has downloaded and verified an update for the current installation type; confirm installation and restart"],[7656,"The application Python version and Git source take effect on the next launch:"],[8095,"The application rejects dangerous paths, symbolic-link paths, invalid parent-child relationships, and paths that overlap another instance root, Python, or Core. Keeping the default Python and Core directories is the most reliable option."],[7642,"The application remains stuck at runtime preparation after opening."],[7218,"The application runs a management **MCP server**: the instance management tools the built-in assistant uses, available to any MCP client. It listens only on this computer, at the address shown on **Settings › API Servers**, and only a client holding a valid token can use it. The built-in assistant is connected to it automatically. Other AI tools can connect too, once you let them."],[7822,"The application runtime, settings, platform, global tasks, or several instances fail together"],[5734,"The application serves the frame client at the reserved path `__hanafubuki/frame.js` of every package's root (a file of that name in the package is replaced by it). It is an ES module, imported by a relative URL:"],[5192,"The application then starts it before your roles, shows the instance's Management API in its information and in Settings → API Servers, and keeps it running while the instance is managed or launched. Stopping or restarting it does not stop your roles. A type without a Python runtime cannot declare `control`, and the error says why. The role alone adds no management section; a type takes the built-in WebUIs' versions, extensions, models, and PyTorch sections by adopting a built-in type's management."],[5961,"The application versions it runs on, a semver range (such as `\">=0.3, <0.5\"`); any version without one"],[4808,"The application waits for its managed Python and verified launcher resources to be ready, then runs `<python> <version dir>/backend.py`."],[6074,"The application's **Marketplace** lists the extensions in the extension registry, licyk/hanafubuki-extension: one file, `extensions.json`. To be listed, add an entry for your extension there by pull request; the repository's README describes the checks a pull request must pass."],[5296,"The application's calls on a backend"],[5318,"The application's components a frame may use: the component bundle, `__hanafubuki/ui.js`, with Vue at `__hanafubuki/vue.js` and their styles at `__hanafubuki/ui-components.css`. A page installs `frameUi(frame)` on each Vue app and renders them with `h()`, since the served Vue has no template compiler. Their typings are `sdk/ui/ui.d.ts`. How to use them is on Interface."],[5235,"The application's discovery (the instance scan, and dropping a folder on the application) recognizes the built-in WebUIs by their layouts. Your type recognizes its own installations with `[[discovery]]` signatures; a type without one is never discovered."],[5758,"The application's language (`en`, `zh`), or `null` until the first theme arrives after `ready()`; the client also sets it as the root's `lang`"],[5133,"The application