icy, instance lifecycle, process ownership, and operating-system account permissions also remain in force at all times."],[5926,"The backend runs in a separate process. A frame runs in a sandboxed iframe and uses the frame client to read extension settings, call its own backend, or ask the host to open an external link."],[5250,"The backend takes part through these callbacks (see Backends):"],[5511,"The backend: `provider.validateSpec`, `provider.installPlan`, `provider.launchPlan`, the frame's `status` call, the panel's `greet` action, and its UI state (`Ui`, `Host::emit_state`)"],[6832,"The badge beside each server shows its current state. A running server is labeled by its health checks:"],[7094,"The badge on each card shows how the extension stands:"],[5719,"The block follows every push without a query: the application reads `ui.state` again and shows what is at the path. When the state cannot be read, the block says why in its place until a state arrives; while the backend is not running, or does not list `ui`, it shows no rows."],[5433,"The block's data: `{\"rows\": [...]}` or `{\"lines\": [...]}`"],[5316,"The blocks of a panel (a `ui` entry of `kind = \"schema\"`). Each kind lists how the application renders it, how a panel's file writes it, and the data it is rendered from."],[6465,"The bottom-right status area reports operations started from the current Instance Manager. Task\nCenter retains tasks across pages, along with detailed phases and output. Closing the page while a\nstatus is still “Running” does not end the task."],[7274,"The bridge does not start the application. If the application is not running, or external access\nis off, Claude Desktop shows \"Hanafubuki is not running, or its external MCP access is off\"; if\nthe client was revoked, \"the token was refused\". Start the application, turn external access on\nand restart the server in Claude Desktop. The endpoint file (`data/mcp/endpoint.json` in the\napplication's data folder) holds only the a