ose the WebUI tabs using it, click the trash button on its row, and check the name in the confirmation. Pages using other stores can stay open. Clearing **Shared by every instance** affects every instance using that store. To clear the whole list, close all WebUI tabs and choose **Clear WebView data** beside the total."],[4634,"To configure one model separately, open **Models → Provider models** and add a `PROVIDER_ID/MODEL_ID` record. It can override the context window, maximum output, image support, and reasoning levels. If the service changes a model's capabilities, clear its learned facts to discard the Agent's observations while keeping your manual overrides. The action on a model affects that model. On a provider, it covers all of its models."],[7316,"To enter a custom GitHub or Hugging Face address, disable automatic selection and enable the corresponding manual mirror. Enter a complete address with `http://` or `https://` and a hostname."],[8428,"To find an extension-provided type, enable its extension before starting the scan. When the scanner recognizes the type’s directory markers and validates the required components, the app adds a ready instance. This also works for types that can only be attached by scanning. Deleting the instance preserves any component the scan rule explicitly marks as external."],[6546,"To keep an output folder or a shared model library close at hand, select **Add quick path…** under **Quick paths**, choose a directory, and click its tile to open it. Drag the tile by its icon to reorder it. Right-click or use its menu to rename or remove it. Changes are saved automatically. Removing a shortcut leaves the directory on disk."],[5055,"To let users reuse an existing installation, declare which component can point to it. For example, this type can use an existing Node.js directory:"],[6220,"To move the environment, exit the application and copy the Launcher, `.hanafubuki-launcher`, and\nany WebUI directories registered by the first scan