as no feed. The tab reports how many registry entries it skipped because it could not read them."],[7445,"When a page asks for a new window through a link or script, such as a `target=\"_blank\"` link or a popup sign-in, the choice decides what happens:"],[6893,"When a server has work in progress, **Restart now** and **Stop** ask for confirmation first.\nInterrupted tasks cannot resume and must be run again after the restart. Without a specific\nreason, prefer **Restart**, which waits for the work to finish."],[4446,"When a session is created or forked, it records whether memory generation was allowed at that time. You can later manage the current session with `/memories`, but no memory is retrieved or generated while memory is globally disabled."],[6417,"When a type offers only `update-check`, updates are managed externally. Reinstalling local components preserves the last reported update and its component details until the next check."],[5686,"When an action is pressed, the application checks its form and calls `ui.panel.action` with `panel`, `action`, `values`, `context`, and `row`. A regular button sends `row: null`. A list action sends `values: {}`. The backend may return `{ \"notice\": \"…\" }` to display a message."],[4466,"When an answer materially relies on memory, the Agent cites the resources it read. The application validates those citations against what memory actually attributes the fact to, and removes the citation block from the visible answer once the turn commits."],[6135,"When an enabled desktop extension provides a page, the **Extension pages** menu appears in the title bar. Choose a page there, then use the back button to return to Home."],[7140,"When an extension is turned off, fails, or is uninstalled, instances of its types stay in the instance list but are shown as unavailable, with the reason. Their records and files stay exactly as they are; nothing is changed or deleted. The only thing you can do with such an instance is delete its record